{"items":[{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#amazon-kinesis-data-streams-announces-service-managed-partition-keys-for-simplified-data-ingestion","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"amazon-kinesis-data-streams-announces-service-managed-partition-keys-for-simplified-data-ingestion","dateCreated":"2026-08-07T23:50:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-09-23T23:08:43+0000","additionalFields":{"regionalAvailability":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eAll AWS commercial regions\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports service-managed partition keys for On-Demand Standard and On-Demand Advantage streams, automatically distributing records across shards without requiring customers to specify partition keys to publish data. This capability simplifies data ingestion for workloads where record ordering is not required, eliminating hot partition keys and reducing time to production for streaming workloads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless streaming data service that makes it easy to capture, process, and store data streams at any scale. Many streaming use cases such as log aggregation, metrics collection, and IoT telemetry do not require ordering guarantees and benefit from prewarmed capacity for instant scaling. Previously, customers generated random partition keys (such as UUIDs) to distribute data, but random partitioning can still produce uneven throughput across shards, causing throttling for some partition keys even when the stream has sufficient aggregate capacity. By opting into service-managed partition keys, customers no longer need to specify partition keys when publishing data to streams in on-demand mode. The service automatically distributes records based on available warm capacity, allowing customers to scale to gigabytes per second without maintaining any distribution logic. Customers who want to send records without specifying a partition key can simply upgrade to the latest AWS SDK or Kinesis Producer Library (KPL) version to benefit from this capability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eService-managed partition keys for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is available today in all AWS commercial regions at no additional cost. To get started, visit the Amazon Kinesis Data Streams documentation (\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis\"\u003ehttps://aws.amazon.com/kinesis\u003c/a\u003e).\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/kinesis/service-managed-partition-keys","postDateTime":"2026-09-23T22:51:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams announces Service-Managed Partition Keys for simplified data ingestion"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-mmp2pbsymsoxx4qqrsfqcx","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-mmp2pbsymsoxx4qqrsfqcx","dateCreated":"2026-09-01T22:43:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-09-01T22:43:15+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","nosnippet":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports a dry run feature to check whether an API request would succeed without executing the operation. Customers can now set the new optional parameter ‘DryRun’ to true in their API requests to validate permissions before interacting with a stream in production.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePreviously, customers had no safe way to test whether their application had the correct permissions to access a stream. They would often send a request engineered to fail after checking permissions, such as a PutRecord request with a payload deliberately larger than the maximum supported size. This approach was fragile as it depended on current service limits, and if those limits ever changed, the request could unexpectedly succeed, writing unintended records into the production stream and into any downstream consumers. Now, customers can simply set the parameter ‘DryRun’ to true to indicate they only want to validate the API request. If all checks complete successfully, the API returns a ‘DryRunOperationException’, confirming the request would have succeeded without the ‘DryRun’ parameter.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe dry run feature is available for five APIs (PutRecord, PutRecords, GetRecords, GetShardIterator, and SubscribeToShard) in all AWS Regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is available. For more information about dry run, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/kds-dryrun-validation.html\"\u003eTest your permissions and request inputs with dry run\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Data Streams Developer Guide. To get started with dry run, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/APIReference/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams API Reference\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-api/","postDateTime":"2026-09-01T19:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports a dry run feature to validate API requests"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-mupqrfpwl4rbsi6gabtgaj","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-mupqrfpwl4rbsi6gabtgaj","dateCreated":"2026-07-20T18:59:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2026-08-20T17:32:20+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless streaming data service that makes it easy to capture, process, and store data streams at any scale. On-demand streams automatically increase ingest capacity in response to rising data ingest usage. With On-demand Advantage mode, you can proactively manage stream capacity using warm throughput to prepare streams for sudden changes in data traffic. We are extending warm throughput with the ability to also scale down ingest capacity, giving you full control to scale your stream\u0027s write throughput up or down.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo scale down, simply set a lower warm throughput value on your on-demand stream. The stream adjusts to the requested capacity or the amount needed to support peak data ingest usage in the last hour, whichever is higher. This ensures your stream always retains sufficient capacity for current traffic while releasing excess capacity you no longer need. As a result, you get optimal stream-processing performance and cost efficiency.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWarm throughput scale-down is available at no additional cost for all on-demand streams with On-demand Advantage mode enabled.\u0026nbsp; For more information about On-demand Advantage, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/how-do-i-size-a-stream.html\"\u003eChoose the right mode to stream in\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Data Streams Developer Guide. To get started with the feature, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/updating-a-stream.html\"\u003eUpdate a stream\u003c/a\u003e. For pricing details, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/pricing/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams pricing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe feature is available in all AWS Regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Streams On-demand Advantage is supported.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/kinesis/on-demand-scale-down","postDateTime":"2026-07-24T18:55:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports scaling down ingest capacity with warm throughput"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2026","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2026","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-12-05T19:55:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#aws-aws-products-and-services#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#aws-aws-products-and-services","name":"AWS GovCloud (US)","description":"description placeholder","dateCreated":"2025-05-01T17:24:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-05-01T17:24:16+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"serverless","description":"marketing:marchitecture/serverless","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-9ut2vcjwb2t9jei5lprs8q","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-9ut2vcjwb2t9jei5lprs8q","dateCreated":"2025-11-20T14:48:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-11-20T22:29:45+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports 50 enhanced fan-out consumers for On-demand Advantage streams. A higher fan-out limit lets customers attach many more independent, low-latency, high-throughput consumers to the same stream—unlocking parallel analytics, ML pipelines, compliance workflows, and multi-team architectures without creating extra streams or causing throughput contention. On-demand Advantage is an account-level setting that unlocks more capabilities and provides a different pricing structure for all on-demand streams in an AWS Region. On-demand Advantage offers data usage with 60% lower pricing compared to On-demand Standard, with data ingest at $0.032/GB, data retrieval at $0.016/GB, and enhanced fan-out data retrieval at $0.016/GB. High fan-out workloads are most cost effective with On-demand Advantage.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAmazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless streaming data service that makes it easy to capture, process, and store data streams at any scale. Enhanced fan-out is an Amazon Kinesis Data Streams feature that enables consumers to receive records from a data stream with dedicated throughput of up to 2 MB of data per second per shard, and this throughput automatically scales with the number of shards in a stream. A consumer that uses enhanced fan-out doesn\u0027t have to contend with other consumers that are receiving data from the stream. For accounts with On-demand Advantage enabled, you can continue to use the existing Kinesis API RegisterStreamConsumer to register new consumers to use enhanced fan-out up to the new 50 limit.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nSupport for enhanced fan-out consumers is available in the AWS Regions listed \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/enhanced-consumers.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. For more information on Kinesis Data Streams quotas and limits, please see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/service-sizes-and-limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. For more information on On-demand Advantage, please see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/how-do-i-size-a-stream.html#diff-modes-kds\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e for On-demand Advantage.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/11/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-enhanced-fan-out-consumers","postDateTime":"2025-11-20T15:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports up to 50 enhanced fan-out consumers"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"serverless","description":"marketing:marchitecture/serverless","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-vhvscxidufojqkemdrpraf","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-vhvscxidufojqkemdrpraf","dateCreated":"2025-10-30T16:42:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-11-04T18:48:35+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams launches On-demand Advantage, so customers can warm on-demand streams to handle instant throughput increases up to 10GB or 10 million events per second, eliminating the need to over-provision or build custom scaling solutions. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless streaming data service that makes it easy to capture, process, and store data streams at any scale. On-demand streams automatically scale capacity based on data usage, and now you can warm write capacity ad hoc. On-demand Advantage also provides a simpler pricing structure that removes the fixed, per-stream charge, so customers only pay for data usage at better rates.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nOn-demand Advantage offers data usage with 60% lower pricing compared to On-demand Standard, with data ingest at $0.032/GB and data retrieval at $0.016/GB in the US East (N. Virginia) region. The price of Enhanced fan-out data retrieval is the same as shared-throughput retrievals, making higher fan-out use cases more cost effective. The mode also decreases the price of extended retention by 77% from $0.10/GB-month to $0.023/GB-month. Once you enable On-demand Advantage mode, the account will be billed for a minimum of 25MB/s of data ingest and 25MB/s of data retrieval at the lower rates across all on-demand streams. The new pricing means On-demand Advantage is the most cost effective way to stream with Kinesis Data Streams when you ingest at least 10MB/s in aggregate, fan out to more than two consumer applications, or have hundreds of streams in a region. You can check directly in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/home#\" contenteditable\u003d\"false\" style\u003d\"cursor: pointer;\"\u003eKinesis console\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/pricing/\" contenteditable\u003d\"false\" style\u003d\"cursor: pointer;\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e if On-demand Advantage is a good fit for your account.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nOn-demand Advantage is available in all AWS regions where Kinesis Data Streams is available, including AWS GovCloud (US) and China regions. To learn more, see the \u003ca contenteditable\u003d\"false\" style\u003d\"cursor: pointer;\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/big-data/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-launches-on-demand-advantage-for-instant-throughput-increases-and-streaming-at-scale/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" contenteditable\u003d\"false\" style\u003d\"cursor: pointer;\"\u003elaunch blog\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/working-with-streams.html\" contenteditable\u003d\"false\" style\u003d\"cursor: pointer;\"\u003eKinesis Data Streams User Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/11/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-ondemand-advantage","postDateTime":"2025-11-04T08:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams launches On-demand Advantage mode"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"serverless","description":"marketing:marchitecture/serverless","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-tlkqtpkvwt26xmkvr1ugfr","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-tlkqtpkvwt26xmkvr1ugfr","dateCreated":"2025-10-13T18:05:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-10-15T18:06:42+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports Fault Injection Service (FIS) actions for Kinesis API errors. Customers can now test their application\u0027s error handling capabilities, retry mechanisms (such as exponential backoff patterns), and CloudWatch alarms in a controlled environment. This allows customers to validate their monitoring systems and recovery processes before encountering real-world failures, ultimately improving application resilience and availability. This integration supports Kinesis Data Streams API errors including throttling, internal errors, service unavailable, and expired iterator exceptions for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nAmazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless data streaming service that enables customers to capture, process, and store real-time data streams at any scale. Now customers can create real-world Kinesis Data Stream API errors (including 500, 503, and 400 errors for GET and PUT operations) to test application resilience. This feature eliminates the previous need for custom implementation or to wait for actual production failures to verify error handling mechanisms. To get started, customers can create experiment templates through the FIS console to run tests directly or integrate them into their continuous integration pipeline. For additional safety, FIS experiments include automatic stop mechanisms that trigger when customer-defined thresholds are reached, ensuring controlled testing without risking application stability.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThese actions are generally available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/fis.html\" contenteditable\u003d\"false\" style\u003d\"cursor: pointer;\"\u003eAWS Regions where FIS is available\u003c/a\u003e, including the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. To learn more about using these actions, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/working-with-streams.html\" contenteditable\u003d\"false\" style\u003d\"cursor: pointer;\"\u003eKinesis Data Streams User Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fis/latest/userguide/fis-actions-reference.html#aws-kinesis-actions\" contenteditable\u003d\"false\" style\u003d\"cursor: pointer;\"\u003eFIS User Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/10/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-fis-actions-api-errors/","postDateTime":"2025-10-15T07:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams announces new Fault Injection Service (FIS) actions for API errors"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-fault-injection-simulator","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-fault-injection-service","description":"AWS Fault Injection Service ","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:40:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-10T17:59:44+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#developer-tools","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"developer-tools","description":"marketing:marchitecture/developer-tools","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:40:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:40:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#launch-bcsl1rqoa6tlqrzaayvbwc","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-bcsl1rqoa6tlqrzaayvbwc","dateCreated":"2025-09-18T18:59:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-09-18T21:13:19+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams now allows customers to make API requests over Internet Protocol version 6 (IPv6) in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. Customers have the option of using either IPv6 or IPv4 when sending requests over dual-stack public or VPC endpoints. The new endpoints have also been validated under the Federal Information Processing Standard (FIPS) 140-3 program.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nKinesis Data Streams allows users to capture, process, and store data streams in real time at any scale. IPv6 increases the number of available addresses by several orders of magnitude, so customers will no longer need to manage overlapping address spaces. Many devices and networks today already use IPv6, and now they can easily write to and read from data streams. FIPS-compliant endpoints help companies contracting with the US federal governments meet the FIPS security requirement to encrypt sensitive data in supported Regions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nSupport for IPv6 with Kinesis Data Streams is now available in all Regions where Kinesis Data Streams is available, including AWS GovCloud (US) and China Regions. See \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/ak.html\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e for a full listing of our Regions. To learn more about Kinesis Data Streams, please refer to our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/introduction.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/09/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-ipv6-govcloud","postDateTime":"2025-09-18T17:00:00Z","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams expands Internet Protocol version 6 support to the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"serverless","description":"marketing:marchitecture/serverless","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p218269408","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"launch-ethgisGKk2qnynXTpZUfkF","dateCreated":"2025-04-11T17:34:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-04-30T16:33:44+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, Amazon Kinesis Data Streams introduces support for tagging and Attribute-Based Access Control (ABAC) for enhanced fan-out consumers. You can register enhanced fan-out consumers to have dedicated low latency read throughput per shard, up to 2MB/s. ABAC is an authorization strategy that defines access permissions based on tags that can be attached to IAM users, roles, and AWS resources for fine-grained access control. This new feature enables you to apply tags for allocating costs and simplifying permission management for your enhanced fan-out consumers.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nWith this launch, you can now tag your enhanced fan-out consumers used by different business units to track and allocate costs in AWS Cost Explorer without manually tracking costs per consumer. You can apply tags to enhanced fan-out consumers using the Kinesis Data Streams API or AWS Command Line Interface (CLI). Additionally, ABAC support for enhanced fan-out consumers allows you to use IAM policies to allow or deny specific Kinesis Data Streams API actions when the IAM principal\u0026#39;s tags match the tags on a registered consumer.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTagging and Attribute-Based Access Control for enhanced fan-out consumers are available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e, including the AWS China and AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. To learn more about tagging and ABAC support for consumers, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/tagging.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTag your resources\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/identity/attribute-based-access-control/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAttribute-Based Access Control (ABAC) for AWS\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2025/04/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-consumer-tagging-abac/","postDateTime":"2025-04-30T10:00:00-07:00","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports tagging and Attribute-Based Access Control for consumers"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2025","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2025","description":"\u003cp\u003e2025\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-12-30T16:07:22+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1526510074","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"jy4ocLYAUr7s8q1w5DvfNm","dateCreated":"2024-10-17T19:47:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-11-20T21:31:09+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams On-Demand Mode now automatically scales to support streaming applications that write up to 10GB/s per stream and consumers that read up to 20 GB/s per stream. This is a 5x increase from the previously supported limits of 2 GB/s per stream for writers and 4 GB/s for readers.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nAmazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless data streaming service that allows customers to build de-coupled applications that publish and consume real-time data streams. It includes integrations with 40+ AWS and third-party services, enabling customers to easily build real-time stream processing, analytics, and machine learning applications. Customers use Kinesis Data Streams On-demand Mode for workloads with unpredictable and variable traffic patterns, so they do not have to manage capacity. They can pay based on the amount of data streamed. Customers can now use On-demand Mode for high-throughput data streams.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThere is no action required on your part to use this feature in US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon) and Europe (Ireland) AWS Regions. When you write data to your Kinesis On-demand stream, it will automatically scale to write up to 10 GB/s. For other AWS Regions, you can reach out to\u003ca href\u003d\"https://support.console.aws.amazon.com/support/home#/case/create?issueType\u003dservice-limit-increase\u0026amp;limitType\u003dkinesis-streams\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e AWS support\u003c/a\u003e to raise the peak write throughput capacity of your OD Streams to 10 GB/s. To learn more, see the Kinesis Data Streams \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/service-sizes-and-limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eQuotas and Limits\u003c/a\u003e documentation.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-on-demand-mode-writing-up-10gbs","postDateTime":"2024-11-20T16:30:00-05:00","contentType":"launch announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams On-Demand mode supports streams writing up to 10GB/s"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p163535905","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"giAS7MqGaKMHsYi2K3naqu","dateCreated":"2024-10-22T18:08:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-11-11T18:16:02+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams now provides AWS CloudFormation supports for managing resource policies for data streams and consumers. You can use CloudFormation templates to programmatically deploy resource policies in a secure, efficient, and repeatable way, reducing the risk of human error from manual configuration.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nKinesis Data Streams allows users to capture, process, and store data streams in real time at any scale. CloudFormation uses stacks to manage AWS resources, allowing you to track changes, apply updates automatically, and easily roll back changes when needed.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nCloudFormation support for resource policies is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is offered, including the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions and China Regions. To learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Streams resource policies, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/controlling-access.html#sharing-data-streams\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/11/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-cloudformation-resource-policies","postDateTime":"2024-11-11T13:15:00-05:00","contentType":"launch announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams launches CloudFormation support for resource policies"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"serverless","description":"marketing:marchitecture/serverless","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p128454236","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"8uW5d9PSBGrTVAsywyVHhC","dateCreated":"2024-06-13T18:32:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-25T20:48:02+0000","additionalFields":{"regionalAvailability":"\u003cp\u003eAttribute-based access control (ABAC) for Kinesis Data Streams is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e, including the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nFor more information on getting started with ABAC in Kinesis Data Streams, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/tagging.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation.\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about ABAC in Amazon Web Services, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/identity/attribute-based-access-control/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAttribute-Based Access Control (ABAC) for AWS.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams announces support for attribute-based access control (ABAC) using stream tags, enabling customers to enhance their overall security postures with a scalable access control solution. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless data streaming service that enables customers to capture, process, and store data streams at any scale. ABAC is an authorization strategy that defines access permissions based on tags which can be attached to IAM resources, such as IAM users and roles, and to AWS resources for fine-grained access control.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nABAC support for Kinesis Data Streams makes it simple for you to give granular access to developers without requiring a policy update when a user or project is added, removed or updated. With ABAC support for Kinesis Data Streams, IAM policies can be used to allow or deny specific Kinesis Data Streams API actions when the IAM principal\u0026#39;s tags match the tags on a data stream.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nGetting started with ABAC for Kinesis Data Streams is easy. Kinesis Data Streams supports using stream tags and attaching them to IAM policies that allow or deny access to the Kinesis Data Stream based on your tags. You can use the Amazon APIs, the Amazon CLI, or the Amazon Web Services Management Console to tag your resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/09/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-abac","postDateTime":"2024-09-25T16:46:00-04:00","contentType":"launch announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams announces support for Attribute-Based Access Control (ABAC)"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-17T18:03:36+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#p147123112","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"bU2joVghdAZwYafjs9gTz3","dateCreated":"2024-08-14T17:59:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-06T20:30:28+0000","additionalFields":{"nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, Amazon Kinesis Data Streams supports adding a VPC endpoint using AWS PrivateLink that connects through the regional endpoint that has been validated under the Federal Information Processing Standard (FIPS) 140-3 program. With this new launch, you can easily use AWS PrivateLink with Kinesis Data Streams for those regulated workloads that require a secure connection using a FIPS 140-3 validated cryptographic module.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nFIPS compliant endpoints helps companies contracting with the US federal governments meet the FIPS security requirement to encrypt sensitive data in supported Regions. To create an interface VPC endpoint that connects to a Kinesis Data Streams FIPS endpoint, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/vpc.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eusing Amazon Kinesis Data Streams with Interface VPC Endpoints\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nThis new capability is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e in the United States, including the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. To learn more about AWS PrivateLink, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/privatelink-access-aws-services.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eaccessing AWS services through AWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about FIPS 140-3 at AWS, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/fips/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eFIPS 140-3 Compliance\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/09/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-fips-140-3-interface-vpc-endpoint","postDateTime":"2024-09-06T16:25:00-04:00","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports FIPS 140-3 enabled interface VPC endpoint"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"serverless","description":"marketing:marchitecture/serverless","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#v1360533934","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"xoojAdsStPLRoymaw44s5C","dateCreated":"2024-05-16T15:34:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-05-24T21:11:12+0000","additionalFields":{"regionalAvailability":"\u003cp\u003eLogging data plane Kinesis Data Streams APIs using AWS CloudTrail is now available in all commercial AWS Regions and AWS GovCloud (US) Regions.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nTo learn more about logging data plane APIs using AWS CloudTrail, see AWS Documentation. For more information about CloudTrail, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/\"\u003eAWS CloudTrail User Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nofollow":"0","noindex":"0","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, Amazon Kinesis Data Streams announces support for logging data plane APIs using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudtrail/\"\u003eAWS CloudTrail\u003c/a\u003e, enabling customers to have greater visibility into data stream activity in their AWS account for best practices in security and operational troubleshooting. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless data streaming service that enables customers to capture, process, and store data streams at any scale.\u003cbr /\u003e\n\u003cbr /\u003e\nCloudTrail captures API activities related to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams as events, including calls from the Amazon Kinesis Data Streams console and calls made programmatically using Amazon Kinesis Data Streams APIs. Using the information that CloudTrail collects, you can identify a specific request to an Amazon Kinesis Data Streams API, the IP address of the requester, the requester\u0026#39;s identity, and the date and time of the request. Logging Kinesis Data Streams APIs using CloudTrail helps you enable operational and risk auditing, governance, and compliance of your AWS account. Kinesis Data Streams APIs that are now supported for CloudTrail logging are:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cul\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eGetRecords\u003c/li\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eGetShardIterator\u003c/li\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003ePutRecord\u003c/li\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003ePutRecords\u003c/li\u003e\n\t\u003cli\u003eSubscribeToShard\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTo opt-in for CloudTrail logging of the above mentioned data plane APIs, you can simply configure logging on your data stream using the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/cloudtrail\"\u003eAWS CloudTrail Console\u003c/a\u003e or by using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/logging-data-events-with-cloudtrail.html\"\u003eCloudTrail APIs\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","nosnippet":"0","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2024/05/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-data-plane-logging-aws-cloudtrail","postDateTime":"2024-05-20T04:00:00-04:00","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams supports data plane logging to AWS CloudTrail"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-cloudtrail","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-cloudtrail","description":"general:products/aws-cloudtrail","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2024","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2024","description":"year#2024","dateCreated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-01-02T21:28:59+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-12-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-zero-buffering","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-zero-buffering/","dateCreated":"2023-12-26T21:57:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:44:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWith zero buffering, customers can deliver data to Amazon S3, Amazon OpenSearch Service, Amazon Redshift, and third-party HTTP destinations within seconds enabling real time use cases. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eCurrently, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose buffers data for at least sixty seconds before delivering it to a destination. However, many customers want faster insights from their data. With zero buffering, customers can setup a Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose stream to not buffer data before delivery, and most streams with no additional processing are delivered within five seconds. To meet lower latency use cases, zero buffering is also supported for Lambda that is used by customers for data transformation within Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. For some use cases where zero buffering is not suitable, customers have the flexibility to choose a lower buffering interval anywhere from zero to maximum buffering interval range.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor third party destinations, before you make the change, please check with the vendor for recommended buffering settings of Kinesis Data Firehose.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS. To get started with Kinesis Data Firehose, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;To learn more about zero buffering, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/buffering-hints.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-12-26T21:56:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-zero-buffering/","postDateTime":"2023-12-26T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now supports zero buffering","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWith zero buffering, customers can deliver data to Amazon S3, Amazon OpenSearch Service, Amazon Redshift, and third-party HTTP destinations within seconds enabling real time use cases. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-12-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-decompressed-cloudwatch-logs-destinations","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-decompressed-cloudwatch-logs-destinations/","dateCreated":"2023-12-15T17:59:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:02:08+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose now delivers decompressed CloudWatch Logs to S3 and Splunk destinations.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon CloudWatch Logs enable customers to aggregate log events from their systems, applications, and services for monitoring purposes. Customers use Amazon CloudWatch Logs subscriptions to deliver log events using Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to Amazon S3 and Splunk for troubleshooting and monitoring use cases. CloudWatch Logs are delivered as gzip-compressed objects and with the support of decompression for Cloudwatch Logs in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, customers can now automatically deliver decompressed logs. This eliminates the need for additional services or post-processing to do decompression and allows customers to use optional Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose features such as Data Format Conversion or Dynamic Partitioning.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data. To get started with Kinesis Data Firehose, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:46:10Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/12/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-decompressed-cloudwatch-logs-destinations/","postDateTime":"2023-12-15T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose supports delivery of decompressed CloudWatch Logs to destinations","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose now delivers decompressed CloudWatch Logs to S3 and Splunk destinations.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-ingestion","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-ingestion/","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:39:42+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams now offers fully managed capabilities to stream video and audio in real-time from Web Real-time Communication (WebRTC) standards compliant cameras, IoT devices and browsers to the cloud for secure storage, playback and analytical processing. Customers can now use our enhanced WebRTC SDK and cloud APIs to enable real-time streaming as well as media ingestion to the cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you can install the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-sdk-c/tree/wrtc-stream-ingestion-support\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC SDK\u003c/a\u003e on any security camera or IoT device with a video sensor, and use our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_Operations_Amazon_Kinesis_Video_Streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAPIs\u003c/a\u003e to enable media streaming with sub 1-second latency, as well as ingestion and storage in the cloud. Once ingested, you can access your data through our easy-to-use APIs. Amazon Kinesis Video Streams enables you to playback video for live and on-demand viewing, and quickly build applications that take advantage of computer vision and video analytics through integration with Amazon Rekognition Video, and Amazon SageMaker.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC Ingestion is available in all regions\u0026nbsp;where Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is available, except for the China (Beijing, operated by Sinnet) Region. To learn more about these new capabilities for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/webrtc-ingestion.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGetting Started Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-11-08T19:07:24Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-ingestion/","postDateTime":"2023-11-08T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC Ingestion is now generally available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams now offers fully managed capabilities to stream video and audio in real-time from Web Real-time Communication (WebRTC) standards compliant cameras, IoT devices and browsers to the cloud for secure storage, playback and analytical processing. Customers can now use our enhanced WebRTC SDK and cloud APIs to enable real-time streaming as well as media ingestion to the cloud.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-11-amazon-kinesis-data-streams-eventbridge-pipes-console","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-eventbridge-pipes-console/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:04:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:47:55+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday, Amazon Kinesis Data Streams announces an integration with Amazon EventBridge Pipes in the Kinesis Data Streams service console, making it easier to send records from your stream to one of over 14 AWS service targets, including Amazon SQS, AWS Step Functions, Amazon SNS, Amazon ECS, Amazon EventBridge event buses, or another Kinesis Data Stream. The EventBridge Pipes integration also supports the EventBridge API Destinations target which uses API calls to send your Kinesis Data Stream records to software as a service (SaaS) applications or your own applications within or outside AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eGetting your data flowing from your Kinesis Data Stream is as simple as clicking the “Connect Kinesis Data Stream to pipe” button on the selected Kinesis Data Stream page, naming the connection, and selecting a target. You can customize batch size, batch window, concurrency, and more, if desired. An optional filtering step allows only specific records to flow into the pipe and an optional enrichment step using AWS Lambda, AWS Step Functions, API Destinations, or Amazon API Gateway can be used to enrich or transform your Kinesis Data Stream records before they reach the target. By removing the need to write, manage, and scale undifferentiated integration code, the EventBridge Pipes integration allows you spend your time building your services rather than connecting them.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eGet started by selecting a Kinesis Data Stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eKinesis console\u003c/a\u003e, and then selecting the EventBridge Pipes tab, or, learn more by reading the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/new-create-point-to-point-integrations-between-event-producers-and-consumers-with-amazon-eventbridge-pipes/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS News blog post\u003c/a\u003e on how Amazon EventBridge Pipes can help you more easily integrate your services.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-11-03T20:42:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/11/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-eventbridge-pipes-console/","postDateTime":"2023-11-03T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams announces Amazon EventBridge Pipes console integration","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday, Amazon Kinesis Data Streams announces an integration with Amazon EventBridge Pipes in the Kinesis Data Streams service console, making it easier to send records from your stream to one of over 14 AWS service targets, including Amazon SQS, AWS Step Functions, Amazon SNS, Amazon ECS, Amazon EventBridge event buses, or another Kinesis Data Stream. The EventBridge Pipes integration also supports the EventBridge API Destinations target which uses API calls to send your Kinesis Data Stream records to software as a service (SaaS) applications or your own applications within or outside AWS.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#application-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"application-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/application-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-eventbridge","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-eventBridge","description":"general:products/amazon-eventBridge","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:42+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-10-amazon-kinesis-data-streams-increases-write-throughput-limit","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/10/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-increases-write-throughput-limit/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:10:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:58:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports On-Demand write throughput limit of 2 GB/s, a 2x increase from the current limit of 1 GB/s. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless streaming data service that makes it easier to capture, process, and store streaming data at any scale. On-Demand is a capacity mode for Kinesis Data Streams that automates capacity management, so that you never have to provision and manage the scaling of resources. It requires you to pay for throughput consumed rather than for provisioned resources, making it easier to balance costs and performance while providing the same availability, durability, and integrations. You can create a new On-Demand data stream or convert an existing data stream into the On-Demand mode with a single-click without requiring any code changes or downtime for your existing applications.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eBy default, On-Demand mode can automatically scale up to 200MB/s write and 400MB/s read throughput. Earlier in the year, we increased this limit up to 1 GB/s write and 2GB/s read throughput. As we continue to innovate to provide more powerful streaming capabilities, you can now request a limit increase through AWS Support to enable your On-Demand stream to scale up to 2 GB/s write and 4 GB/s read throughput.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe increased limit is available in all AWS Regions, including the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. Submit a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://support.console.aws.amazon.com/support/home#/case/create?issueType\u003dservice-limit-increase\u0026amp;limitType\u003dkinesis-streams\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eSupport Ticket\u003c/a\u003e to request the limit increase for your account. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/service-sizes-and-limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eQuotas and Limits\u003c/a\u003e page to learn more.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-10-30T17:19:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/10/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-increases-write-throughput-limit/","postDateTime":"2023-10-30T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams increases On-Demand write throughput limit to 2 GB/s","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports On-Demand write throughput limit of 2 GB/s, a 2x increase from the current limit of 1 GB/s. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless streaming data service that makes it easier to capture, process, and store streaming data at any scale. On-Demand is a capacity mode for Kinesis Data Streams that automates capacity management, so that you never have to provision and manage the scaling of resources. It requires you to pay for throughput consumed rather than for provisioned resources, making it easier to balance costs and performance while providing the same availability, durability, and integrations. You can create a new On-Demand data stream or convert an existing data stream into the On-Demand mode with a single-click without requiring any code changes or downtime for your existing applications.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-09-amazon-chime-sdk-webrtc-audio-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/09/amazon-chime-sdk-webrtc-audio-kinesis-video-streams/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:03:00+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:53:26+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Chime SDK media pipelines now enable the sending of Amazon Chime SDK WebRTC audio to Amazon Kinesis Video Streams.  With the Amazon Chime SDK, developers can add real-time audio, video, and screen share to their web and mobile applications. Sending WebRTC session audio to Amazon Kinesis Video Streams provides developers access to the audio for live analysis during the session.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eDevelopers can send the meeting audio to a single stream, the audio for each attendee to a separate stream, or both - depending on their use case.  For example, if using audio to perform conversation analysis, sending each attendee’s audio in a separate stream enables attendee-specific analysis and attribution.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe ability to send Amazon Chime SDK WebRTC audio to Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is available in all Media Pipeline Regions. To learn more, review the following resources:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/chime/chime-sdk/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Chime SDK website\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams website\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/chime-sdk/latest/dg/create-media-stream-pipeline.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCreating media stream pipelines\u003c/a\u003e in the Developer Guide\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/chime-sdk/latest/dg/sdk-available-regions.html#sdk-media-pipelines\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAvailable regions\u003c/a\u003e in the Developer Guide\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-09-26T16:56:06Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/09/amazon-chime-sdk-webrtc-audio-kinesis-video-streams/","postDateTime":"2023-09-26T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Chime SDK now supports sending WebRTC audio to Amazon Kinesis Video Streams","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Chime SDK media pipelines now enable the sending of Amazon Chime SDK WebRTC audio to Amazon Kinesis Video Streams.  With the Amazon Chime SDK, developers can add real-time audio, video, and screen share to their web and mobile applications. Sending WebRTC session audio to Amazon Kinesis Video Streams provides developers access to the audio for live analysis during the session.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#business-productivity","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"business-productivity","description":"marketing:marchitecture/business-productivity","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:38+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-chime-sdk","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-chime-sdk","description":"general:products/amazon-chime-sdk","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:51+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#media-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"media-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/media-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-08-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-israel-tel-aviv-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-israel-tel-aviv-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:35:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e in the Israel (Tel Aviv) AWS Region. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch, and third-party providers like Splunk and Datadog etc., enabling near real-time analytics. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write any code to process and deliver your data. You can configure your producers to automatically deliver your data to the destination that you specify. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\nFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003csub\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:42:51Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/08/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-israel-tel-aviv-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2023-08-01T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in Israel (Tel Aviv) AWS Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e in the Israel (Tel Aviv) AWS Region. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-06-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-edge-agent","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-edge-agent/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:51:32+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:57:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe are announcing the general availability of the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Edge Agent. This feature offers a simple, efficient, and cost-effective way to connect to IP cameras on customer premises, locally record and store video from those cameras, and stream videos to the cloud on a customer-defined schedule for long term storage, playback, and analytical processing.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can download the Amazon Kinesis Video Edge Agent and deploy it on your on-premise edge compute devices. Alternatively, you can easily deploy them in docker containers running on Amazon EC2 machines. Once deployed, you can use the new Amazon Kinesis Video Streams \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/edge.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAPIs\u003c/a\u003e to update video recording and cloud uploading configurations. The feature works with any IP camera that can stream over RTSP protocol, and requires no additional firmware deployment on the cameras.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWe offer the following installations for the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Edge Agent:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eOn \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/snowball/latest/developer-guide/using-ami.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Snowball Edge\u003c/a\u003e devices\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eAs a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/greengrass/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGreengrass\u003c/a\u003e component on Greengrass qualified devices\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003eOn a native IoT deployment: The Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Edge Agent leverages \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/iot-gs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS IoT core\u003c/a\u003e for managing edge configuration through the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_Operations_Amazon_Kinesis_Video_Streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEdge cloud APIs\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe Kinesis Video Streams Edge Agent and APIs are now available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is available, except for the Africa (Cape Town) Region.\u0026nbsp;AWS will not charge for the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Edge Agent, though you may still incur Amazon Kinesis Video Streams or other AWS costs associated with usage of this product. To learn more about these new capabilities for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, see the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/edge.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e, and to access these components, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://pages.awscloud.com/GLOBAL-launch-DL-KVS-Edge-2023-learn.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-06-29T20:10:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-edge-agent/","postDateTime":"2023-06-29T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Edge Agent is now generally available","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe are announcing the general availability of the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Edge Agent. This feature offers a simple, efficient, and cost-effective way to connect to IP cameras on customer premises, locally record and store video from those cameras, and stream videos to the cloud on a customer-defined schedule for long term storage, playback, and analytical processing.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-06-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-studio-apache-flink-version-1-15","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-studio-apache-flink-version-1-15/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:02:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:35:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now use Apache Flink 1.15 with Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Studio to perform ad hoc queries to quickly inspect data streams and build and run stream processing applications in minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Data Analytics Studio allows you to query data streams in real time, and more easily build and run stream processing applications using standard SQL, Python, and Scala in an interactive notebook. Studio notebooks are powered by \u003ca href\u003d\"https://zeppelin.apache.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eApache Zeppelin\u003c/a\u003e and use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://flink.apache.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eApache Flink\u003c/a\u003e as the stream processing engine. Studio notebooks seamlessly combine these technologies to make advanced analytics on data streams accessible to developers of all skill sets. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn more about Kinesis Data Analytics Studio in our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/how-notebook.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. For Kinesis Data Analytics region availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csup\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003cb\u003eAugust, 30 2023:\u003c/b\u003e Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics has been renamed to Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink.\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-30T17:51:48Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-studio-apache-flink-version-1-15/","postDateTime":"2023-06-28T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Studio now supports Apache Flink version 1.15","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now use Apache Flink 1.15 with Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Studio to perform ad hoc queries to quickly inspect data streams and build and run stream processing applications in minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-managed-service-for-apache-flink","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-managed-service-for-apache-flink","description":"general:products/amazon-managed-service-for-apache-flink","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:49:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:49:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-06-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-stream-delivery-redshift-serverless","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-stream-delivery-redshift-serverless/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T15:00:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:48:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e can now deliver streaming data to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/redshift/redshift-serverless/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Redshift Serverless\u003c/a\u003e. With few clicks, you can more easily ingest, transform, and reliably deliver streaming data into Amazon Redshift Serverless without building and managing your own data ingestion and delivery infrastructure. Kinesis Data Firehose is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and without ongoing administration.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Redshift Serverless allows you to run and scale analytics without having to provision and manage data warehouse clusters. With Amazon Redshift Serverless, all users including data analysts, developers, and data scientists, can use Amazon Redshift to get insights from data in seconds. You only pay for the compute used for the duration of the workloads on a per-second basis. You can benefit from this simplicity without making any changes to your existing analytics and business intelligence applications. You can configure the Amazon Redshift Serverless instance to be publicly accessible and start using Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose with it to reliably load real-time streams.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose with Amazon Redshift Serverless is generally available in the regions \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/redshift-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e under Redshift Serverless API section.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:40:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/06/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-data-stream-delivery-redshift-serverless/","postDateTime":"2023-06-19T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds support for data stream delivery to Amazon Redshift Serverless","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e can now deliver streaming data to \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/redshift/redshift-serverless.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Redshift Serverless\u003c/a\u003e. With few clicks, you can more easily ingest, transform, and reliably deliver streaming data into Amazon Redshift Serverless without building and managing your own data ingestion and delivery infrastructure. Kinesis Data Firehose is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and without ongoing administration.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-05-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-document-id-amazon-opensearch-service","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-document-id-amazon-opensearch-service/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:59:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:02:43+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e customers can now send data to Amazon OpenSearch Service using OpenSearch Service auto-generated document ID option. This configuration option enables write-heavy operations, such as log analytics and observability, to consume fewer CPU resources at the OpenSearch domain, resulting in improved performance.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into Amazon OpenSearch Service and Amazon OpenSearch Serverless. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You can configure your producers to automatically deliver your data to the destination that you specify. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. Kinesis Data Firehose is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and without ongoing administration. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:34:45Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/05/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-document-id-amazon-opensearch-service/","postDateTime":"2023-05-11T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds support for document ID that is auto-generated by Amazon OpenSearch Service","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e customers can now send data to Amazon OpenSearch Service using OpenSearch Service auto-generated document ID option. This configuration option enables write-heavy operations, such as log analytics and observability, to consume fewer CPU resources at the OpenSearch domain, resulting in improved performance.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-03-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-asia-pacific-melbourne-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-asia-pacific-melbourne-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:48:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:53:51+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e in the Asia Pacific (Melbourne) AWS Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch, and third-party providers like Splunk and Datadog etc., enabling near real-time analytics. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You can configure your producers to automatically deliver your data to the destination that you specify. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csub\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eAs of Feb 09, 2024, Kinesis Data Firehose is now Amazon Data Firehose\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2024-02-14T19:32:05Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-asia-pacific-melbourne-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2023-03-13T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in Asia Pacific (Melbourne) AWS Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, customers can use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e in the Asia Pacific (Melbourne) AWS Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-03-amazon-kinesis-data-streams-on-demand-write-throughput-1gb","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-on-demand-write-throughput-1gb/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:44:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:35:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports an increased On-Demand write throughput limit to 1 GB/s, a 5x increase from the current limit of 200 MB/s. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless streaming data service that makes it easy to capture, process, and store streaming data at any scale. On-Demand is a capacity mode for Kinesis Data Streams that automates capacity management, so that you never have to provision and manage the scaling of resources. In the On-Demand mode you pay for throughput consumed rather than for provisioned resources, making it easier to balance costs and performance.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eBy default, On-Demand capacity mode can automatically scale up to 200MB/s of write and 400MB/s of read throughput. Now you can request a limit increase through AWS Support to enable your On-Demand stream to scale up to 1 GB/s write and 2 GB/s read throughput.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can create a new On-Demand data stream or convert an existing data stream into the On-Demand mode with a single-click. When you choose On-Demand capacity mode, Kinesis Data Streams automatically accommodates your workloads as they ramp up. On-Demand mode provides the same high availability and durability that Kinesis Data Streams already offers. When switching existing streams to On-Demand, you can continue to use your existing applications without making any code changes or requiring downtime. On-Demand streams work with all existing AWS integrations, such as Amazon CloudWatch Logs, Amazon DynamoDB, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, Amazon Lambda, and open-source technologies such as Apache Spark and Apache Flink.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe 1GB/s write throughput limit increase for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams On-Demand is available in all AWS Regions, including the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. Submit a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://support.console.aws.amazon.com/support/home#/case/create?issueType\u003dservice-limit-increase\u0026amp;limitType\u003dkinesis-streams\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eSupport Ticket\u003c/a\u003e to request the limit increase for your account. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/service-sizes-and-limits.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eQuotas and Limits\u003c/a\u003e page to learn more.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-03-01T20:35:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/03/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-on-demand-write-throughput-1gb/","postDateTime":"2023-03-01T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams increases On-Demand write throughput limit to 1 GB/s","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports an increased On-Demand write throughput limit to 1 GB/s, a 5x increase from the current limit of 200 MB/s. Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless streaming data service that makes it easy to capture, process, and store streaming data at any scale. On-Demand is a capacity mode for Kinesis Data Streams that automates capacity management, so that you never have to provision and manage the scaling of resources. In the On-Demand mode you pay for throughput consumed rather than for provisioned resources, making it easier to balance costs and performance.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-02-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-middle-east-uae-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-middle-east-uae-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:57:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:34:14+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics makes it easier to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Opensearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams, Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors. You can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of the AWS Regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-02-20T19:37:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-middle-east-uae-region/","postDateTime":"2023-02-20T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in the Middle East (UAE) region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics makes it easier to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Opensearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams, Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors. You can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2023-02-amazon-kinesis-data-streams-dynamodb-aws-cloudformation-global-tables","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-dynamodb-aws-cloudformation-global-tables/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:43:56+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T15:01:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/kds.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams for Amazon DynamoDB\u003c/a\u003e now supports AWS CloudFormation for DynamoDB \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/dynamodb/global-tables/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eglobal tables\u003c/a\u003e, which means you can enable streaming to an Amazon Kinesis data stream on your DynamoDB global tables with CloudFormation templates. By streaming your DynamoDB data changes to a Kinesis data stream, you can build advanced streaming applications with Amazon Kinesis services. For example, Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building, managing, and integrating with Apache Flink and provides built-in functions to filter, aggregate, and transform streaming data for advanced analytics. You also can use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to take advantage of managed streaming delivery of DynamoDB table data to other AWS services such as Amazon OpenSearch Service, Amazon Redshift, and Amazon S3.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eGlobal tables build on the global Amazon DynamoDB footprint to provide you with a fully managed, multi-Region, and multi-active database that delivers fast, local, read and write performance for massively scaled, global applications. Global tables replicate your DynamoDB tables automatically across your choice of AWS Regions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Kinesis Data Streams for DynamoDB, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/kds.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eChange Data Capture for Kinesis Data Streams with DynamoDB\u003c/a\u003e. For more information about working with CloudFormation, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/Welcome.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eWhat Is AWS CloudFormation\u003c/a\u003e?\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-02-16T19:20:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2023/02/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-dynamodb-aws-cloudformation-global-tables/","postDateTime":"2023-02-15T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams for Amazon DynamoDB now supports AWS CloudFormation for Global Tables","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/kds.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams for Amazon DynamoDB\u003c/a\u003e now supports AWS CloudFormation for DynamoDB \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/dynamodb/global-tables.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eglobal tables\u003c/a\u003e, which means you can enable streaming to an Amazon Kinesis data stream on your DynamoDB global tables with CloudFormation templates. By streaming your DynamoDB data changes to a Kinesis data stream, you can build advanced streaming applications with Amazon Kinesis services. For example, Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building, managing, and integrating with Apache Flink and provides built-in functions to filter, aggregate, and transform streaming data for advanced analytics. You also can use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to take advantage of managed streaming delivery of DynamoDB table data to other AWS services such as Amazon OpenSearch Service, Amazon Redshift, and Amazon S3.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-cloudformation","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-cloudformation","description":"general:products/aws-cloudformation","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2023","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2023","description":"year#2023","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-dynamodb","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-dynamodb","description":"general:products/amazon-dynamodb","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:06+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-12-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-edge-recording-scheduled-cloud-streaming-preview","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-edge-recording-scheduled-cloud-streaming-preview/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:29:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams now offers a simple, efficient and cost-effective way to connect to IP cameras on customer premises, locally record and store video from those cameras, and stream videos to the cloud on a customer defined schedule for long term storage, playback and analytical processing.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can download the KVS edge runtime agent and deploy it at your on-premise edge compute devices. Alternatively, you can easily deploy them in docker containers running on Amazon EC2 machines. Once deployed, you can use the new Amazon Kinesis Video Streams \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/edge.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAPIs\u003c/a\u003e to update video recording and cloud uploading configurations. The feature works with any IP camera that can stream over RTSP protocol, and requires no additional firmware deployment on the cameras.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWe offer the following Amazon Kinesis Video Streams installations for the edge runtime agent:\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eOn Snowball Edge:\u003c/b\u003e You can run the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams edge runtime agent on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/snowball/latest/developer-guide/using-ami.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Snowball Edge\u003c/a\u003e devices\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eAs a Greengrass component:\u003c/b\u003e You can install the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams edge runtime agent as a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/greengrass/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGreengrass\u003c/a\u003e component on any Greengrass certified device\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eOn a native IoT deployment:\u003c/b\u003e You can install the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams edge runtime agent natively on any compute instance: Edge SDK leverages \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iot/latest/developerguide/iot-gs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS IoT core\u003c/a\u003e for managing edge configuration through the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_Operations_Amazon_Kinesis_Video_Streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEdge cloud APIs\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eKVS edge runtime and APIs are available in the US West (Oregon) Region. AWS will not charge for the use of this feature during the preview period, though you may still incur KVS or other AWS costs associated with usage. To learn more about these new capabilities for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, see documentation, and to access these components, \u003ca href\u003d\"mailto:%20kinesis-video-edge-info@amazon.com\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eemail us\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-12-14T22:26:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-edge-recording-scheduled-cloud-streaming-preview/","postDateTime":"2022-12-14T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams announces edge recording and scheduled cloud streaming capabilities (preview)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams now offers a simple, efficient and cost-effective way to connect to IP cameras on customer premises, locally record and store video from those cameras, and stream videos to the cloud on a customer defined schedule for long term storage, playback and analytical processing.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#internet-of-things","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"internet-of-things","description":"marketing:marchitecture/internet-of-things","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-apache-flink-supports-flink-version-1-15","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-apache-flink-supports-flink-version-1-15/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:53:45+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:50:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink now supports Apache Flink version 1.15. This new version includes improvements to Flink\u0027s exactly-once processing semantics, Kinesis Data Streams and Kinesis Data Firehose connectors, Python User Defined Functions, Flink SQL, and more. The release also includes an AWS-contributed capability, a new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://flink.apache.org/2022/05/06/async-sink-base.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAsync-Sink\u003c/a\u003e framework which simplifies the creation of custom sinks to deliver processed data. For a complete list of features, improvements, and bug fixes please see the Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/flink-1-15-2.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003erelease notes\u003c/a\u003e for 1.15.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics makes it easier to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Opensearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams, Amazon S3, custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn more about Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink in our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and what Apache Flink 1.15 offers by visiting the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-release-1.15/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eofficial website\u003c/a\u003e. For Kinesis Data Analytics region availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003csup\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003cb\u003eAugust, 30 2023:\u003c/b\u003e Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics has been renamed to Amazon Managed Service for Apache Flink.\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/sup\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2023-08-30T17:52:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-apache-flink-supports-flink-version-1-15/","postDateTime":"2022-11-22T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink now supports Apache Flink version 1.15","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink now supports Apache Flink version 1.15. This new version includes improvements to Flink\u0027s exactly-once processing semantics, Kinesis Data Streams and Kinesis Data Firehose connectors, Python User Defined Functions, Flink SQL, and more. The release also includes an AWS-contributed capability, a new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://flink.apache.org/2022/05/06/async-sink-base.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAsync-Sink\u003c/a\u003e framework which simplifies the creation of custom sinks to deliver processed data. For a complete list of features, improvements, and bug fixes please see the Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/flink-1-15-2.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003erelease notes\u003c/a\u003e for 1.15.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-managed-service-for-apache-flink","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-managed-service-for-apache-flink","description":"general:products/amazon-managed-service-for-apache-flink","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:49:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:49:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-11-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-middle-east-uae-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-middle-east-uae-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:55:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:38:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch, and third party providers like Splunk and Datadog, enabling near real-time analytics.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You can configure your producers to automatically deliver your data to the destination that you specify. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;For Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-11-04T21:11:36Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-middle-east-uae-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2022-11-04T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in the Middle East (UAE) AWS region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch, and third party providers like Splunk and Datadog, enabling near real-time analytics.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-10-amazon-kinesis-data-streams-capability-inspect-data-records-aws-management-console","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/10/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-capability-inspect-data-records-aws-management-console/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:54:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:39:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless streaming data service that makes it easy to capture, process, and store streaming data at massive scale. Data Viewer is a new capability for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams that allows viewing data records directly from AWS Management Console. As a result, you can easily inspect the data records without programming a dedicated consumer app just to view the data, quickly check the data structure of an unfamiliar stream, or query specific records for QA and troubleshooting. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo access Data Viewer, login to AWS Management Console for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams and navigate to detail page of your data stream. In the Data Viewer tab, you can select the shard, and then specify the starting position of the records that you want to view.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams Data Viewer is available in all AWS Regions. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/data-viewer.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e to learn more.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-10-31T20:57:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/10/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-capability-inspect-data-records-aws-management-console/","postDateTime":"2022-10-31T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams adds capability to easily inspect data records in AWS Management Console","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams is a serverless streaming data service that makes it easy to capture, process, and store streaming data at massive scale. Data Viewer is a new capability for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams that allows viewing data records directly from AWS Management Console. As a result, you can easily inspect the data records without programming a dedicated consumer app just to view the data, quickly check the data structure of an unfamiliar stream, or query specific records for QA and troubleshooting. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-apache-flink-three-container-level-metrics-cloudformation-support","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-apache-flink-three-container-level-metrics-cloudformation-support/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:59:52+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now publishes three new container-level metrics to Amazon CloudWatch: CPU Utilization, Memory Utilization, and Disk Utilization of Flink Task Managers. Task Managers are the worker nodes of a Flink application that perform the data processing. These new metrics provide enhanced visibility to Task Manager resource usage and can be used to easily scale applications running on Kinesis Data Analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith this launch,\u0026nbsp;Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics also provides improved logging performance and CloudFormation support for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-properties-kinesisanalyticsv2-application-vpcconfiguration.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eVPC applications\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-properties-kinesisanalyticsv2-application-applicationmaintenanceconfiguration.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMaintenance Windows\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics makes it easy to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Opensearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams, Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors. You can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics region availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-21T18:54:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-apache-flink-three-container-level-metrics-cloudformation-support/","postDateTime":"2022-09-09T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink supports three new container level metrics and improved CloudFormation support ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now publishes three new container-level metrics to Amazon CloudWatch: CPU Utilization, Memory Utilization, and Disk Utilization of Flink Task Managers. Task Managers are the worker nodes of a Flink application that perform the data processing. These new metrics provide enhanced visibility to Task Manager resource usage and can be used to easily scale applications running on Kinesis Data Analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-09-amazon-vpc-flow-logs-delivered-amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-vpc-flow-logs-delivered-amazon-kinesis-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:52+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:46:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now deliver Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) Flow Logs directly to Amazon Kinesis Firehose, allowing you to stream your flow logs real-time to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-destination.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edestinations supported by Amazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/introducing-amazon-vpc-flow-logs-kinesis-data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edownstream logging solutions\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;via custom HTTP endpoints.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVPC Flow Logs enable you to capture and log information about your VPC network traffic. Until today, you could deliver VPC Flow Logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3). With this release, you can now stream your flow logs in real-time to supported Amazon Kinesis Firehose destinations. In addition, you can also use AWS Lambda functions on Amazon Kinesis to enrich or transform the VPC Flow logs while delivering them to downstream logging solutions.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVPC Flow Log delivery to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available through the AWS Management Console, the AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI), and the AWS Software Development Kit (AWS SDK). To get started, simply create a new flow log subscription and select Amazon Kinesis Firehose as a destination. To learn more about Amazon VPC Flow Logs delivery to Amazon Kinesis Firehose, please refer to the Amazon Kinesis Firehose documentation and VPC Flow Logs documentation. See the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/introducing-amazon-vpc-flow-logs-kinesis-data-firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e to learn about AWS Partner Network solutions that support ingestion of VPC Flow Logs to Amazon Kinesis Firehose. Refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eCloudWatch pricing\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;for cost of delivering VPC Flow Logs to Amazon Kinesis Firehose.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVPC Flow Logs delivery to Amazon Kinesis Firehose is generally available in the following AWS Regions:\u0026nbsp;US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (Northern California), US West (Oregon), Africa (Cape Town), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), Asia Pacific (Jakarta), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Osaka), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Canada (Central), Europe (Frankfurt), Europe (Ireland), Europe (London), Europe (Milan), Europe (Paris), Europe (Stockholm), South America (Sao Paulo), Middle East (Bahrain), AWS GovCloud (US-East) and AWS GovCloud (US-West).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-09-08T21:23:37Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/09/amazon-vpc-flow-logs-delivered-amazon-kinesis-firehose/","postDateTime":"2022-09-08T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) Flow Logs can now be delivered to Amazon Kinesis Firehose ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now deliver Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) Flow Logs directly to Amazon Kinesis Firehose, allowing you to stream your flow logs real-time to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-destination.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edestinations supported by Amazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/networking-and-content-delivery/introducing-amazon-vpc-flow-logs-kinesis-data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edownstream logging solutions\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;via custom HTTP endpoints.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-vpc","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-vpc","description":"general:products/amazon-vpc","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-05-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-fedramp-compliant","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-fedramp-compliant/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:48:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:21:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now authorized as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/fedramp/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFedRAMP\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;Moderate in\u0026nbsp;US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (N. California), US West (Oregon) and as FedRAMP High in AWS GovCloud (US-West) and AWS GovCloud (US-East).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThe Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program (FedRAMP) is a US government-wide program that delivers a standard approach to the security assessment, authorization, and continuous monitoring for cloud products and services. FedRAMP uses the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) Special Publication 800 series and requires cloud service providers to receive an independent security assessment conducted by a third-party assessment organization (3PAO), to ensure that authorizations are compliant with the Federal Information Security Management Act (FISMA). US Federal agencies and commercial customers working with the US Federal government can now utilize Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics to process streaming data in real time.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics makes it easier to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon DynamoDB Streams, Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about FedRAMP compliance for AWS services, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/compliance/services-in-scope/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ecompliance page\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-05-23T20:40:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-fedramp-compliant/","postDateTime":"2022-05-23T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now FedRAMP compliant ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now authorized as \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/compliance/fedramp.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFedRAMP\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;Moderate in\u0026nbsp;US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (N. California), US West (Oregon) and as FedRAMP High in AWS GovCloud (US-West) and AWS GovCloud (US-East).\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-05-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-asia-jakarta-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-asia-jakarta-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:52:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:19:34+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Asia Pacific (Jakarta) AWS Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. You can use it to capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch Service, and third party providers like Splunk and Datadog, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You can configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to automatically deliver the data to the destination that you specify. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e. For Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-05-06T15:47:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/05/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-asia-jakarta-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2022-05-06T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in the Asia Pacific (Jakarta) AWS Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Asia Pacific (Jakarta) AWS Region.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2022-01-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-delivers-honeycomb","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-delivers-honeycomb/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:46:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:16:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://partners.amazonaws.com/partners/0010L00001rElnvQAC/Honeycomb\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eHoneycomb\u003c/a\u003e, enabling Honeycomb users to ingest streaming data without having to manage applications or write code. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose makes it easier to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. It can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon OpenSearch Service, generic HTTP endpoints, and service providers like Honeycomb. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eThis new capability makes it easier than ever to route your AWS log data directly into Honeycomb. With these logs available in Honeycomb, you can instrument your own code then query, trace, graph, and alert on everything from system-wide events down to individual request traces in real time. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e to configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and specify Honeycomb as the destination. Once set, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose takes care of reliable, scalable delivery of your streaming data to Honeycomb. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2022-01-28T17:51:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2022/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-delivers-honeycomb/","postDateTime":"2022-01-28T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now delivers to Honeycomb","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://partners.amazonaws.com/partners/0010L00001rElnvQAC/Honeycomb\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eHoneycomb\u003c/a\u003e, enabling Honeycomb users to ingest streaming data without having to manage applications or write code. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2022","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2022","description":"year#2022","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:33:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-12-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-available-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/12/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-available-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:49:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:15:32+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is now available in the Asia Pacific (Osaka) and Africa (Cape Town) regions.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics makes it easier to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Opensearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams, Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors. You can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink and for SQL applications \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-12-09T21:57:44Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/12/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-available-regions/","postDateTime":"2021-12-09T08:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in the Asia Pacific (Osaka) and  Africa (Cape Town) regions.","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is now available in the Asia Pacific (Osaka) and Africa (Cape Town) regions.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-08-introducing-dynamic-partitioning-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/08/introducing-dynamic-partitioning-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:41:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:00:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eToday we announced Dynamic Partitioning in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. With Dynamic Partitioning, you can continuously partition streaming data in Kinesis Data Firehose using keys within data like “customer_id” or “transaction_id” and deliver data grouped by these keys into corresponding Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) prefixes, making it easier for you to run high performance, cost-efficient analytics on streaming data in Amazon S3 using Amazon Athena, Amazon EMR, and Amazon Redshift Spectrum.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003ePartitioning your data minimizes the amount of data scanned, optimizing performance and reducing costs of your analytics queries on Amazon S3, and increasing granular access to data. Traditionally, customers use Kinesis Data Firehose delivery streams to capture and load their data streams into Amazon S3. To partition a streaming data set for Amazon S3-based analytics, customers would need to run partitioning applications between Amazon S3 buckets prior to making the data available for analysis, which could become complicated or costly.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eNow with Dynamic Partitioning, Kinesis Data Firehose will continuously group data in-transit by dynamically or statically defined data keys, and deliver to individual Amazon S3 prefixes by key. This will reduce time-to-insight by minutes or hours, reducing costs and simplifying architectures. Along with Apache Parquet and Apache ORC format conversion features, this feature makes Kinesis Data Firehose the best place to capture, prepare, and load analytics-ready streaming data to Amazon S3.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/dynamic-partitioning.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003euser guide\u003c/a\u003e to get started with dynamic partitioning, or visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about on-demand pricing for dynamic partitioning. Dynamic partitioning can be used in all commercial AWS regions \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ewhere Kinesis Data Firehose is available\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-08T19:48:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/08/introducing-dynamic-partitioning-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","postDateTime":"2021-08-31T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Dynamic Partitioning in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eToday we announced Dynamic Partitioning in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. With Dynamic Partitioning, you can continuously partition streaming data in Kinesis Data Firehose using keys within data like “customer_id” or “transaction_id” and deliver data grouped by these keys into corresponding Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) prefixes, making it easier for you to run high performance, cost-efficient analytics on streaming data in Amazon S3 using Amazon Athena, Amazon EMR, and Amazon Redshift Spectrum.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-athena","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-athena","description":"general:products/amazon-athena","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#emr-studio","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"emr-studio","description":"general:products/emr-studio","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:30:06+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-05-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-supports-rollbackapplication-listapplicationversions-describeapplicationversion-apis","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-supports-rollbackapplication-listapplicationversions-describeapplicationversion-apis/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:42:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e for Apache Flink now supports three new application management APIs in preview. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/apiv2/API_RollbackApplication.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eRollbackApplication\u003c/a\u003e allows you to restore your application to the last running version and application state from the most recent, successful snapshot. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/apiv2/API_ListApplicationVersions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eListApplicationVersions\u003c/a\u003e allows you to get all application versions and a summary of the associated configurations. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/apiv2/API_DescribeApplicationVersion.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDescribeApplicationVersio\u003c/a\u003en gives you the most comprehensive view of the application configuration of a particular version.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eApplications can sometimes become unresponsive and stuck in a transient status such as creating, updating, autoscaling, or stopping. This is often due to misconfigurations that cause the application to become unhealthy. You can use the RollbackApplication API when your application is in the updating or autoscaling statuses to maintain your application’s uptime. In addition, ListApplicationVersions and DescribeApplicationVersion APIs can be used to retrieve information about all application versions, including those that were rolled back. You can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/troubleshooting-runtime.html#troubleshooting-symptoms\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTroubleshooting Guide\u003c/a\u003e for best practices to help you avoid and mitigate unresponsive applications.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Elasticsearch Service (Amazon ES), Amazon DynamoDB streams, Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors. You can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-05-11T20:20:08Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/05/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-supports-rollbackapplication-listapplicationversions-describeapplicationversion-apis/","postDateTime":"2021-05-11T07:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports RollbackApplication, ListApplicationVersions, and DescribeApplicationVersion APIs in preview","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e for Apache Flink now supports three new application management APIs in preview. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/apiv2/API_RollbackApplication.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eRollbackApplication\u003c/a\u003e allows you to restore your application to the last running version and application state from the most recent, successful snapshot. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/apiv2/API_ListApplicationVersions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eListApplicationVersions\u003c/a\u003e allows you to get all application versions and a summary of the associated configurations. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/apiv2/API_DescribeApplicationVersion.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDescribeApplicationVersio\u003c/a\u003en gives you the most comprehensive view of the application configuration of a particular version.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-04-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-apache-flink-introduces-custom-maintenance-windows-in-preview","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-apache-flink-introduces-custom-maintenance-windows-in-preview/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:38:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:14:28+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e for Apache Flink now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/apiv2/API_UpdateApplicationMaintenanceConfiguration.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUpdateApplicationMaintenanceConfiguration\u003c/a\u003e in preview. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics periodically patches the underlying infrastructure of applications with OS and container-image security updates to meet AWS compliance and security goals during the \u003ca target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/maintenance.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edefault maintenance windows\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u0026nbsp;in each region. You can use UpdateApplicationMaintenanceConfiguration via the CLI or the API to choose your preferred maintenance window start times for an application.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eMaintenance for your application’s infrastructure might occur at any time during the maintenance window. However, the downtime experienced by your application will be in the 10s of seconds when the application status changes to “MAINTENANCE”. Actual downtime depends on your application state. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink will automatically recover application state from the latest checkpoint or snapshot. To minimize downtime, ensure you are taking snapshots and frequent checkpoints regularly as recommended in the fault tolerance section\u0026nbsp;under \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/best-practices.html#how-dev-bp-checkpoint\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eBest Practices\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon DynamoDB Streams, Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors. You can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-04-30T23:38:48Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/04/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-apache-flink-introduces-custom-maintenance-windows-in-preview/","postDateTime":"2021-04-30T21:52:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink introduces custom maintenance windows in preview","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e for Apache Flink now supports \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/apiv2/API_UpdateApplicationMaintenanceConfiguration.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eUpdateApplicationMaintenanceConfiguration\u003c/a\u003e in preview. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics periodically patches the underlying infrastructure of applications with OS and container-image security updates to meet AWS compliance and security goals during the \u003ca target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/maintenance.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edefault maintenance windows\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u0026nbsp;in each region. You can use UpdateApplicationMaintenanceConfiguration via the CLI or the API to choose your preferred maintenance window start times for an application.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-03-announcing-amazon-cloudwatch-metric-streams","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/announcing-amazon-cloudwatch-metric-streams/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:11:09+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAnnouncing Amazon CloudWatch Metric Streams - a new feature that enables customers to create a continuous, near real-time stream of metrics to a destination of their choice. \u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can use Metric Streams to send metrics to partner solutions including Datadog, New Relic, Splunk, Dynatrace and Sumo Logic. Alternatively, you can send metrics to your data lake on AWS, such as Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3). This enables you to continuously ingest monitoring data, and combine billing and performance data with the latest CloudWatch metric data to create rich datasets. You can then use tools such as Amazon Athena to get insight into cost optimization, resource performance and resource utilization. Metric Streams are fully-managed, scalable, and easy to set up, reducing overhead. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, click on the Streams link under Metrics in the left navigation panel of the CloudWatch console. You can set up a stream of metrics to be delivered to S3 with a few clicks. Alternatively, you can use the CloudWatch API, AWS SDK, AWS CLI, or AWS CloudFormation to provision and configure Metric Streams. You can also use AWS  CloudFormation templates provided by third party service providers to setup Metric Streams to destinations outside AWS.  Metric Streams supports OpenTelemetry and JSON output formats. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eMetric Streams are now available in all commercial AWS Regions, excluding the AWS China (Beijing) Region and the AWS China (Ningxia) Region. To learn more about Metric Streams pricing, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudwatch/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon CloudWatch pricing page\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about Metric Streams, please refer to our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch-Metric-Streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-03T18:03:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/announcing-amazon-cloudwatch-metric-streams/","postDateTime":"2021-03-31T17:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing Amazon CloudWatch Metric Streams","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAnnouncing Amazon CloudWatch Metric Streams - a new feature that enables customers to create a continuous, near real-time stream of metrics to a destination of their choice. \u003cbr /\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cloudwatch","description":"general:products/amazon-cloudwatch","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#management-and-governance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"management-and-governance","description":"marketing:marchitecture/management-and-governance","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T19:30:55+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-03-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-python-with-apache-flink-v1-11","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-python-with-apache-flink-v1-11/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:43:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:12:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming applications built using Python version 3.7. This enables you to write streaming applications in the Python language and run them using Apache Flink v1.11 on Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics. Apache Flink v1.11 offers support for Python through the Table API, which is a unified, relational API for data processing.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams.  Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB Streams, Amazon S3, custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e and get started with Python examples \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/gs-python.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. You can learn more about what Flink 1.11\u0026nbsp;offers by visiting their official website.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics region availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp style\u003d\"text-align: center;\"\u003e\u003csub\u003eModified 9/27/2021 – In an effort to ensure a great experience, expired links in this post have been updated or removed from the original post.\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-28T00:43:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/03/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-python-with-apache-flink-v1-11/","postDateTime":"2021-03-25T17:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports Python with Apache Flink v1.11","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming applications built using Python version 3.7. This enables you to write streaming applications in the Python language and run them using Apache Flink v1.11 on Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics. Apache Flink v1.11 offers support for Python through the Table API, which is a unified, relational API for data processing.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2021-01-amazon-sns-adds-support-for-message-archiving-and-analytics-via-kineses-data-firehose-subscriptions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/01/amazon-sns-adds-support-for-message-archiving-and-analytics-via-kineses-data-firehose-subscriptions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:42:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:09:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/sns/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)\u003c/a\u003e to deliver messages to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e. This new subscription type for SNS enables message storage, analytics, and auditing by providing a simple way to send Amazon SNS messages to data lakes, data stores, and analytics services.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis integration makes it easier for customers using Amazon SNS to collect data for analytics and to keep records for backup or audit in applications such as e-commerce and banking. You can use Amazon SNS topics with Kinesis Data Firehose subscriptions to capture, transform, buffer, compress and upload data to Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service (Amazon ES), HTTP endpoints, and third party service providers such as Datadog, New Relic, MongoDB, and Splunk. With this feature, you can deliver Amazon SNS messages to these destinations without writing custom code.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt launch, Kinesis Data Firehose subscriptions for Amazon SNS are available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/sns.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e22 AWS Regions\u003c/a\u003e. You can subscribe a Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to an Amazon SNS standard topic by using the AWS Software Development Kit (SDK), AWS Command Line Interface (CLI), AWS Management Console, or AWS CloudFormation.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about delivering Amazon SNS messages to Kinesis Data Firehose, see the following:\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/compute/introducing-message-archiving-and-analytics-for-amazon-sns/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eIntroducing message archiving and analytics for Amazon SNS blog post\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/sns/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon SNS product page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-firehose-as-subscriber.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon SNS developer guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/sns/pricing/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon SNS pricing page\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n\u003cul\u003e\r\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/sns/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon SNS console\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\r\n\u003c/ul\u003e\r\n","modifiedDate":"2021-09-03T18:07:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2021/01/amazon-sns-adds-support-for-message-archiving-and-analytics-via-kineses-data-firehose-subscriptions/","postDateTime":"2021-01-12T11:34:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon SNS adds support for message archiving and analytics via Kinesis Data Firehose subscriptions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/sns.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Simple Notification Service (SNS)\u003c/a\u003e to deliver messages to \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e. This new subscription type for SNS enables message storage, analytics, and auditing by providing a simple way to send Amazon SNS messages to data lakes, data stores, and analytics services.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2021","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2021","description":"year#2021","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:24:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-sns","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-sns","description":"general:products/amazon-sns","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:04+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-apache-flink","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-apache-flink/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:34:18+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now build and run streaming applications using Apache Flink version 1.11 in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e. Apache Flink v1.11 provides improvements to the Table and SQL API, which is a unified, relational API for stream and batch processing and acts as a superset of the SQL language specially designed for working with Apache Flink. Apache Flink v1.11 capabilities also include an improved memory model and RocksDB optimizations for increased application stability, and support for task manager stack traces in the Apache Flink Dashboard.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this launch, Kinesis Data Analytics supports JDK 11 and Scala 2.12, with support for Python coming soon. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams Amazon S3, custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink in our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. You can learn more about what Flink 1.11\u0026nbsp;offers by visiting the official website.\u003cbr\u003e\r\n\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics region availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2021-12-14T22:00:15Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-apache-flink/","postDateTime":"2020-11-20T10:48:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports Apache Flink v1.11","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now build and run streaming applications using Apache Flink version 1.11 in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e. Apache Flink v1.11 provides improvements to the Table and SQL API, which is a unified, relational API for stream and batch processing and acts as a superset of the SQL language specially designed for working with Apache Flink. Apache Flink v1.11 capabilities also include an improved memory model and RocksDB optimizations for increased application stability, and support for task manager stack traces in the Apache Flink Dashboard.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-the-apache-flink-dashboard","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-the-apache-flink-dashboard/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:12:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now provides access to the Apache Flink Dashboard, giving you greater visibility into your applications and advanced monitoring capabilities. You can now view your Apache Flink application’s environment variables, over 120 metrics, logs, and the directed acyclic graph (DAG) of the Apache Flink application in a simple, contextualized user interface.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can access the Apache Flink dashboard via a browser by clicking on the ‘Apache Flink Dashboard’ button on the Kinesis Data Analytics console or by calling the service’s new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/apiv2/API_CreateApplicationPresignedUrl.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eCreateApplicationPresignedURL API\u003c/a\u003e. The dashboard is enabled by default for all Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink applications and includes data on Apache Flink job performance and critical application health such as watermarks, checkpoints, and backpressure.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams.  Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB Streams, Amazon S3, custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink in our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/how-dashboard.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics region availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNote: The Flink Dashboard feature is available in all regions except Europe (Milan), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), and Middle East (Bahrain). Support for these three regions is coming soon.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-20T16:26:08Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-the-apache-flink-dashboard/","postDateTime":"2020-11-19T12:56:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports the Apache Flink Dashboard","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;now provides access to the Apache Flink Dashboard, giving you greater visibility into your applications and advanced monitoring capabilities. You can now view your Apache Flink application’s environment variables, over 120 metrics, logs, and the directed acyclic graph (DAG) of the Apache Flink application in a simple, contextualized user interface.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-sdk-in-c-supports-client-metrics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-sdk-in-c-supports-client-metrics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:15:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e adds client metrics support to its WebRTC SDK in C. Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC enables developers to build web, mobile, and IoT devices application for real-time media and data streaming. Developers can use this capability to build applications for use cases such as home security and monitoring, camera-enabled doorbells, baby and pet monitoring, smart appliances, and more. Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC SDK in C enables IoT devices to securely connect with Kinesis Video Streams for peer discovery and media streaming. The client metrics allows developers to monitor and track performance of the applications built using the WebRTC SDK in C. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC client metrics include metrics for WebRTC signaling and multiple \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.w3.org/TR/webrtc-stats/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eW3C standards\u003c/a\u003e compliant metrics for networking, media, and data streaming. Developers can use simple APIs to obtain various metrics to monitor application behaviors such as connectivity states, connection latencies, and statistics for media or data streaming. For example, developers can monitor media streaming quality by tracking the data packet loss as percentage of data packets exchanged for an outbound stream in a specific duration. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams support for WebRTC, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/what-is-kvswebrtc.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about the client metrics included in Amazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC SDK in C and for examples, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/kvswebrtc-reference.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-13T20:07:45Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-webrtc-sdk-in-c-supports-client-metrics/","postDateTime":"2020-11-13T12:27:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC SDK in C now supports client metrics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e adds client metrics support to its WebRTC SDK in C. Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC enables developers to build web, mobile, and IoT devices application for real-time media and data streaming. Developers can use this capability to build applications for use cases such as home security and monitoring, camera-enabled doorbells, baby and pet monitoring, smart appliances, and more. Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC SDK in C enables IoT devices to securely connect with Kinesis Video Streams for peer discovery and media streaming. The client metrics allows developers to monitor and track performance of the applications built using the WebRTC SDK in C. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#media-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"media-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/media-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-11-amazon-kinesis-data-streams-enables-data-stream-retention","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-enables-data-stream-retention/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:12:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:48:51+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now store streaming data for up to one year in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e. Long term retention of streaming data enables you to use the same platform for both real-time and older data retained in Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. For example, you can train machine learning algorithms for financial trading, marketing personalization, and recommendation models without moving the data into a different data store or writing a new application. You can also satisfy certain data retention regulations, including under HIPAA and FedRAMP, using long term retention. You only pay for data stored and retrieved without provisioning additional storage or compute resources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams is a massively scalable and durable real-time data streaming service. It can continuously capture gigabytes of data per second from hundreds of thousands of sources like website clickstreams, IoT data, database event streams, financial transactions, social media feeds, IT logs, and location-tracking events. The data collected is available in milliseconds for real-time analytics use cases like dashboards, anomaly detection, dynamic pricing, and more. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, refer to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/kinesis-extended-retention.html\"\u003eChanging the Data Retention Period\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Data Streams Developer Guide and visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/pricing/\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e. Long term retention of data is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-11-04T23:44:12Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/11/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-enables-data-stream-retention/","postDateTime":"2020-11-04T10:45:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams enables data stream retention up to one year","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now store streaming data for up to one year in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e. Long term retention of streaming data enables you to use the same platform for both real-time and older data retained in Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. For example, you can train machine learning algorithms for financial trading, marketing personalization, and recommendation models without moving the data into a different data store or writing a new application. You can also satisfy certain data retention regulations, including under HIPAA and FedRAMP, using long term retention. You only pay for data stored and retrieved without provisioning additional storage or compute resources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-10-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-the-us-west-california-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-the-us-west-california-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:21:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the US West (California) AWS region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams, Amazon S3, custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors. You can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink and for SQL applications \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-10-21T21:22:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-the-us-west-california-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2020-10-21T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in the US West (California) AWS region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the US West (California) AWS region.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-10-kinesis-client-library-enables-multi-stream-processing","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/kinesis-client-library-enables-multi-stream-processing/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:14:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now process multiple Amazon Kinesis data streams with a single \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-client\"\u003eKinesis Client Library\u003c/a\u003e (KCL) based consumer application. Previously, each KCL based application processes a single Kinesis data stream. With this new capability,  you can update the list of streams at runtime for multi-stream processing in a scalable KCL application without redeploying the application. This reduces operational overhead  of maintaining multiple KCL applications.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKCL helps you quickly build custom stream consumer applications that you can run in either Amazon EC2 or containers on Amazon ECS or EKS. KCL enables you to focus on business logic while building applications. It handles complex issues such as adapting to changes in stream volume, load-balancing streaming data, coordinating distributed services, and processing data with fault-tolerance. You need to use the latest KCL version 2.3.1 to enable multi-stream processing with your KCL consumer application.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e is a massively scalable and durable real-time data streaming service. It can continuously capture gigabytes of data per second from hundreds of thousands of sources like website clickstreams, IoT data, database event streams, financial transactions, social media feeds, IT logs, and location-tracking events. The data collected is available in milliseconds for real-time analytics use cases like dashboards, anomaly detection, dynamic pricing, and more. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, refer to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/shared-throughput-kcl-consumers.html\"\u003eUsing Kinesis Client Library\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Data Streams Developer Guide. The latest KCL 2.3.1 release is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-10-20T19:00:57Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/kinesis-client-library-enables-multi-stream-processing/","postDateTime":"2020-10-20T09:28:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Kinesis Client Library now enables multi-stream processing ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now process multiple Amazon Kinesis data streams with a single \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-client\"\u003eKinesis Client Library\u003c/a\u003e (KCL) based consumer application. Previously, each KCL based application processes a single Kinesis data stream. With this new capability,  you can update the list of streams at runtime for multi-stream processing in a scalable KCL application without redeploying the application. This reduces operational overhead  of maintaining multiple KCL applications.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-10-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-supports-force-stop-and-new-autoscaling-status","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-supports-force-stop-and-new-autoscaling-status/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:04:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e now allows you to Force Stop a running application and reset its status to Ready, giving you more control over your applications. In addition, you can check if your application is scaling up or down through the new ‘Autoscaling\u0027 application status.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApplications can sometimes become unresponsive and stuck in a transient status such as creating, updating, or stopping. This is often due to misconfigurations that cause the application to become unhealthy. You can choose to Force Stop unresponsive applications on the console or by setting the force flag in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/apiv2/API_StopApplication.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eStopApplication\u003c/a\u003e API. A Force Stop will cease data processing and move the application to a Ready status without taking additional actions like saving application state. You can go to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/troubleshooting.html#troubleshooting\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTroubleshooting Guide\u003c/a\u003e for best practices to help you avoid and mitigate unresponsive applications. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new Autoscaling application status provides you with better visibility into when applications are being scaled up or down, if Autoscaling is enabled for your application. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams, Amazon S3, custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors. You can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink and for SQL applications \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Regional Services List\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-10-08T19:41:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-supports-force-stop-and-new-autoscaling-status/","postDateTime":"2020-10-08T12:40:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports Force Stop and a new Autoscaling status","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e now allows you to Force Stop a running application and reset its status to Ready, giving you more control over your applications. In addition, you can check if your application is scaling up or down through the new ‘Autoscaling\u0027 application status.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-10-apache-flink-kinesis-consumer-supports-efo-http-2-data-retrieval","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/apache-flink-kinesis-consumer-supports-efo-http-2-data-retrieval/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:06:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:16:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eApache Flink Kinesis Consumer now supports Enhanced Fan Out (EFO) and the HTTP/2 data retrieval API for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e. EFO allows Amazon Kinesis Data Streams consumers to scale by offering each consumer a dedicated read throughput up to 2MB/second. The HTTP/2 data retrieval API reduces latency of data delivery from producers to consumers to 70 milliseconds or better. In combination, these two features allow you to build low latency Apache Flink applications that utilize dedicated throughput from Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams.  Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams, Amazon S3, custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors. You can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started with the Apache Flink Kinesis Data Streams connector with EFO, see the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/software.amazon.kinesis/amazon-kinesis-connector-flink/1.0.0\"\u003eMaven Repository\u003c/a\u003e and the GitHub \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-connector-flink\"\u003erepository\u003c/a\u003e for Apache Flink version 1.8. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-10-07T22:17:40Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/apache-flink-kinesis-consumer-supports-efo-http-2-data-retrieval/","postDateTime":"2020-10-07T13:52:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Apache Flink Kinesis Consumer supports EFO and HTTP/2 data retrieval","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eApache Flink Kinesis Consumer now supports Enhanced Fan Out (EFO) and the HTTP/2 data retrieval API for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e. EFO allows Amazon Kinesis Data Streams consumers to scale by offering each consumer a dedicated read throughput up to 2MB/second. The HTTP/2 data retrieval API reduces latency of data delivery from producers to consumers to 70 milliseconds or better. In combination, these two features allow you to build low latency Apache Flink applications that utilize dedicated throughput from Amazon Kinesis Data Streams. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-10-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-java-is-now-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-apache-flink","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-java-is-now-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-apache-flink/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:19:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAWS has repositioned Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Java to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e to emphasize our continued support for Apache Flink. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics launched in 2016 as an easy way to analyze streaming data using SQL. When customers asked us to support additional languages, we built a new offering called Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Java that employed Apache Flink as a stream processing engine. Today, customers experience Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Java as an easy way to build and manage Apache Flink applications. Kinesis Data Analytics also now supports more languages provided by Apache Flink, including Scala, with more coming soon. We are now reflecting that experience in the updated name, Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink reduces the complexity of building, managing, and integrating Apache Flink applications with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon S3, and more. You can learn more in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics region availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-10-05T19:01:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/10/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-java-is-now-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-apache-flink/","postDateTime":"2020-10-05T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Java is now Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAWS has repositioned Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Java to \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e to emphasize our continued support for Apache Flink. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-09-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-available-europe-milan-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-available-europe-milan-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:03:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Europe (Milan) AWS region.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams, Amazon S3, custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors. You can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink and for SQL applications \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-09-16T20:24:04Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-available-europe-milan-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2020-09-16T13:46:11Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in the Europe (Milan) AWS region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Europe (Milan) AWS region.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-09-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-java-based-apache-beam-streaming-workloads","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-java-based-apache-beam-streaming-workloads/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:07:46+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming applications built using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://beam.apache.org/\"\u003eApache Beam\u003c/a\u003e Java SDK version 2.23. Apache Beam is an open-source, unified model for defining streaming and batch data processing applications that can be executed across multiple execution engines. This release allows you to build Apache Beam streaming applications in Java and run them using Apache Flink 1.8 on Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, Apache Spark running on-premises, and other execution engines supported by Apache.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams.  Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building and managing Apache Flink applications. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink integrates with Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK), Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon DynamoDB streams Amazon S3, custom integrations, and more using built-in connectors.  \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e and build your own Apache Beam pipeline through the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://streaming-analytics.workshop.aws/beam-on-kda/\"\u003eStreaming Analytics Workshop\u003c/a\u003e. You can learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://flink.apache.org/\"\u003eApache Flink\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://beam.apache.org/\"\u003eApache Beam\u003c/a\u003e by visiting their official website. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics region availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-09-17T21:23:09Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-java-based-apache-beam-streaming-workloads/","postDateTime":"2020-09-15T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports Java-based Apache Beam streaming workloads","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Apache Flink\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming applications built using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://beam.apache.org/\"\u003eApache Beam\u003c/a\u003e Java SDK version 2.23. Apache Beam is an open-source, unified model for defining streaming and batch data processing applications that can be executed across multiple execution engines. This release allows you to build Apache Beam streaming applications in Java and run them using Apache Flink 1.8 on Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, Apache Spark running on-premises, and other execution engines supported by Apache.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-09-introducing-aws-data-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/introducing-aws-data-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-kinesis/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:58:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:14:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/aws-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-kinesis/\"\u003eAWS Streaming Data Solution for Amazon Kinesis\u003c/a\u003e is an AWS Solutions Implementation that provides an automated configuration of the AWS services necessary to easily capture, store, process, and deliver streaming data. This solution helps you solve for several real-time streaming use cases like capturing high volume application logs, analyzing clickstream data, continuously delivering to a data lake to name a few. To provide flexibility to adapt to different use cases and business needs, this solution offers two deployment options. Developers can use this solution to test new service combinations as the basis for their production environment, or to improve an existing application they have already implemented.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDevelopers want to build a high performance, security compliant, and easy-to-manage streaming solution. This solution shortens your development time by reducing the need for you to: model and provision resources using AWS CloudFormation; set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms, dashboards, and logging; and manually implement streaming data best practices in AWS.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis solution provides two AWS CloudFormation templates, both of which use Amazon Kinesis Data Streams for streaming storage. One template uses Amazon API Gateway for ingestion and AWS Lambda as a consumer. The second template uses direct ingestion to Kinesis Data Streams from Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2), Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics as a consumer, and Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) as a storage destination. To learn more about AWS Data Streaming Solution for Amazon Kinesis, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/aws-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-kinesis/\"\u003eAWS Solutions Implementation webpage\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/aws-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-kinesis\"\u003eGitHub repository\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditional AWS Solutions are available on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/implementations/\"\u003eAWS Solutions Implementation\u003c/a\u003e webpage, where customers can browse solutions by product category or industry to find AWS-vetted, automated, turnkey reference implementations that address specific business needs.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-09-01T17:05:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/09/introducing-aws-data-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-kinesis/","postDateTime":"2020-09-01T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing AWS Data Streaming Data Solution for Amazon Kinesis","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/solutions/implementations/aws-streaming-data-solution-for-amazon-kinesis.html\"\u003eAWS Streaming Data Solution for Amazon Kinesis\u003c/a\u003e is an AWS Solutions Implementation that provides an automated configuration of the AWS services necessary to easily capture, store, process, and deliver streaming data. This solution helps you solve for several real-time streaming use cases like capturing high volume application logs, analyzing clickstream data, continuously delivering to a data lake to name a few. To provide flexibility to adapt to different use cases and business needs, this solution offers two deployment options. Developers can use this solution to test new service combinations as the basis for their production environment, or to improve an existing application they have already implemented.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-supports-data-delivery-mongodb-cloud","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-supports-data-delivery-mongodb-cloud/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:10:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:08:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.mongodb.com/cloud\"\u003eMongoDB Cloud\u003c/a\u003e. This feature enables you to use a fully managed service to stream data to MongoDB Cloud without building custom applications or worrying about operating and managing the data delivery infrastructure. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose incorporates error handling, auto-scaling, transformation, conversion, aggregation, and compression to help you accelerate the deployment of data streams across your organization.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores, and analytics services. It can capture, transform, and deliver streaming data to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, generic HTTP endpoints, and service providers like MongoDB. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMongoDB Cloud is a great way to build data-driven applications. The core of MongoDB Cloud is \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas/aws-mongodb\"\u003eMongoDB Atlas\u003c/a\u003e, an elastic cloud database with built-in Search and Data Lake services for powering diverse workloads through a common API. The streaming delivery from Kinesis Data Firehose to MongoDB is powered by \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.mongodb.com/realm/services/configure/service-webhooks/\"\u003eMongoDB Realm webhooks\u003c/a\u003e making it easier than ever to build robust, reactive data pipelines that stream directly into MongoDB collections, and enable real-time querying, enrichment, and analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e to configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and specify MongoDB Cloud as the destination. Once set, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose takes care of reliable, scalable delivery of your streaming data to MongoDB. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, read, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://developer.mongodb.com/how-to/Realm-AWS-Kinesis-Firehose-Destination\"\u003eUsing MongoDB Realm WebHooks with AWS Kinesis Data Firehose Delivery Streams\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information on MongoDB, refer to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.mongodb.com/\"\u003eMongoDB\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-29T22:23:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-supports-data-delivery-mongodb-cloud/","postDateTime":"2020-07-29T15:20:54Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now supports data delivery to MongoDB Cloud","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.mongodb.com/cloud\"\u003eMongoDB Cloud\u003c/a\u003e. This feature enables you to use a fully managed service to stream data to MongoDB Cloud without building custom applications or worrying about operating and managing the data delivery infrastructure. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose incorporates error handling, auto-scaling, transformation, conversion, aggregation, and compression to help you accelerate the deployment of data streams across your organization.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-07-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-milan-cape-town","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-milan-cape-town/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:12:38+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Europe (Milan) and Africa (Cape Town) AWS Regions. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose developer guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-07-21T15:46:31Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/07/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-milan-cape-town/","postDateTime":"2020-07-21T12:25:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in the Europe (Milan) and Africa (Cape Town) AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Europe (Milan) and Africa (Cape Town) AWS Regions. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-06-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-the-aws-china-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-the-aws-china-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:13+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:10:19+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet and the AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, you can build sophisticated streaming applications using Apache Flink or develop SQL queries using an interactive editor to transform and analyze data in real time. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics in the Developer Guide for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003eApache Flink Applications\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\"\u003eSQL\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-06-26T01:40:11Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-the-aws-china-region/","postDateTime":"2020-06-25T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in  the AWS China (Beijing) Region, Operated by Sinnet and the AWS China (Ningxia) Region, Operated by NWCD ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet and the AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-06-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-available-aws-govcloud-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-available-aws-govcloud-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:03:08+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to transform and analyze streaming data in real time with Apache Flink. Apache Flink is an open source framework and engine for processing data streams. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics reduces the complexity of building, managing, and integrating Apache Flink applications with other AWS services. You can learn about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics in the Developer Guide for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003eApache Flink\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\"\u003eSQL\u003c/a\u003e applications. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-06-30T16:58:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/06/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-available-aws-govcloud-regions/","postDateTime":"2020-06-24T11:34:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in AWS GovCloud (US) Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/govcloud-us.html\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-05-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-provides-enhanced-monitoring-for-apache-flink-applications","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-provides-enhanced-monitoring-for-apache-flink-applications/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:00:47+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e now provides enhanced monitoring for Apache Flink applications through new metrics sent to Amazon CloudWatch. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics emits 19 application metrics by default such as CPU and memory utilization. You can also easily create custom metrics in your application code using Apache Flink’s built-in metrics system. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers (leveraging Apache Flink) build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real time. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDeveloper Guide for Java Applications\u003c/a\u003e, and learn about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/monitoring-overview.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003elogging and metrics\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cb\u003eRecent announcements:\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-available-hong-kong-bahrain/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in Asia Pacific (Hong Kong) and Middle East (Bahrain)\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/access-resources-within-your-amazon-virtual-private-cloud-using-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAccess Resources within your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud using Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-apache-flink-18/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports Apache Flink 1.8\u003cbr\u003e\n \u003c/a\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/you-can-now-run-fully-managed-apache-flink-applications-with-apache-kafka/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eYou can now run fully managed Apache Flink applications with Apache Kafka\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-05-12T20:37:52Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/05/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-provides-enhanced-monitoring-for-apache-flink-applications/","postDateTime":"2020-05-12T10:17:56Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics now provides enhanced monitoring for Apache Flink applications","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e now provides enhanced monitoring for Apache Flink applications through new metrics sent to Amazon CloudWatch. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics emits 19 application metrics by default such as CPU and memory utilization. You can also easily create custom metrics in your application code using Apache Flink’s built-in metrics system. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-api-support-to-easily-retrieve-media-clips","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-api-support-to-easily-retrieve-media-clips/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:07:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:10:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e adds a new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_reader_GetClip.html\"\u003eGetClip API\u003c/a\u003e that makes it easy for developers to retrieve media stored in their Kinesis video streams. Developers can use the API to synchronously generate MP4 clips for offline playback, sharing playable clips, long term archival of interesting events, file based processing via Machine Learning applications, and other use cases.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDevelopers can use the GetClip API by providing the video stream name or its Amazon Resource Name (ARN) where the data is stored, and a time range of media to be included in the clip. The API will then synchronously package the selected media in MP4 format and return it through the API. The API supports video data in H.264 or H.265 encoding formats, and audio data in AAC or G.711 encoding formats. The GetClip API is available via the AWS SDKs for all supported languages.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, you pay only for what you use. See Amazon Kinesis Video Streams \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/pricing/\"\u003epricing\u003c/a\u003e for details.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams and the GetClip API, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/what-is-kinesis-video.html\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-29T20:00:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-api-support-to-easily-retrieve-media-clips/","postDateTime":"2020-04-29T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams adds API support to easily retrieve media clips ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e adds a new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_reader_GetClip.html\"\u003eGetClip API\u003c/a\u003e that makes it easy for developers to retrieve media stored in their Kinesis video streams. Developers can use the API to synchronously generate MP4 clips for offline playback, sharing playable clips, long term archival of interesting events, file based processing via Machine Learning applications, and other use cases.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-04-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-streaming-data-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service-in-amazon-vpc","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-streaming-data-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service-in-amazon-vpc/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:00:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e can now deliver streaming data to an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/elasticsearch-service/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elasticsearch Service\u003c/a\u003e domain in an Amazon VPC. You can now easily ingest, transform, and reliably deliver streaming data in to an Amazon Elasticsearch Service domain running in a VPC without building and managing your own data ingestion and delivery infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to reliably load streaming data into data lakes, data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools and dashboards you are already using today. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. It can also batch, compress, convert, and encrypt the data before loading it, minimizing the amount of storage used at the destination and increasing security.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Elasticsearch Service makes it easy for you to deploy, secure, and run Elasticsearch cost effectively at scale. You can build, monitor, and troubleshoot your applications using the tools you love, at the scale you need. The service provides support for open source Elasticsearch APIs, managed Kibana, integration with Logstash and other AWS services, and built-in alerting and SQL querying. With Amazon Elasticsearch Service, you get the ELK stack you need, without the operational overhead.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlacing an Amazon Elasticsearch Service domain within a VPC enables secure communication between Amazon Elasticsearch Service and other services within the VPC without the need for an internet gateway, NAT device, or VPN connection. Because of their logical isolation, domains that reside within a VPC have an extra layer of security when compared to domains that use public endpoints.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose and Amazon Elasticsearch Service availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-04-24T21:49:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/04/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-streaming-data-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service-in-amazon-vpc/","postDateTime":"2020-04-24T11:41:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds support for streaming data delivery to an Amazon Elasticsearch Service domain in an Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e can now deliver streaming data to an \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/elasticsearch-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Elasticsearch Service\u003c/a\u003e domain in an Amazon VPC. You can now easily ingest, transform, and reliably deliver streaming data in to an Amazon Elasticsearch Service domain running in a VPC without building and managing your own data ingestion and delivery infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elasticsearch-service","description":"general:products/amazon-elasticsearch-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-03-amazon-kinesis-data-streams-now-supports-scaling-up-to-10000-mbs-throughput-with-a-single-api-call","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-now-supports-scaling-up-to-10000-mbs-throughput-with-a-single-api-call/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:28:47+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can use the UpdateShardCount API in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e to scale up to 10,000 shards for a single data stream. You can use Amazon Kinesis Data Streams to capture, store, and analyze terabytes of data per hour from clickstreams, financial transactions, social media feeds, and more. The UpdateShardCount API enables you to rapidly scale the capacity of data streams up or down to handle changes in data volumes without any disruption to the producing or the consuming applications.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Kinesis shard provides 1 MB/s ingress and 2 MB/s egress throughput. You can increase stream throughput by adding more shards. Previously, the UpdateShardCount API could scale up to 500 shards. Today’s announcement enables you to rapidly scale your steam capacity up to 10,000 shards, a 20X increase. As an example, if you had 10 shards delivering 10 MB/s throughput, you could previously scale up to 500 shards to ingest 500 MB/s. Now, you can scale up to 10,000 shards or 10,000 MB/s in response to traffic increase with a single API call or a click in the console. You can then scale down capacity after a reduction in traffic. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdating the shard count is an asynchronous operation. Kinesis Data Streams performs splits or merges on individual shards to update the shard count. You can continue to read and write data to your stream while the scaling operation is in progress. We recommend using KPL version \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-producer\"\u003e0.14.0\u003c/a\u003e or higher, and upgrade KCL to version 1.9 or above for using this capability. Please refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/APIReference/API_UpdateShardCount.html\"\u003eAPI Reference documentation\u003c/a\u003e for more details.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe 10,000 shard increase for the UpdateShardCount API is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-03-23T16:57:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-now-supports-scaling-up-to-10000-mbs-throughput-with-a-single-api-call/","postDateTime":"2020-03-23T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams now supports scaling up to 10,000 MB/s throughput with a single API call","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, you can use the UpdateShardCount API in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e to scale up to 10,000 shards for a single data stream. You can use Amazon Kinesis Data Streams to capture, store, and analyze terabytes of data per hour from clickstreams, financial transactions, social media feeds, and more. The UpdateShardCount API enables you to rapidly scale the capacity of data streams up or down to handle changes in data volumes without any disruption to the producing or the consuming applications.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-03-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-aws-privatelink-in-govcloud-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-aws-privatelink-in-govcloud-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:00:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:11:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose through AWS PrivateLink in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e. AWS PrivateLink allows you to privately access services hosted on AWS in a highly available and scalable manner, without using public IPs and without requiring the traffic to traverse the internet. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose APIs are now available to use inside your VPC through AWS PrivateLink in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ecommercial Regions\u003c/a\u003e, China Regions, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/govcloud-us/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US)\u003c/a\u003e. For more information about this feature, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-03-11T20:08:40Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/03/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-now-supports-aws-privatelink-in-govcloud-regions/","postDateTime":"2020-03-11T12:02:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose now supports AWS PrivateLink in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose through AWS PrivateLink in the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/govcloud-us.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS GovCloud (US) Regions\u003c/a\u003e. AWS PrivateLink allows you to privately access services hosted on AWS in a highly available and scalable manner, without using public IPs and without requiring the traffic to traverse the internet. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose APIs are now available to use inside your VPC through AWS PrivateLink in the AWS GovCloud (US) Regions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-01-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-available-hong-kong-bahrain","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-available-hong-kong-bahrain/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T12:59:05+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in two additional AWS regions: Asia Pacific (Hong Kong) and Middle East (Bahrain). Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in seventeen AWS regions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers (leveraging Apache Flink) build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real time. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics in the Developer Guide for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSQL\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eJava Applications\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-01-15T21:20:34Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-available-hong-kong-bahrain/","postDateTime":"2020-01-15T12:40:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in Asia Pacific (Hong Kong) and Middle East (Bahrain)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in two additional AWS regions: Asia Pacific (Hong Kong) and Middle East (Bahrain). Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in seventeen AWS regions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2020-01-access-resources-within-your-amazon-virtual-private-cloud-using-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/access-resources-within-your-amazon-virtual-private-cloud-using-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:19:08+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now enable your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e for Java applications to access resources within your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC). This feature was \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/access-resources-within-your-amazon-virtual-private-cloud-using-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics/\"\u003epreviously announced\u003c/a\u003e in four regions on November 25th, 2019 and is now available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available. For a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers (leveraging Apache Flink) build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real time. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can configure your Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Java application to connect to private subnets in a VPC using the AWS Management Console or AWS SDKs. You add VPC connectivity to your application by configuring one to many security groups and subnet identifiers associated with the VPCs you want to access resources in. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics creates one or more elastic network interfaces in one of the subnets provided in the application’s VPC configuration.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn about accessing resources within a VPC in the Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide for Java Applications\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-01-10T19:01:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2020/01/access-resources-within-your-amazon-virtual-private-cloud-using-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics/","postDateTime":"2020-01-09T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Access Resources within your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud using Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now enable your \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e for Java applications to access resources within your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC). This feature was \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/access-resources-within-your-amazon-virtual-private-cloud-using-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics/\"\u003epreviously announced\u003c/a\u003e in four regions on November 25th, 2019 and is now available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available. For a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services.html\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2020","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2020","description":"year#2020","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-available-nine-more-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-available-nine-more-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:22:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:24:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e is now available in nine additional AWS regions: US East (Ohio), Canada (Central), South America (São Paulo), Europe (London), Europe (Paris), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), and Asia Pacific (Singapore).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from connected devices to AWS for real-time machine learning (ML), storage, playback, and batch-oriented processing and analytics. Kinesis Video Streams automatically provisions and elastically scales all the infrastructure needed to ingest streaming video data in real time from millions of devices. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access and playback your data through easy-to-use APIs. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams also supports real-time media streaming via WebRTC that enables developers to easily stream real-time two-way media for use cases like home security and monitoring, camera-enabled doorbells, baby and pet monitoring, camera-enabled vacuums, smart home automation, smart appliances, and more.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information on AWS regions and services, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, please see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/what-is-kinesis-video.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-19T19:01:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-available-nine-more-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-12-19T10:45:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is now available in nine more regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e is now available in nine additional AWS regions: US East (Ohio), Canada (Central), South America (São Paulo), Europe (London), Europe (Paris), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Hong Kong), and Asia Pacific (Singapore).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#media-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"media-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/media-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-two-additional-aws-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-two-additional-aws-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:12:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:28:22+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in two additional AWS regions: Canada (Central) and South America (Sao Paulo). Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in fifteen AWS regions. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers (leveraging Apache Flink) build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real time. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics in the Developer Guide for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\"\u003eSQL\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003eJava Applications\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-18T22:09:19Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-two-additional-aws-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-12-18T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in two additional AWS regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in two additional AWS regions: Canada (Central) and South America (Sao Paulo). Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in fifteen AWS regions. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-apache-flink-18","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-apache-flink-18/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:55:01+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now build and run streaming applications using Apache Flink 1.8 in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e. Apache Flink 1.8 capabilities include exactly once connectors for Amazon S3 and Apache Kafka, improvements to the Amazon Kinesis Data Streams connector, a new Amazon DynamoDB streams connector, eight new SQL functions, SQL pattern detection, improvements to recovery speed and memory usage, and more. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers (leveraging Apache Flink) build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real time. This release upgrades the Apache Flink runtime of Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics from 1.6 to 1.8. You can learn more about what is included in the Apache Flink releases in the release announcements for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://flink.apache.org/news/2019/04/09/release-1.8.0.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eApache Flink 1.8.0\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://flink.apache.org/news/2018/11/30/release-1.7.0.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eApache Flink 1.7.0\u003c/a\u003e. Apache Flink 1.8 supports prior Apache Flink versions described in the Compatibility Table in the Apache Flink \u003ca href\u003d\"https://ci.apache.org/projects/flink/flink-docs-stable/ops/upgrading.html#compatibility-table\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDeveloper Guide for Java Applications\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-17T22:02:05Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-apache-flink-18/","postDateTime":"2019-12-17T13:38:27Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports Apache Flink 1.8","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now build and run streaming applications using Apache Flink 1.8 in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e. Apache Flink 1.8 capabilities include exactly once connectors for Amazon S3 and Apache Kafka, improvements to the Amazon Kinesis Data Streams connector, a new Amazon DynamoDB streams connector, eight new SQL functions, SQL pattern detection, improvements to recovery speed and memory usage, and more. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-12-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-support-for-real-time-two-way-media-streaming-with-webrtc","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-support-for-real-time-two-way-media-streaming-with-webrtc/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:46:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e now supports real-time media streaming via WebRTC. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://webrtc.org/\"\u003eWebRTC\u003c/a\u003e is an open-source project that enables real-time communication between web browsers, mobile applications, and connected devices via simple APIs. Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC enables developers to build applications with real-time two-way media streaming and interactivity between applications and connected devices. Typical uses include interactive video and audio between a video  doorbell or baby monitor and your mobile phone, video chat, and  peer-to-peer media streaming\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDevelopers can use Amazon Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC to easily stream real-time two-way media for use cases like home security and monitoring, camera-enabled doorbells, baby and pet monitoring, smart appliances, and more. Kinesis Video Streams brings WebRTC capabilities to camera IoT device via hardware-platform specific SDKs, and can elastically scale to support millions of devices. As a fully-managed capability, customers do not have to build, operate, or scale any WebRTC related cloud infrastructure like signaling or media relay servers.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Video Streams includes a WebRTC signaling end-point for fast peer discovery and secure connection establishment. It includes managed Session Traversal Utilities for NAT (STUN) and Traversal Using Relays around NAT (TURN) end-points for real-time exchange of media between peers. It also includes a free open-source SDK that directly integrates with camera firmware to enable secure communication with Kinesis Video Streams end-points for peer discovery and media streaming. Finally, it provides client libraries for Android and iOS, and JavaScript that allow WebRTC standard compliant mobile and web players to securely discover and connect with a camera device for media streaming and two-way communication.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Video Streams, you pay only for what you use. See Amazon Kinesis Video Streams \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/pricing/\"\u003epricing\u003c/a\u003e for details.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams support for WebRTC, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/what-is-kvswebrtc.html\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-12-05T00:15:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/12/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-support-for-real-time-two-way-media-streaming-with-webrtc/","postDateTime":"2019-12-04T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams adds support for real-time two-way media streaming with WebRTC","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e now supports real-time media streaming via WebRTC. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://webrtc.org/\"\u003eWebRTC\u003c/a\u003e is an open-source project that enables real-time communication between web browsers, mobile applications, and connected devices via simple APIs. Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC enables developers to build applications with real-time two-way media streaming and interactivity between applications and connected devices. Typical uses include interactive video and audio between a video  doorbell or baby monitor and your mobile phone, video chat, and  peer-to-peer media streaming\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#media-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"media-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/media-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-customer-provided-keys-for-server-side-encryption","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-customer-provided-keys-for-server-side-encryption/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:53+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:28:09+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now provides additional protection of sensitive data through customer-provided keys for server-side encryption (SSE) of delivery streams. This feature is integrated with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kms/\"\u003eAWS Key Management Service\u003c/a\u003e (KMS), which allows you to centrally manage keys that protect Kinesis Data Firehose delivery streams along with keys that protect your other AWS resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen you ingest records to encrypted delivery streams, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose immediately encrypts your messages. The encryption takes place on the server, using a 256-bit AES-GCM algorithm and a customer master key (CMK) issued by AWS KMS. Kinesis Data Firehose now works with both customer-provided CMKs and AWS-provided CMKs. The records are stored in encrypted form in multiple availability zones (AZs), and decrypted only as they are delivered to destinations like \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/\"\u003eAmazon S3\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/elasticsearch-service/\"\u003eAmazon Elasticsearch Service\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/redshift/\"\u003eAmazon Redshift\u003c/a\u003e and Splunk. To learn more, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/security.html\"\u003eSecurity in Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis capability is now available in all AWS Regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eavailable\u003c/a\u003e. There are no additional Kinesis Data Firehose charges for using this capability. You are only charged for AWS KMS usage. For pricing details, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kms/pricing/\"\u003eAWS KMS pricing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-26T21:29:49Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-for-customer-provided-keys-for-server-side-encryption/","postDateTime":"2019-11-26T13:09:25Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose Adds Support For Customer-Provided Keys for Server-Side Encryption","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now provides additional protection of sensitive data through customer-provided keys for server-side encryption (SSE) of delivery streams. This feature is integrated with \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kms.html\"\u003eAWS Key Management Service\u003c/a\u003e (KMS), which allows you to centrally manage keys that protect Kinesis Data Firehose delivery streams along with keys that protect your other AWS resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-access-resources-within-your-amazon-virtual-private-cloud-using-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/access-resources-within-your-amazon-virtual-private-cloud-using-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:43:53+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now enable your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e for Java applications to access resources within your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC). This feature enables you to use your streaming applications to read and write data from resources within your VPCs like Amazon Elasticsearch Service clusters, Amazon RDS databases, Amazon Redshift data warehouses, Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) clusters, and more. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers (leveraging Apache Flink) build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real time.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can configure your Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Java application to connect to private subnets in a VPC using the AWS Management Console or AWS SDKs. You add VPC connectivity to your application by configuring one to many security groups and subnet identifiers associated with the VPCs you want to access resources in. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics creates one or more elastic network  interfaces in one of the subnets provided in the application’s VPC  configuration. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. This capability is available in US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), EU (Frankfurt), and EU (Ireland). The capability is coming soon in all other regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn about accessing resources within a VPC in the Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide for Java Applications\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2020-01-07T20:39:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/access-resources-within-your-amazon-virtual-private-cloud-using-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics/","postDateTime":"2019-11-25T14:32:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Access resources within your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud using Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now enable your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e for Java applications to access resources within your Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (Amazon VPC). This feature enables you to use your streaming applications to read and write data from resources within your VPCs like Amazon Elasticsearch Service clusters, Amazon RDS databases, Amazon Redshift data warehouses, Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) clusters, and more. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-vpc","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-vpc","description":"general:products/amazon-vpc","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#networking-and-content-delivery","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"networking-and-content-delivery","description":"marketing:marchitecture/networking-and-content-delivery","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:17+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-you-can-now-run-fully-managed-apache-flink-applications-with-apache-kafka","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/you-can-now-run-fully-managed-apache-flink-applications-with-apache-kafka/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:38+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:27:38+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now run Apache Flink and Apache Kafka together using fully managed services on AWS. AWS provides a fully managed service for Apache Flink through \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e, enabling you to quickly build and easily run sophisticated streaming applications. You can use these fully managed Apache Flink applications to process streaming data stored in Apache Kafka running within Amazon VPC or on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/msk/\"\u003eAmazon MSK\u003c/a\u003e, a fully managed, highly available, and secure Apache Kafka service. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApache Flink is a distributed framework and engine for processing data streams. With Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, developers use Apache Flink to build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real time.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApache Kafka is an open-source platform for building real-time streaming data pipelines and applications. With Amazon MSK, you can use Apache Kafka APIs to populate data lakes, stream changes to and from databases, and power machine learning and analytics applications.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started building your first application, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/msk/home?ad\u003dc\u0026amp;cp\u003dbn\u0026amp;p\u003dmsk\u0026amp;region\u003dus-east-1#/home\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e to easily attach a streaming application to your Amazon MSK cluster. You can learn how to build an Apache Flink application that integrate with Amazon MSK in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon MSK and Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics are available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. This integration is available in US East (N. Virginia) and EU (Ireland). The integration is coming soon in all other regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-26T03:17:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/you-can-now-run-fully-managed-apache-flink-applications-with-apache-kafka/","postDateTime":"2019-11-25T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"You can now run fully managed Apache Flink applications with Apache Kafka","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now run Apache Flink and Apache Kafka together using fully managed services on AWS. AWS provides a fully managed service for Apache Flink through \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e, enabling you to quickly build and easily run sophisticated streaming applications. You can use these fully managed Apache Flink applications to process streaming data stored in Apache Kafka running within Amazon VPC or on \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/msk.html\"\u003eAmazon MSK\u003c/a\u003e, a fully managed, highly available, and secure Apache Kafka service. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-msk","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-msk","description":"general:products/amazon-msk","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-11-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-middle-east-bahrain-aws-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-middle-east-bahrain-aws-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:30:17+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Middle East (Bahrain) AWS Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-11-07T19:04:16Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/11/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-middle-east-bahrain-aws-region/","postDateTime":"2019-11-07T13:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in the Middle East (Bahrain) AWS Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the Middle East (Bahrain) AWS Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-amazon-api-gateway-now-supports-access-logging-to-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-api-gateway-now-supports-access-logging-to-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:49:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now configure Amazon API Gateway to send API access logs to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.  It\u0027s easy to configure Kinesis Data Firehose as a log destination by enabling access logging on an API and specifying the Firehose stream.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChoosing Kinesis Data Firehose as a destination for access logs allows customers to analyze API access patterns in real time and quickly troubleshoot issues using Amazon services like Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, or using 3rd-party tools like Splunk.  For example, using Kinesis Data Firehose integration with S3 allows customers to create Amazon Quicksight dashboards to visualize live API log data.  Customers can also use Splunk\u0027s integration with Kinesis Data Firehose to continuously monitor, diagnose, and resolve issues.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAPI Gateway’s support for Kinesis Data Firehose access logging is generally available in all regions where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/rande.html#fh_region\"\u003eKinesis Data Firehose is available\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more, refer to the API Gateway \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-logging-to-kinesis.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-16T17:50:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-api-gateway-now-supports-access-logging-to-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","postDateTime":"2019-10-16T12:07:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon API Gateway now supports access logging to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCustomers can now configure Amazon API Gateway to send API access logs to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.  It\u0027s easy to configure Kinesis Data Firehose as a log destination by enabling access logging on an API and specifying the Firehose stream.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-data-stream-delivery-amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-data-stream-delivery-amazon-elasticsearch-service/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:05:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:26:16+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service version 7.x clusters for near real-time data analysis and visualization. Kinesis Data Firehose automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and handles all of the underlying stream management.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-09T22:46:05Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-support-data-stream-delivery-amazon-elasticsearch-service/","postDateTime":"2019-10-09T09:57:01Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds support for data stream delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service 7.x clusters","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports streaming data delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service version 7.x clusters for near real-time data analysis and visualization. Kinesis Data Firehose automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and handles all of the underlying stream management.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-10-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-cross-account-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-cross-account-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:04:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:29:47+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service across accounts. Now your delivery stream and your Elasticsearch clusters can reside in different accounts. This makes it easier for Amazon Elasticsearch Service customers with multiple accounts to ingest streaming data and analyze it in near real time.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. You can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you would need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-08T20:49:45Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/10/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-adds-cross-account-delivery-to-amazon-elasticsearch-service/","postDateTime":"2019-10-08T14:42:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose adds cross-account delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e now supports delivery to Amazon Elasticsearch Service across accounts. Now your delivery stream and your Elasticsearch clusters can reside in different accounts. This makes it easier for Amazon Elasticsearch Service customers with multiple accounts to ingest streaming data and analyze it in near real time.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#applications","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"applications","description":"marketing:marchitecture/applications","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elasticsearch-service","description":"general:products/amazon-elasticsearch-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#application-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"application-services","description":"marketing:marchitecture/application-services","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-08-amazon-kinesis-data-streams-changes-license-for-its-producer-library-to-apache-license2","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/08/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-changes-license-for-its-producer-library-to-apache-license2/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:29:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams has changed the license of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-producer\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Producer Library\u003c/a\u003e from the Amazon Software License to Apache License 2.0. This change allows you to easily build and integrate the Amazon Kinesis Producer Library with other Apache software projects such as Apache Flink and Apache Spark.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e is a massively scalable and durable real-time data streaming service. The Amazon Kinesis Producer Library makes it simple to achieve high write throughput to a Kinesis data stream.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn more about in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/developing-producers-with-kpl.html\"\u003eDeveloping Producers Using the Amazon Kinesis Producer Library\u003c/a\u003e section of the Developer Guide.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:02:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/08/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-changes-license-for-its-producer-library-to-apache-license2/","postDateTime":"2019-08-15T15:37:42Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams Changes License for its Producer Library to Apache License 2.0","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams has changed the license of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-producer\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Producer Library\u003c/a\u003e from the Amazon Software License to Apache License 2.0. This change allows you to easily build and integrate the Amazon Kinesis Producer Library with other Apache software projects such as Apache Flink and Apache Spark.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-08-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-available-mumbai-paris-stockholm-aws-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/08/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-available-mumbai-paris-stockholm-aws-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:03:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:40:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is now available in thirteen AWS regions with the addition of Asia Pacific (Mumbai), EU (Paris), and EU (Stockholm). \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers (leveraging Apache Flink) build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real time.  \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn about Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics in the Developer Guide for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\"\u003eSQL\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003eJava Applications\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:02:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/08/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-available-mumbai-paris-stockholm-aws-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-08-14T15:46:48Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is Now Available in Asia Pacific (Mumbai), EU (Paris), and EU (Stockholm) AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is now available in thirteen AWS regions with the addition of Asia Pacific (Mumbai), EU (Paris), and EU (Stockholm). \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-08-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-announces-full-unicode-support","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/08/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-announces-full-unicode-support/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:25:27+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use the full Unicode standard (UTF-8) in your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e SQL applications. This new feature enables you to build real-time applications using the full breadth of languages and characters supported by the Unicode standard. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real time. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFull Unicode support is now supported in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS regions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn about this feature and more in the Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Developer Guide for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\"\u003eSQL\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\"\u003eJava Applications\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:59Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/08/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-announces-full-unicode-support/","postDateTime":"2019-08-13T15:19:07Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Announces Full Unicode Support","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use the full Unicode standard (UTF-8) in your \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e SQL applications. This new feature enables you to build real-time applications using the full breadth of languages and characters supported by the Unicode standard. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-07-aws-iot-events-supports-invoking-actions-to-lambda-sqs-kinesis-firehose-iot-events","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/aws-iot-events-supports-invoking-actions-to-lambda-sqs-kinesis-firehose-iot-events/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:10:52+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWhen using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/iot-events/\"\u003eAWS IoT Events\u003c/a\u003e, you now have the option to define actions to invoke AWS Lambda functions, publish messages to the Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS) queue or an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream, and republish messages to IoT Events. Previously, you could only define actions to publish messages to SNS and MQTT. These expanded actions make it easier to build monitoring applications that help you quickly understand the state of your devices by providing more options to process messages created by IoT Events.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can define a Lambda action to invoke a specific Lambda function with the message payload. The Lambda function receives the message payload as an input parameter and can further process the information in the message. Similarly, you can define an SQS action to send the message payload to a SQS queue that other services could read from. You can send the message payload to a Firehose delivery stream to display alerts in applications such as real-time dashboards. Finally, by defining IoT Events as an action, you send the message payload as an input to another detector model which can help simplify complex detector models into a hierarchy of simple ones. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e These new actions are available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eall regions where AWS IoT Events\u003c/a\u003e is available. To get started, open the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/iotevents\"\u003eIoT Events console\u003c/a\u003e and select a state for a detector model. Add an event to the state, and select from the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/iotevents/latest/developerguide/iotevents-with-others.html\"\u003elist of available actions\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:42Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/07/aws-iot-events-supports-invoking-actions-to-lambda-sqs-kinesis-firehose-iot-events/","postDateTime":"2019-07-25T15:44:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"AWS IoT Events actions now support AWS Lambda, SQS, Kinesis Firehose, and IoT Events as targets","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWhen using \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/iot-events.html\"\u003eAWS IoT Events\u003c/a\u003e, you now have the option to define actions to invoke AWS Lambda functions, publish messages to the Amazon Simple Queue Service (SQS) queue or an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream, and republish messages to IoT Events. Previously, you could only define actions to publish messages to SNS and MQTT. These expanded actions make it easier to build monitoring applications that help you quickly understand the state of your devices by providing more options to process messages created by IoT Events.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-iot","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-iot","description":"general:products/aws-iot","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:20+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-lambda","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-lambda","description":"general:products/aws-lambda","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T20:18:23+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-iot-events","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-iot-events","description":"general:products/aws-iot-events","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:58:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:58:31+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-sqs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-sqs","description":"general:products/amazon-sqs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:05+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-06-new-digital-course-now-available-data-analytics-fundamentals","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/new-digital-course-now-available-data-analytics-fundamentals/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:12:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:14:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eData Analytics Fundamentals\u003c/i\u003e, which replaces the digital training course \u003ci\u003eBig Data Technology Fundamentals\u003c/i\u003e, will teach you the latest on how to seamlessly plan a data analysis solution using the suite of AWS services. In this 3.5-hour, self-paced digital course, you will understand the big picture of data analysis, how to plan data analysis solutions, as well as the data analytic processes involved in those solutions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou will learn how to use various AWS services (Amazon S3, Amazon Kinesis, Amazon EMR, AWS Glue, and Amazon Redshift) to collect, process, analyze and present data. You will complete the course with an appreciation of the basic architectures, value propositions, and potential use cases to help build and enhance data analysis solutions. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.aws.training/learningobject/wbc?id\u003d35364\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eEnroll today\u003c/a\u003e!\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/new-digital-course-now-available-data-analytics-fundamentals/","postDateTime":"2019-06-27T10:33:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"New Digital Training Course Now Available: Data Analytics Fundamentals","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eData Analytics Fundamentals\u003c/i\u003e, which replaces the digital training course \u003ci\u003eBig Data Technology Fundamentals\u003c/i\u003e, will teach you the latest on how to seamlessly plan a data analysis solution using the suite of AWS services. In this 3.5-hour, self-paced digital course, you will understand the big picture of data analysis, how to plan data analysis solutions, as well as the data analytic processes involved in those solutions.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-emr","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-emr","description":"general:products/amazon-emr","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-glue","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-glue","description":"general:products/aws-glue","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:46+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#training-and-certification","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"training-and-certification","description":"marketing:marchitecture/training-and-certification","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:02+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"databases","description":"marketing:marchitecture/databases","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:00:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-06-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-in-aws-govcloud-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-in-aws-govcloud-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:26+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:40:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-East)  Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you would need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:01:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/06/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-available-in-aws-govcloud-region/","postDateTime":"2019-06-27T08:20:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in the AWS GovCloud (US-East) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-East)  Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"analytics","description":"marketing:marchitecture/analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-05-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-europe-stockholm-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon_kinesis_data_firehose_is_now_available_in_the_aws_europe_stockholm_region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:24:08+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS Europe (Stockholm) Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, you would need an AWS account. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e For Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:50Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon_kinesis_data_firehose_is_now_available_in_the_aws_europe_stockholm_region/","postDateTime":"2019-05-15T14:11:22Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in the AWS Europe (Stockholm) region ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS Europe (Stockholm) Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-05-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-allows-you-to-assign-aws-resource-tags-to-your-real-time-applications","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon_kinesis_data_analytics_now_allows_you_to_assign_aws_resource_tags_to_your_real_time_applications/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:36+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:23:03+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now assign AWS resource tags to applications in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e. Each tag consists of a key and an optional value, both of which you define. You can use tags in Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics to easily organize and identify your resources, create cost allocation reports, and control access to resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers (leveraging Apache Flink) build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real-time. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS resource tags are now supported by Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics in all \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eregions where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn more about this feature by visiting the Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Developer Guide for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSQL\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eJava Applications\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:46Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon_kinesis_data_analytics_now_allows_you_to_assign_aws_resource_tags_to_your_real_time_applications/","postDateTime":"2019-05-08T09:13:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics now allows you to assign AWS resource tags to your real-time applications","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now assign AWS resource tags to applications in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e. Each tag consists of a key and an optional value, both of which you define. You can use tags in Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics to easily organize and identify your resources, create cost allocation reports, and control access to resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-05-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-asia-pacific-seoul-asia-pacific-singapore-asia-pacific-sydney-asia-pacific-tokyo-and-eu-london","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon_kinesis_data_analytics_is_now_available_in_asia_pacific_seoul_asia_pacific_singapore_asia_pacific_sydney_asia_pacific_tokyo_and_eu_london/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:46+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:20:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in five additional AWS regions including Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and EU (London). Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in ten AWS regions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers (leveraging Apache Flink) build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real-time. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of where Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:46Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/05/amazon_kinesis_data_analytics_is_now_available_in_asia_pacific_seoul_asia_pacific_singapore_asia_pacific_sydney_asia_pacific_tokyo_and_eu_london/","postDateTime":"2019-05-08T08:46:16Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and EU (London)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now available in five additional AWS regions including Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and EU (London). Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in ten AWS regions. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-04-amazon-kinesis-data-streams-changes-license-for-its-consumer-library-to-apache-license-2-0","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/04/amazon_kinesis_data_streams_changes_license_for_its_consumer_library_to_apache_license_2_0/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:22:41+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e is a massively scalable and durable real-time data streaming service.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams has changed the license of the Amazon Kinesis Client Library from the Amazon Software License to Apache License 2.0. This change allows you to easily build and integrate the Amazon Kinesis Client Library with other Apache software projects such as Apache Flink and Apache Spark.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Kinesis Client Library helps you consume and process data from a Kinesis data stream. You can learn more about the Amazon Kinesis Client Library in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/shared-fan-out-consumers.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDeveloping Amazon Kinesis Data Streams Consumers\u003c/a\u003e section of the Developer Guide.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:16Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/04/amazon_kinesis_data_streams_changes_license_for_its_consumer_library_to_apache_license_2_0/","postDateTime":"2019-04-24T17:01:59Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams changes license for its consumer library to Apache License 2.0","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e is a massively scalable and durable real-time data streaming service.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-04-expanding-aws-privatelink-support-for-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/04/expanding_aws_privatelink_support_for_amazon_kinesis_data_firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:01:15+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:19:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;can now utilize \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e to securely ingest data.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e provides private connectivity between VPCs, AWS services, and on-premises applications, securely over the Amazon network. When \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e is used with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, all traffic to a Kinesis Data Firehose from a VPC flows over a private connection. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information go to the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;page or read the techncial\u0026nbsp; documentation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/vpc.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis capability is now available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eall regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:14Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/04/expanding_aws_privatelink_support_for_amazon_kinesis_data_firehose/","postDateTime":"2019-04-16T04:51:21Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Expanding AWS PrivateLink support for Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;can now utilize \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/privatelink.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e to securely ingest data.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-03-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-supports-aws-cloudtrail-logging","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/03/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-supports-aws-cloudtrail-logging/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:13:32+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now integrated with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudtrail/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CloudTrail\u003c/a\u003e. AWS CloudTrail captures changes made to your Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics applications and delivers the log files to an Amazon S3 bucket you specify.\u0026nbsp;Customers can now get visibility into their Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics application modifications including creation, deletion, and updates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. With Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real-time. AWS CloudTrail is a service that enables governance, compliance, operational auditing, and risk auditing of your AWS account. With AWS CloudTrail, you can log, continuously monitor, and retain account activity related to actions across your AWS infrastructure.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn more about this feature by visiting the Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Developer Guide for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSQL\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/java/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eJava Applications\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS CloudTrail support for Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eall regions where Kinesis Data Analytics is available\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:36Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/03/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-supports-aws-cloudtrail-logging/","postDateTime":"2019-03-22T09:33:29Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Supports AWS CloudTrail Logging","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is now integrated with \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cloudtrail.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CloudTrail\u003c/a\u003e. AWS CloudTrail captures changes made to your Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics applications and delivers the log files to an Amazon S3 bucket you specify.\u0026nbsp;Customers can now get visibility into their Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics application modifications including creation, deletion, and updates.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-cloudtrail","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-cloudtrail","description":"general:products/aws-cloudtrail","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:12+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-03-tag-on-create-and-tag-based-iam-application-for-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/03/tag-on-create-and-tag-based-iam-application-for-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:11:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eTag-on create is now available for Kinesis Data Firehose. Upon creation, you can tag your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e from the AWS Management Console or using the AWS APIs. By tagging resources at the time of creation you can eliminate the need to run custom tagging scripts after resource creation. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn addition, you can now set IAM policies on your Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose during creation using tags. This enables automated policy application to give you more granular control over who has access to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose APIs. You can also enforce the use of tagging and can control which tag keys and values are set on your resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVisit the AWS User Documentation\u0026nbsp;to learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/firehose-tagging.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003etag-on create\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/controlling-access.html#tag-based-access-control\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003etag-based IAM application\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese capabilities are available at no additional cost in all AWS commercial \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eregions\u003c/a\u003e where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T05:00:27Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/03/tag-on-create-and-tag-based-iam-application-for-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose/","postDateTime":"2019-03-11T11:11:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Tag-on Create and Tag-Based IAM Application for Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eTag-on create is now available for Kinesis Data Firehose. Upon creation, you can tag your \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e from the AWS Management Console or using the AWS APIs. By tagging resources at the time of creation you can eliminate the need to run custom tagging scripts after resource creation. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-02-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-synchronized-audio-video-playback-and-mpeg-ts-container-format-support-via-http-live-streaming-hls","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-synchronized-audio-video-playback-and-mpeg-ts-container-format-support-via-http-live-streaming-hls/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:09:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-03-12T22:10:46+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e enables developers to use its fully-managed HLS capability for synchronized audio video (AV) playback and also output HLS streams in MPEG-TS container format. Developers can now ingest both audio and video in a single multi-track Kinesis Video stream and use HLS APIs to deliver pre-segmented files and playlists in fragmented MP4 (fMP4) and MPEG-TS container formats for playback on compatible mobile and web players.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs an increasing number of camera-enabled devices now include a microphone, developers want to ingest both audio and video data in a Kinesis Video stream and build player applications for synchronized AV playback. Developers can now enable this capability by ingesting both video (H.264) and audio (AAC) in a single multi-track Kinesis Video stream. As the media is ingested, developers can then use KVS HLS APIs to playback the ingested media in both live and on-demand mode. Kinesis Video Streams now also allows developers to deliver media in both fMP4 and MPEG-TS as the HLS output container, increasing compatibility with earlier generation platforms such as iOS9.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producersdk-cpp-write.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproducer integration guide\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/getting-started.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about ingesting audio and video data in a single Kinesis Video stream. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for regional availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:47Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-adds-synchronized-audio-video-playback-and-mpeg-ts-container-format-support-via-http-live-streaming-hls/","postDateTime":"2019-02-22T16:48:15Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams adds Synchronized Audio Video Playback and MPEG-TS Container Format Support via HTTP Live Streaming (HLS)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e enables developers to use its fully-managed HLS capability for synchronized audio video (AV) playback and also output HLS streams in MPEG-TS container format. Developers can now ingest both audio and video in a single multi-track Kinesis Video stream and use HLS APIs to deliver pre-segmented files and playlists in fragmented MP4 (fMP4) and MPEG-TS container formats for playback on compatible mobile and web players.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-02-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-java-now-supports-aws-cloudformation","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-java-now-supports-aws-cloudformation/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:09:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:16:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudformation/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CloudFormation\u003c/a\u003e templates to model and provision \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e for Java applications using version 2 of the Kinesis Data Analytics API. This improvement enables you to use AWS CloudFormation to deploy Kinesis Data Analytics applications in a safe and repeatable manner. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real-time. With Kinesis Data Analytics, SQL users and Java developers build streaming applications to transform and analyze data in real-time. AWS CloudFormation provides a common language for you to describe and provision all the infrastructure resources in your cloud environment. You can now use AWS CloudFormation to provision Java applications in Kinesis Data Analytics.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS CloudFormation support for Kinesis Data Analytics for Java is available now, in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eall regions where Kinesis Data Analytics for Java is available\u003c/a\u003e. You can learn more \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-resource-kinesisanalyticsv2-application.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. \u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-for-java-now-supports-aws-cloudformation/","postDateTime":"2019-02-19T15:14:31Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for Java Now Supports AWS CloudFormation","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cloudformation.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS CloudFormation\u003c/a\u003e templates to model and provision \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e for Java applications using version 2 of the Kinesis Data Analytics API. This improvement enables you to use AWS CloudFormation to deploy Kinesis Data Analytics applications in a safe and repeatable manner. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-02-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-support-for-custom-amazon-s3-prefixes","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-support-for-custom-amazon-s3-prefixes/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:17:19+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e today announced support for custom Amazon S3 prefixes allowing customers more flexibility when configuring S3 paths for data delivery.\u0026nbsp;This new capability enables customers to simplify and accelerate ETL (Extract Transform Load) workflows and to enable data partitions for faster query performance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow customers can customize the Amazon S3 prefix using the Apache Hive format and timestamp formats (supported by the Java DateTimeFormatter class). \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started with Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/02/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-support-for-custom-amazon-s3-prefixes/","postDateTime":"2019-02-12T12:14:22Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose Announces Support for Custom Amazon S3 Prefixes","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e today announced support for custom Amazon S3 prefixes allowing customers more flexibility when configuring S3 paths for data delivery.\u0026nbsp;This new capability enables customers to simplify and accelerate ETL (Extract Transform Load) workflows and to enable data partitions for faster query performance.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-west-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-west-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:18:48+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region, an isolated AWS Region designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for customers who have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  To get started, create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose Console\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-govcloud-us-west-region/","postDateTime":"2019-01-16T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS GovCloud (US-West) Region, an isolated AWS Region designed to host sensitive data and regulated workloads in the cloud for customers who have U.S. federal, state, and local government compliance requirements. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-govcloud-us","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-govcloud-us","description":"general:products/aws-govcloud-us","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T18:41:18+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-china-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-china-regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:06:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:23:37+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet, and AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3 and Amazon Elasticsearch Service, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  With Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, you don\u0027t need to write applications or manage resources. You configure your data producers to send data to Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and it automatically delivers the data to the destination that you specified. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to transform your data before delivering it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  To get started, you would need an AWS (China) account. You can request an AWS (China) account by completing \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.amazonaws.cn/en/sign-up/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ethis form\u003c/a\u003e. Once you have an account, you can create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://console.amazonaws.cn/kinesis/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Console\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.amazonaws.cn/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  For Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose availability, refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:57Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-the-aws-china-regions/","postDateTime":"2019-01-16T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in the AWS China (Beijing) Region, Operated by Sinnet, and the AWS China (Ningxia) Region, Operated by NWCD","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is now available in the AWS China (Beijing) Region, operated by Sinnet, and AWS China (Ningxia) Region, operated by NWCD. Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3 and Amazon Elasticsearch Service, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-kinesis-data-streams-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:00+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:23:57+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  AWS will use commercially reasonable efforts to make Amazon Kinesis Data Streams available with a Monthly Uptime Percentage, during any monthly billing cycle, of at least 99.9% (the “Service Commitment”). In the event Amazon Kinesis Data Streams does not meet the Service Commitment, you will be eligible to receive a Service Credit as described in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/sla/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams Service Level Agreement\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  This SLA is now available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is available. For more information on availability, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-streams-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","postDateTime":"2019-01-14T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams Announces 99.9% Service Level Agreement","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:08:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:08:27+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  AWS will use commercially reasonable efforts to make Amazon Kinesis Video Streams available with a Monthly Uptime Percentage, during any monthly billing cycle, of at least 99.9% (the “Service Commitment”). In the event Amazon Kinesis Video Streams does not meet the Service Commitment, you will be eligible to receive a Service Credit as described in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/sla/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams Service Level Agreement\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  This SLA is now available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Video Streams is available. For more information on availability, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","postDateTime":"2019-01-14T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Announces 99.9% Service Level Agreement","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2019-01-amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:02:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:18:11+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  AWS will use commercially reasonable efforts to make Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose available with a Monthly Uptime Percentage, during any monthly billing cycle, of at least 99.9% (the “Service Commitment”). In the event Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose does not meet the Service Commitment, you will be eligible to receive a Service Credit as described in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/sla/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose Service Level Agreement\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  This SLA is now available in all regions where Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is available. For more information on availability, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e. Please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:59:55Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2019/01/amazon-kinesis-data-firehose-announces-99-9-service-level-agreement/","postDateTime":"2019-01-14T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose Announces 99.9% Service Level Agreement","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  AWS has published a service level agreement (SLA) for \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, which provides availability guarantees for Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2019","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2019","description":"year#2019","dateCreated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-06T18:17:49+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-java-based-stream-processing-applications","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-java-based-stream-processing-applications/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:34:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:59:16+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports Java-based stream processing applications, in addition to the previously supported SQL. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. Now, you can use your own Java code in Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics to continuously transform and load your data lake, generate metrics to feed real-time gaming leaderboards, apply machine-learning models to data streams from connected devices, and more.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can now use \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e to build and run sophisticated Java applications that process streaming data. You build your application with the IDE of your choice using open source Java libraries based on Apache Flink, an open source framework and engine for processing data streams, and AWS SDKs. The extensible libraries include more than 25 pre-built stream processing operators like window and aggregate, and AWS service integrations like Amazon Kinesis Data Streams and Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose. Once built, Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics takes care of everything required to run your real-time applications continuously and scales automatically to match the volume and throughput of your incoming data.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSupport for Java applications in Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in 4 AWS Regions: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland).\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:48Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-java-based-stream-processing-applications/","postDateTime":"2018-11-27T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Now Supports Java-based Stream Processing Applications","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports Java-based stream processing applications, in addition to the previously supported SQL. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to analyze streaming data, gain actionable insights, and respond to your business and customer needs in real time. Now, you can use your own Java code in Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics to continuously transform and load your data lake, generate metrics to feed real-time gaming leaderboards, apply machine-learning models to data streams from connected devices, and more.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-analyze-live-video-at-scale-in-real-time-using-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-and-amazon-sagemaker","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/analyze-live-video-at-scale-in-real-time-using-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-and-amazon-sagemaker/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-03-12T22:08:54+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now analyze live video at scale in real time using the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Inference Template (KIT) for Amazon SageMaker. The KIT enables you to build scalable, real-time, ML-driven video analytics pipelines without using other libraries or writing custom software. You can attach Kinesis video streams to Amazon SageMaker endpoints in minutes and quickly deploy your machine learning algorithms to analyze live video feeds on the AWS Cloud.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe KIT contains the Kinesis Video Consumer Library software packaged as a Docker container and an AWS CloudFormation template that automates the deployment of all required AWS resources. The KIT also comes with a step-by-step example of integrating Amazon Kinesis Video Streams to Amazon SageMaker.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e makes it easy to securely stream audio, video, and related metadata from connected devices to AWS for analytics, machine learning (ML), playback, and other processing. \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/sagemaker.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon SageMaker\u003c/a\u003e is the managed platform for developers and data scientists to build, train, and deploy ML models quickly and easily.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Inference Template, refer to our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/examples-sagemaker.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:31Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/analyze-live-video-at-scale-in-real-time-using-amazon-kinesis-video-streams-and-amazon-sagemaker/","postDateTime":"2018-11-20T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Analyze live video at scale in real-time using Amazon Kinesis Video Streams and Amazon SageMaker","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now analyze live video at scale in real time using the Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Inference Template (KIT) for Amazon SageMaker. The KIT enables you to build scalable, real-time, ML-driven video analytics pipelines without using other libraries or writing custom software. You can attach Kinesis video streams to Amazon SageMaker endpoints in minutes and quickly deploy your machine learning algorithms to analyze live video feeds on the AWS Cloud.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-the-aws-us-east-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-the-aws-us-east-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:36:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:11:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in the AWS US East (Ohio) Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to process streaming data in real time with standard SQL without having to learn new programming languages or processing frameworks. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics enables you to query streaming data or build entire streaming applications using SQL, so that you can gain actionable insights and respond to your business and customer needs promptly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/getting-started/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eget started\u003c/a\u003e, create an Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics application in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management console\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the addition of this region, Kinesis Data Analytics is now  available in 5 AWS Regions globally: US East (N. Virginia), US East  (Ohio), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland), and EU (Frankfurt).\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:19Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-the-aws-us-east-region/","postDateTime":"2018-11-07T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in the AWS US East (Ohio) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in the AWS US East (Ohio) Region. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to process streaming data in real time with standard SQL without having to learn new programming languages or processing frameworks. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics enables you to query streaming data or build entire streaming applications using SQL, so that you can gain actionable insights and respond to your business and customer needs promptly.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-11-stream-data-from-microsoft-windows-based-services-using-the-amazon-kinesis-agent-for-microsoft-windows","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/stream-data-from-microsoft-windows-based-services-using-the-amazon-kinesis-agent-for-microsoft-windows/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:33:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:05:39+0000","additionalFields":{"modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:58:16Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/11/stream-data-from-microsoft-windows-based-services-using-the-amazon-kinesis-agent-for-microsoft-windows/","postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use the Amazon Kinesis Agent for Microsoft Windows to stream data from Microsoft Windows based services into AWS for monitoring, analysis, and visualization. For example, Amazon Kinesis Agent for Microsoft Windows can stream logs, events, and metrics from Microsoft services such as Exchange and DHCP, or from your own services deployed on Windows to AWS services. You can then detect service failures, performance issues, security issues, etc. and automatically take action to resolve the issues. With Amazon Kinesis Agent for Microsoft Windows you have in-depth visibility into the health of your deployed services throughout your operational environment.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Agent for Microsoft Windows is a highly configurable and extensible agent. It runs on Microsoft Windows laptops, desktop computers, and servers, either on-premises or in the AWS Cloud. It can parse, filter, decorate, and transform events, logs, and metrics en route to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose, and Amazon CloudWatch for real-time or near real-time processing. It eliminates cloud-based log processing by parsing and transforming logs into standard formats such as JSON. The visualization and business intelligence tools in the data pipeline can then immediately consume these formats.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Agent for Microsoft Windows is free to use and is available now on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/kinesis-agent-windows\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGitHub\u003c/a\u003e. Visit the AWS \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis-agent-windows/latest/userguide/what-is-kinesis-agent-windows.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003euser documentation\u003c/a\u003e to learn more about the Amazon Kinesis Agent for Microsoft Windows \u003c/p\u003e\n","postDateTime":"2018-11-06T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Stream data from Microsoft Windows based services using the Amazon Kinesis Agent for Microsoft Windows"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-10-kinesis-video-streams-fragment-level-metadata-support","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/kinesis-video-streams-fragment-level-metadata-support/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:07:02+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e now enables you to easily add metadata to and retrieve from individual fragments in a Kinesis Video stream to build richer applications in the AWS cloud. For example, you can now send GPS values as metadata with each video fragment from an on-person camera, or send temperature values with videos fragments from a baby monitor, and then use both the metadata and video fragments in your consuming applications to create richer user experiences.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA fragment represents a segment of video, audio, or other time-encoded data. Metadata in Kinesis Video Streams is a mutable key-value pair that can be used to describe the content of the fragment, embed associated sensor readings, or any other custom data that needs to be transferred along with the actual fragment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFragment-level metadata gives you granular control over passing and processing additional information with each video fragment. The metadata is stored along with the video fragment for the entire duration of the stream\u0027s retention period. You can use it to embed GPS or temperature sensor values to video fragments that your consuming application can then use for creating meaningful correlations, or you can use it to mark exactly those video fragments that contain motion detected by your edge device, like a camera. Your deep-learning cloud application can then use this metadata to inform the next stage of processing such as identifying faces or objects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour stream producing application or device can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKinesis Video Producer SDK\u003c/a\u003e to add metadata to a video fragment. Your consuming application can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/parser-library.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKinesis Video Stream Parser Library\u003c/a\u003e to easily retrieve the metadata for each fragment via the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_dataplane_GetMedia.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetMedia\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_reader_GetMediaForFragmentList.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetMediaForFragmentList\u003c/a\u003e API operations for further processing. To learn more, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/how-meta.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:57Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/10/kinesis-video-streams-fragment-level-metadata-support/","postDateTime":"2018-10-04T13:26:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams now supports adding and retrieving Metadata at Fragment-Level","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e now enables you to easily add metadata to and retrieve from individual fragments in a Kinesis Video stream to build richer applications in the AWS cloud. For example, you can now send GPS values as metadata with each video fragment from an on-person camera, or send temperature values with videos fragments from a baby monitor, and then use both the metadata and video fragments in your consuming applications to create richer user experiences.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA fragment represents a segment of video, audio, or other time-encoded data. Metadata in Kinesis Video Streams is a mutable key-value pair that can be used to describe the content of the fragment, embed associated sensor readings, or any other custom data that needs to be transferred along with the actual fragment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFragment-level metadata gives you granular control over passing and processing additional information with each video fragment. The metadata is stored along with the video fragment for the entire duration of the stream\u0027s retention period. You can use it to embed GPS or temperature sensor values to video fragments that your consuming application can then use for creating meaningful correlations, or you can use it to mark exactly those video fragments that contain motion detected by your edge device, like a camera. Your deep-learning cloud application can then use this metadata to inform the next stage of processing such as identifying faces or objects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour stream producing application or device can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKinesis Video Producer SDK\u003c/a\u003e to add metadata to a video fragment. Your consuming application can use the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/parser-library.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKinesis Video Stream Parser Library\u003c/a\u003e to easily retrieve the metadata for each fragment via the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_dataplane_GetMedia.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetMedia\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/API_reader_GetMediaForFragmentList.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGetMediaForFragmentList\u003c/a\u003e API operations for further processing. To learn more, please see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/how-meta.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRefer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-09-new-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-capability-for-time-series-analytics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/09/new-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-capability-for-time-series-analytics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:27:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:05:05+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use a new capability for continuously aggregating data over time, stagger windows, in your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e applications. Stagger windows enable you to emit timely and accurate SQL results in the face of late data.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStreaming data is processed seconds after the data is created, and network disruptions and latency can cause some events to have their processing delayed. When performing real-time analytics, data that arrives after an initial result is generated is called late data. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics can be configured to produce a delta or an update to the initial result if data arrives late. The new stagger windows capability allows you to control whether you want more timely results with more updates or less timely results with fewer to no updates, giving you the flexibility to choose what is best for your use case.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can learn more about \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/stagger-window-concepts.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003estagger windows\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Developer Guide.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available in the US (Northern Virginia), US (Oregon), EU (Ireland), and EU (Frankfurt) AWS regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/09/new-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-capability-for-time-series-analytics/","postDateTime":"2018-09-05T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"New Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics capability for time-series analytics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now use a new capability for continuously aggregating data over time, stagger windows, in your \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e applications. Stagger windows enable you to emit timely and accurate SQL results in the face of late data.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-08-kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-windows","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-windows/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:55:13+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e Producer SDK is now available for Microsoft Windows to help you stream video into AWS from sources such as webcams, USB cameras, or RTSP (network) cameras connected to your Microsoft Windows machine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from millions of connected devices to AWS for real-time machine learning (ML), storage, and batch-oriented processing and analytics. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access your data through easy-to-use APIs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis Video Streams provides Producer SDKs in C++ and Java that you can build, configure, and install on devices. This software makes it easier to securely and reliably stream video into AWS frame-by-frame in real-time. In addition to Mac OS, Android, Linux, and Raspbian, the C++ Producer SDK is now also available for Microsoft Windows. Developers can use the Minimal GNU for Windows (MinGW) or the Microsoft Visual Studio C++ Compiler (MSVC) to build the producer SDK from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-cpp\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003esource\u003c/a\u003e and start streaming from cameras connected to a Microsoft Windows machine. Additionally, we have also packaged the Producer SDK GStreamer Plug-in for Windows as a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/examples-gstreamer-plugin.html#examples-gstreamer-plugin-docker-download\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDocker image\u003c/a\u003e so you can simply do a Docker pull and get started with streaming video in minutes. Please refer the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk-win.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e to learn more. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-windows/","postDateTime":"2018-08-31T19:02:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams Producer SDK Is Now Available For Microsoft Windows","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e Producer SDK is now available for Microsoft Windows to help you stream video into AWS from sources such as webcams, USB cameras, or RTSP (network) cameras connected to your Microsoft Windows machine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from millions of connected devices to AWS for real-time machine learning (ML), storage, and batch-oriented processing and analytics. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access your data through easy-to-use APIs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis Video Streams provides Producer SDKs in C++ and Java that you can build, configure, and install on devices. This software makes it easier to securely and reliably stream video into AWS frame-by-frame in real-time. In addition to Mac OS, Android, Linux, and Raspbian, the C++ Producer SDK is now also available for Microsoft Windows. Developers can use the Minimal GNU for Windows (MinGW) or the Microsoft Visual Studio C++ Compiler (MSVC) to build the producer SDK from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-cpp\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003esource\u003c/a\u003e and start streaming from cameras connected to a Microsoft Windows machine. Additionally, we have also packaged the Producer SDK GStreamer Plug-in for Windows as a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/examples-gstreamer-plugin.html#examples-gstreamer-plugin-docker-download\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDocker image\u003c/a\u003e so you can simply do a Docker pull and get started with streaming video in minutes. Please refer the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk-win.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper documentation\u003c/a\u003e to learn more. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Refer to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS global region table\u003c/a\u003e for Amazon Kinesis Video Streams availability.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-08-stream-data-65-faster-with-5x-higher-fan-out-using-new-kinesis-data-streams-features","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/stream_data_65_faster_with_5x_higher_fan_out_using_new_kinesis_data_streams_features/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:39:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:54:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe are announcing two new Amazon Kinesis Data Streams features that boost the performance of your Kinesis Data Streams applications: a new HTTP/2 data retrieval API and enhanced fan-out.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe new enhanced fan-out feature provides logical pipes with up to 2MB/sec of throughput between one or more consumers and shards, allowing customers to scale the number of consumers reading from a stream in parallel while maintaining performance. The new HTTP/2 data retrieval API, called SubscribeToShard, improves the data delivery speed between producers and multiple consumers by more than 65%. Using this new API, data is typically delivered from producers to multiple consumers using enhanced fan-out within 70 milliseconds. Together, these features allow customers to run multiple high performance, low-latency streaming applications on a single Kinesis data stream.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the US East (N. Virginia) AWS Region, enhanced fan-out usage costs $0.015 per consumer-shard hour and $0.013 per GB of data retrieved from a data stream. These features are available in all AWS regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe are also launching Kinesis Client Library (KCL) version 2.0 to make it easy for customers to use the new HTTP/2 SubscribeToShard API and enhanced fan-out. Follow the step-by-step guidance within the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/introduction.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS user documentation\u003c/a\u003e to upgrade existing KCL applications to version 2.0. Visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e page to learn more about the HTTP/2 SubscribeToShard API and enhanced fan-out.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:25Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/08/stream_data_65_faster_with_5x_higher_fan_out_using_new_kinesis_data_streams_features/","postDateTime":"2018-08-02T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Stream data 65% faster with 5x higher fan-out using new Kinesis Data Streams features","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe are announcing two new Amazon Kinesis Data Streams features that boost the performance of your Kinesis Data Streams applications: a new HTTP/2 data retrieval API and enhanced fan-out.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-expanding-aws-privatelink-support-for-amazon-kinesis-data-streams","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/expanding_aws_privatelink_support_for_amazon_kinesis_data_streams/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:58:40+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eData streaming applications can now utilize \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-streams/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e in US West (N. California), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Canada (Central), EU (Frankfurt), EU (London), and South America (Sao Paulo) AWS Regions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS PrivateLink provides private connectivity between VPCs, AWS services, and on-premises applications, securely over the Amazon network. When AWS PrivateLink is used with Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, all traffic between a Kinesis Data Stream and clients within a VPC flows over a private connection. Visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/privatelink/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e page for more information.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/expanding_aws_privatelink_support_for_amazon_kinesis_data_streams/","postDateTime":"2018-07-31T12:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Expanding AWS PrivateLink support for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eData streaming applications can now utilize \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/privatelink.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS PrivateLink\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-streams.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Streams\u003c/a\u003e in US West (N. California), Asia Pacific (Seoul), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Canada (Central), EU (Frankfurt), EU (London), and South America (Sao Paulo) AWS Regions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-vpc","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-vpc","description":"general:products/amazon-vpc","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-is-now-available-in-eu-frankfurt","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon_kinesis_data_analytics_is_now_available_in_eu_frankfurt/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:27:55+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in the EU (Frankfurt) AWS Region. With the addition of this region, Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in 4 AWS Regions globally: US (Northern Virginia), US (Oregon), EU (Ireland), and EU (Frankfurt).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to process streaming data in real time with standard SQL without having to learn new programming\u0026nbsp; languages or processing frameworks. Kinesis Data Analytics enables you to query streaming data or build entire streaming applications using SQL, so that you can gain actionable insights and respond to your business and customer needs promptly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/getting-started/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTo get started\u003c/a\u003e, create an application in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management console\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Kinesis Data Analytics \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/what-is.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:12Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon_kinesis_data_analytics_is_now_available_in_eu_frankfurt/","postDateTime":"2018-07-18T13:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in EU (Frankfurt)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in the EU (Frankfurt) AWS Region. With the addition of this region, Kinesis Data Analytics is now available in 4 AWS Regions globally: US (Northern Virginia), US (Oregon), EU (Ireland), and EU (Frankfurt).\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-07-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-now-supports-configuring-data-enrichment-from-the-aws-management-console","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon_kinesis_data_analytics_now_supports_configuring_data_enrichment_from_the_aws_management_console/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:27:41+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:51:53+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now configure your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e applications to enrich a source data stream with an Amazon S3 object in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA reference data source is static data that your streaming application uses to enrich data coming in from streaming sources. You store reference data as an object in your S3 bucket. You can use this new console feature to add, edit, or view reference data used to enrich an input data stream. For example, you can add character metadata to streaming game events, system information to log files, and much more.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to process streaming data in real time with standard SQL without having to learn new programming languages or processing frameworks. Kinesis Data Analytics enables you to query streaming data or build entire streaming applications using SQL, so that you can gain actionable insights and respond to your business and customer needs promptly. Kinesis Data Analytics is available in US (Northern Virginia), US (Oregon), and EU (Ireland).\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:10Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/07/amazon_kinesis_data_analytics_now_supports_configuring_data_enrichment_from_the_aws_management_console/","postDateTime":"2018-07-13T11:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics now supports configuring data enrichment from the AWS Management Console","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now configure your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e applications to enrich a source data stream with an Amazon S3 object in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-06-kinesis-data-firehose-is-now-available-in-four-additional-aws-regions","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/kinesis_data_firehose_is_now_available_in_four_additional_aws_regions/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:02:44+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in EU (London), EU (Paris), Asia Pacific (Mumbai), and South America (Sao Paulo). With the addition of these four regions, Kinesis Data Firehose is available in 15 regions globally: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), US West (N. California), Canada (Central), South America (Sao Paulo), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), EU (London), EU (Paris), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Seoul), and Asia Pacific (Mumbai).\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, create a delivery stream in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://signin.aws.amazon.com/signin?redirect_uri\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fconsole.aws.amazon.com%2Ffirehose%2Fhome%3Fstate%3DhashArgs%2523%252Fwizard%252FnameAndSource%26isauthcode%3Dtrue\u0026amp;client_id\u003darn%3Aaws%3Aiam%3A%3A015428540659%3Auser%2Ffirehose\u0026amp;forceMobileApp\u003d0\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e or explore the Kinesis Data Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:57:00Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/kinesis_data_firehose_is_now_available_in_four_additional_aws_regions/","postDateTime":"2018-06-27T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Kinesis Data Firehose is Now Available in Four Additional AWS Regions","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. It can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-06-kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-gstreamer-plugin-and-docker-images","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/Kinesis_Video_Streams_Producer_SDK_Gstreamer_Plugin_and_Docker_Images/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:26:37+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:26:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/video-streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e Producer SDK is now available as a Gstreamer-plugin, and as Docker-images for Ubuntu, MacOS, and Raspberry Pi devices to help you stream video into AWS in minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams makes it easy to securely stream video from connected devices to AWS for real-time machine learning (ML), storage, and batch-oriented processing and analytics. Kinesis Video Streams automatically provisions and elastically scales all the infrastructure needed to ingest streaming video data in real-time from millions of devices. It also durably stores, encrypts, and indexes video data in your streams, and allows you to access your data through easy-to-use APIs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams provides Producer SDKs in C++ and Java that you can build, configure, and install on devices. This software makes it easier to securely and reliably stream video into AWS frame-by-frame in real-time. The Kinesis Video Producer SDK in C++ is now also available as a GStreamer-plugin. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://gstreamer.freedesktop.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGStreamer\u003c/a\u003e is a widely used, open source framework that provides a standard managed environment for constructing media-data flows from the device (camera or other video source) for further processing, rendering, or storage. Developers can use the Kinesis Video Producer GStreamer plugin to simplify their device-side application integration as they can take advantage of existing codecs and filter technology already available within GStreamer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDevelopers can build the individual Kinesis Video Producer and GStreamer components from sources available \u003ca href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-video-streams-producer-sdk-cpp\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e, and fully customize their media pipeline for streaming into Kinesis Video. Additionally, we have also packaged the components as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams/latest/dg/producer-sdk-cpp-gstreamer-docker.html\"\u003eDocker images\u003c/a\u003e for Ubuntu, MacOS, and Raspberry Pi devices. You can simply do a Docker pull and get started with streaming video in minutes.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/Kinesis_Video_Streams_Producer_SDK_Gstreamer_Plugin_and_Docker_Images/","postDateTime":"2018-06-20T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Kinesis Video Streams Producer SDK Gstreamer Plugin and Docker Images","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/video-streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Video Streams\u003c/a\u003e Producer SDK is now available as a Gstreamer-plugin, and as Docker-images for Ubuntu, MacOS, and Raspberry Pi devices to help you stream video into AWS in minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-video-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-video-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-video-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:40+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-06-kinesis-data-firehose-now-available-in-canada-central-and-asia-pacific-seoul","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/Kinesis_Data_Firehose_now_Available_in_Canada_Central_and_Asia_Pacific_Seoul/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:46:50+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. We are excited to announce the availability of Kinesis Data Firehose in Canada (Central) and Asia Pacific (Seoul) regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the addition of these two regions, Kinesis Data Firehose is now available in eleven regions globally: US East (N. Virginia), US East (Ohio), US West (Oregon), US West (N. California), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Sydney), Asia Pacific (Seoul), and Canada (Central).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Data Firehose can capture, transform, and load streaming data into Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, and Splunk, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools you are already using today. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home?region\u003dus-east-1\"\u003eKinesis management console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:52Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/06/Kinesis_Data_Firehose_now_Available_in_Canada_Central_and_Asia_Pacific_Seoul/","postDateTime":"2018-06-13T12:05:03Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose is now Available in Canada (Central) and Asia Pacific (Seoul)","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to load streaming data into data stores and analytics tools. We are excited to announce the availability of Kinesis Data Firehose in Canada (Central) and Asia Pacific (Seoul) regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-05-introducing-real-time-iot-device-monitoring-with-kinesis-data-analytics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/introducing-real-time-iot-device-monitoring-with-kinesis-data-analytics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:51:57+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/answers/iot/real-time-iot-device-monitoring-with-kinesis/\"\u003eReal-Time IoT Device Monitoring with Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is a solution that can help you more easily monitor your IoT device connectivity and activity in real-time. This solution automatically provisions the services necessary to record and visualize device connectivity and activity metrics for your IoT devices. Real-Time IoT Device Monitoring with Kinesis Data Analytics is designed to provide a framework for visualizing metrics in real-time, allowing you to focus on adding new metrics rather than underlying infrastructure operations. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor customers without a method to record and visualize IoT device metrics, this solution can provide valuable insight that can help you make better-informed decisions that increase the reliability, availability, and performance of your IoT devices.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe solution deploys an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/iot/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS IoT\u003c/a\u003e rule that sends device data to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, which archives the data in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/s3/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon S3\u003c/a\u003e and sends it to an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e application that computes metrics in real-time. The solution uses \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/dynamodb/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAmazon DynamoDB\u003c/a\u003e to durably store the computed data. The solution also features a customizable dashboard that visualizes your device connectivity and activity metrics in real-time. For pricing details, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/pricing/services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003epricing webpage\u003c/a\u003e for each AWS service you will be using in this solution. To learn more about Real-Time IoT Device Monitoring with Kinesis Data Analytics, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/answers/iot/real-time-iot-device-monitoring-with-kinesis/\"\u003esolution webpage\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe AWS Solutions team communicates AWS architectural best practices and develops standardized, automated solutions for the platform. Our offerings currently live on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/answers/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Answers webpage\u003c/a\u003e, where customers can browse common questions by category to find answers in the form of succinct Solution Briefs or comprehensive Solutions, which are AWS-vetted, automated, turnkey reference implementations that address specific business needs.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:34Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/introducing-real-time-iot-device-monitoring-with-kinesis-data-analytics/","postDateTime":"2018-05-11T08:27:07Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Real-Time IoT Device Monitoring with Kinesis Data Analytics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/answers/iot/real-time-iot-device-monitoring-with-kinesis.html\"\u003eReal-Time IoT Device Monitoring with Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is a solution that can help you more easily monitor your IoT device connectivity and activity in real-time. This solution automatically provisions the services necessary to record and visualize device connectivity and activity metrics for your IoT devices. Real-Time IoT Device Monitoring with Kinesis Data Analytics is designed to provide a framework for visualizing metrics in real-time, allowing you to focus on adding new metrics rather than underlying infrastructure operations. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-iot","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-iot","description":"general:products/aws-iot","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:52:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:52:20+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-05-stream-real-time-data-in-apache-parquet-or-orc-format-using-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/stream_real_time_data_in_apache_parquet_or_orc_format_using_firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:37:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:51:32+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe have added support for Apache Parquet and Apache ORC formats in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, so you can stream real-time data into Amazon S3 for cost-effective storage and analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApache Parquet and Apache ORC are columnar data formats that allow you to store and query data more efficiently and cost-effectively. You can now configure your Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to automatically convert data into Parquet or ORC format before delivering to your S3 bucket. There is no coding required, and you can query S3 data much faster using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/athena/\"\u003eAmazon Athena\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/redshift/spectrum/\"\u003eAmazon Redshift Spectrum\u003c/a\u003e, allowing you to save storage and query costs.\u0026nbsp;Usage based charges apply for data format conversion in Kinesis Data Firehose. For more information, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-firehose/pricing/\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS. To get started with Kinesis Data Firehose, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003econsole\u003c/a\u003e and the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a list of regions where Kinesis Data Firehose is available, see the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Region Table\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:37Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/stream_real_time_data_in_apache_parquet_or_orc_format_using_firehose/","postDateTime":"2018-05-10T17:51:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Stream Real-Time Data in Apache Parquet or ORC Format Using Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe have added support for Apache Parquet and Apache ORC formats in \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Firehose\u003c/a\u003e, so you can stream real-time data into Amazon S3 for cost-effective storage and analytics.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-simple-storage-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-simple-storage-service","description":"general:products/amazon-simple-storage-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:57:06+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:57:06+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-athena","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-athena","description":"general:products/amazon-athena","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-05-kinesis-data-analytics-application-monitoring-using-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/kinesis_data_analytics_application_monitoring_using_cloudwatch/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:26:00+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:54:20+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now monitor your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;application using the new Amazon CloudWatch KPU-usage metric, which shows you the number of Kinesis Processing Units (KPU) consumed by your application. KPU is a unit of stream processing capacity comprised of 4 GB memory, 1 vCPU compute, and corresponding networking capabilities. The KPU-usage metric makes it easier for you to monitor increases and decreases in your application’s resource usage as the service elastically scales the number of KPUs required to perform your analysis. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to process streaming data in real time with standard SQL without having to learn new programming languages or processing frameworks. Kinesis Data Analytics enables you to query streaming data or build entire streaming applications using SQL, so that you can gain actionable insights and respond to your business and customer needs promptly. To get started with Kinesis Data Analytics, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/getting-started/\"\u003egetting-started page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Data Analytics is available in US (Northern Virginia), US (Oregon), and EU (Ireland) AWS regions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/kinesis_data_analytics_application_monitoring_using_cloudwatch/","postDateTime":"2018-05-07T15:37:12Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Application Monitoring using Amazon CloudWatch","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now monitor your \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;application using the new Amazon CloudWatch KPU-usage metric, which shows you the number of Kinesis Processing Units (KPU) consumed by your application. KPU is a unit of stream processing capacity comprised of 4 GB memory, 1 vCPU compute, and corresponding networking capabilities. The KPU-usage metric makes it easier for you to monitor increases and decreases in your application’s resource usage as the service elastically scales the number of KPUs required to perform your analysis. \u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-05-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-increases-application-limits","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/amazon_kinesis_data_analytics_increases_application_limits/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:03:57+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe have increased the maximum row size allowed in Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics applications from 50KB to 512KB, so you can process and analyze streams with hundreds of columns.\u0026nbsp;We have also increased the maximum code size of Kinesis Data Analytics applications from 50KB to 100KB, allowing several hundreds of SQL statements in an application. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eKinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e is the easiest way to process streaming data in real time with standard SQL without having to learn new programming languages or processing frameworks. Kinesis Data Analytics enables you to query streaming data or build entire streaming applications using SQL, so that you can gain actionable insights and respond to your business and customer needs promptly. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics is available in US (Northern Virginia), US (Oregon), and EU (Ireland) AWS regions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:30Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/05/amazon_kinesis_data_analytics_increases_application_limits/","postDateTime":"2018-05-02T00:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics Increases Application Limits","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe have increased the maximum row size allowed in Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics applications from 50KB to 512KB, so you can process and analyze streams with hundreds of columns.\u0026nbsp;We have also increased the maximum code size of Kinesis Data Analytics applications from 50KB to 100KB, allowing several hundreds of SQL statements in an application. \u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-03-amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-can-now-detect-hotspots-in-real-time","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/03/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-can-now-detect-hotspots-in-real-time/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:59:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/data-analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;supports real-time hotspot detection, which allows you to automatically detect regions of high density in your data, like a high concentration of vehicles on a highway indicating traffic bottlenecks, surging rideshare requests in a certain area indicating a popular event, or higher sales of products within a category indicating feature similarity. Detecting hotspots like these can help you gain actionable insights quickly and react to changing customer and business needs promptly. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, simply call the Kinesis Data Analytics \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/sqlref/sqlrf-hotspots.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehotspot function\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;from your Kinesis application. The hotspot function\u0026nbsp;automatically builds and trains an appropriate machine learning model to identify subsections of your data streams that need attention. It identifies and reports one or more bounding boxes of these subsections in real-time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Data Analytics hotspot detection is unsupervised, meaning that the function does not require you to label the data for model training. In addition, Kinesis Data Analytics automatically updates the model behind the scenes to adapt to changes in the data stream. For more information including sample code and hotspot visualization, see \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/app-hotspots-detection.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDetecting Hotspots on a Stream\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;in the Kinesis Data Analytics developer guide.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Data Analytics is the easiest way to process data streams in real time with standard SQL without having to learn new programming languages or processing frameworks. Kinesis Data Analytics is available in the US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), and EU (Ireland) regions. To get started, visit the Kinesis Data Analytics \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003emanagement console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:56:21Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/03/amazon-kinesis-data-analytics-can-now-detect-hotspots-in-real-time/","postDateTime":"2018-03-19T11:20:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics can Now Detect Hotspots in Real-Time Data Streams","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eStarting today, \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/data-analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Data Analytics\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;supports real-time hotspot detection, which allows you to automatically detect regions of high density in your data, like a high concentration of vehicles on a highway indicating traffic bottlenecks, surging rideshare requests in a certain area indicating a popular event, or higher sales of products within a category indicating feature similarity. Detecting hotspots like these can help you gain actionable insights quickly and react to changing customer and business needs promptly. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2018-02-10x-higher-api-call-rates-for-amazon-kinesis-client-library-kcl-applications","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/02/10x-higher-api-call-rates-for-amazon-kinesis-client-library-kcl-applications/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:21:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:46:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce the new ListShards API which makes it easier for your Kinesis Data Streams KCL applications to scale. Many Kinesis Data Streams customers use the KCL to process records from their data streams. Starting in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://search.maven.org/#search%7Cga%7C1%7Camazon-kinesis-client\"\u003eversion 1.9.0 or later\u003c/a\u003e, key KCL API functions now use the ListShards API, which supports a 10x higher call rate limit compared to the DescribeStream API, which was used for these functions in earlier KCL versions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo benefit from this additional API call rate limit, you will need to upgrade your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://search.maven.org/#search%7Cga%7C1%7Camazon-kinesis-client\"\u003eKCL applications to version 1.9.0\u003c/a\u003e or higher and use AWS SDK version 1.11.272 or higher.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can find more information on the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/APIReference/API_ListShards.html\"\u003eListShards API\u003c/a\u003e in the Kinesis Data Streams documentation.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:55:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2018/02/10x-higher-api-call-rates-for-amazon-kinesis-client-library-kcl-applications/","postDateTime":"2018-02-06T14:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"10x Higher API Call Rates for Amazon Kinesis Client Library (KCL) Applications","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce the new ListShards API which makes it easier for your Kinesis Data Streams KCL applications to scale. Many Kinesis Data Streams customers use the KCL to process records from their data streams. Starting in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://search.maven.org/#search%7Cga%7C1%7Camazon-kinesis-client\"\u003eversion 1.9.0 or later\u003c/a\u003e, key KCL API functions now use the ListShards API, which supports a 10x higher call rate limit compared to the DescribeStream API, which was used for these functions in earlier KCL versions.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2018","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2018","description":"year#2018","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:20:09+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-11-announcing-amazon-kinesis-console-enhancements","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/11/announcing-amazon-kinesis-console-enhancements/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:35:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:51:36+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe new \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis\u003c/a\u003e management console (see screenshot below) makes it easy for you to learn about real-time analytics and simplifies the console user experience. You can use the new visual learning tools in the console to understand how Kinesis Streams, Kinesis Firehose, and Kinesis Analytics can help you stream real-time data from various data sources to AWS, and then process, analyze, and load the data to data stores. The new console experience also includes a dashboard showing all your Kinesis resources on one screen when you log in. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/home?region\u003dus-east-1\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis management console\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor information on where Kinesis Streams, Kinesis Firehose, and Kinesis Analytics are available, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/regional-product-services/\"\u003eAWS region table\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:54:26Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/11/announcing-amazon-kinesis-console-enhancements/","postDateTime":"2017-11-21T15:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing Amazon Kinesis console enhancements","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe new \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis\u003c/a\u003e management console (see screenshot below) makes it easy for you to learn about real-time analytics and simplifies the console user experience. You can use the new visual learning tools in the console to understand how Kinesis Streams, Kinesis Firehose, and Kinesis Analytics can help you stream real-time data from various data sources to AWS, and then process, analyze, and load the data to data stores. The new console experience also includes a dashboard showing all your Kinesis resources on one screen when you log in. To get started, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/home?region\u003dus-east-1\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis management console\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2017-09-new-quick-start-build-a-data-lake-foundation-on-the-aws-cloud-with-aws-services","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/09/new-quick-start-build-a-data-lake-foundation-on-the-aws-cloud-with-aws-services/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:27:49+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:12:47+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThis Quick Start deploys a data lake foundation that integrates Amazon Web Services (AWS) Cloud services such as Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), Amazon Redshift, Amazon Kinesis, Amazon Athena, Amazon Elasticsearch Service (Amazon ES), and Amazon QuickSight. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe data lake foundation provides these features:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eData submission\u003c/b\u003e, including batch submissions to Amazon S3 and streaming submissions via Amazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eIngest processing\u003c/b\u003e, including data validation, metadata extraction, and indexing via Amazon S3 events, Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS), AWS Lambda, Amazon Kinesis Analytics, and Amazon ES\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eDataset management\u003c/b\u003e through Amazon Redshift transformations and Kinesis Analytics\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eData transformation, aggregation, and analysis\u003c/b\u003e through Amazon Athena and Amazon Redshift Spectrum\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003eSearch\u003c/b\u003e, by indexing metadata in Amazon ES and exposing it through Kibana dashboards\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cb\u003ePublishing\u003c/b\u003e into an S3 bucket for use by visualization tools, and \u003cb\u003evisualization \u003c/b\u003ewith Amazon QuickSight\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce this foundation is in place, you may choose to augment the data lake with ISV and software as a service (SaaS) tools.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe deployment also includes an optional wizard and a sample dataset that is loaded into the Amazon Redshift cluster and Kinesis streams. The data lake wizard uses the dataset to demonstrate data lake capabilities such as search, transforms, queries, analytics, and visualization.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAWS CloudFormation templates automate the deployment and provide customization options for network resources and AWS services. You can choose to build a new virtual private cloud (VPC) infrastructure that’s configured for security, scalability, and high availability, or use your existing VPC infrastructure for the data lake foundation. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started, use the following resources:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLearn more about the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/quickstart/architecture/data-lake-foundation-with-aws-services/\"\u003edata lake foundation architecture\u003c/a\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eView the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://fwd.aws/PbXWv\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeployment guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBrowse and launch other \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/quickstart/\"\u003eAWS Quick Start reference deployments\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ci\u003eAbout Quick Starts\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nQuick Starts are automated reference deployments for key workloads on the AWS Cloud. Each Quick Start launches, configures, and runs the AWS compute, network, storage, and other services required to deploy a specific workload on AWS, using AWS best practices for security and availability. This is the latest in a set of AWS customer-ready solutions, which are ready-to-deploy reference architectures and best practices that address specific use cases or business processes.\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:54:02Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2017/09/new-quick-start-build-a-data-lake-foundation-on-the-aws-cloud-with-aws-services/","postDateTime":"2017-09-08T10:52:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"New Quick Start: Build a Data Lake Foundation on the AWS Cloud with AWS Services","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThis Quick Start deploys a data lake foundation that integrates Amazon Web Services (AWS) Cloud services such as Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), Amazon Redshift, Amazon Kinesis, Amazon Athena, Amazon Elasticsearch Service (Amazon ES), and Amazon QuickSight. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-quicksight","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-quicksight","description":"general:products/amazon-quicksight","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T23:19:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T23:19:33+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2017","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2017","description":"year#2017","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:16:58+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elasticsearch-service","description":"general:products/amazon-elasticsearch-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-athena","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-athena","description":"general:products/amazon-athena","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-12-amazon-kinesis-firehose-can-now-prepare-and-transform-streaming-data-before-loading-it-to-data-stores","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/amazon-kinesis-firehose-can-now-prepare-and-transform-streaming-data-before-loading-it-to-data-stores/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:27:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:06:14+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now configure \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e to prepare your streaming data before it is loaded to data stores. With this new feature, you can easily convert raw streaming data from your data sources into formats required by your destination data stores, without having to build your own data processing pipelines.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo use this feature, simply select an AWS Lambda function from the Amazon Kinesis Firehose delivery stream configuration tab in the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home?region\u003dus-east-1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management console\u003c/a\u003e. Amazon Kinesis Firehose will automatically apply that function to every input data record and load the transformed data to destinations.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose provides pre-built Lambda blueprints for converting common data sources such as Apache logs and system logs to JSON and CSV formats. You can use these pre-built blueprints without any change, or customize them further, or write your own custom functions. You can also configure Amazon Kinesis Firehose to automatically retry failed jobs and back up the raw streaming data.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about this feature, see \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/data-transformation.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eData Transformation\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Firehose developer guide.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into Amazon Elasticsearch Service, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Kinesis Analytics, and Amazon S3. To get started with Amazon Kinesis Firehose, sign into the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/firehose/home?region\u003dus-east-1\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eAWS Management console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about Amazon Kinesis Firehose, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:35Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/amazon-kinesis-firehose-can-now-prepare-and-transform-streaming-data-before-loading-it-to-data-stores/","postDateTime":"2016-12-21T09:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Firehose can now prepare and transform streaming data before loading it to data stores","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now configure \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e to prepare your streaming data before it is loaded to data stores. With this new feature, you can easily convert raw streaming data from your data sources into formats required by your destination data stores, without having to build your own data processing pipelines.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-elasticsearch-service","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-elasticsearch-service","description":"general:products/amazon-elasticsearch-service","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:42+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-s3","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-s3","description":"general:products/amazon-s3","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:53:07+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-12-amazon-cloudwatch-adds-support-for-evenly-distributing-log-data-from-cloudwatch-logs-to-amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/amazon-cloudwatch-adds-support-for-evenly-distributing-log-data-from-cloudwatch-logs-to-amazon-kinesis/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:31:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:12:59+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now configure your Amazon Kinesis Streams subscription in  CloudWatch Logs to evenly distribute log data from a log group to  multiple shards. Previously log data from one log stream went to the  same shard.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo enable this feature please refer to the documentation \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/Subscriptions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. To know more about CloudWatch Logs, visit the CloudWatch Logs \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/WhatIsCloudWatchLogs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:32Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/amazon-cloudwatch-adds-support-for-evenly-distributing-log-data-from-cloudwatch-logs-to-amazon-kinesis/","postDateTime":"2016-12-14T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon CloudWatch adds support for evenly distributing log data from CloudWatch Logs to Amazon Kinesis","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eYou can now configure your Amazon Kinesis Streams subscription in  CloudWatch Logs to evenly distribute log data from a log group to  multiple shards. Previously log data from one log stream went to the  same shard.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo enable this feature please refer to the documentation \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/Subscriptions.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ehere\u003c/a\u003e. To know more about CloudWatch Logs, visit the CloudWatch Logs \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/WhatIsCloudWatchLogs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cloudwatch","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cloudwatch","description":"general:products/amazon-cloudwatch","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:50:47+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cloudwatch-logs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cloudwatch-logs","description":"general:products/amazon-cloudwatch-logs","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:30+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-12-announcing-the-aws-canada-central-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/announcing-the-aws-canada-central-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:32:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:42:30+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                    AWS is excited to announce immediate availability of the new Canada (Central) Region. Canada joins Northern Virginia, Ohio, Oregon, Northern California, and AWS GovCloud as the sixth AWS Region in North America and as the fifteenth worldwide, bringing the total number of AWS Availability Zones to 40 globally.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    The new Canada Region is currently available for multiple services, including Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (Amazon EC2), Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), and Amazon Relational Database Service (Amazon RDS). For a complete list of AWS Regions and services, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/global-infrastructure/\"\u003eGlobal Infrastructure page\u003c/a\u003e. Canada Region pricing is available on the detail page of each service, which you can find through our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/products/\"\u003eproducts \u0026amp; services page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:51:31Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/12/announcing-the-aws-canada-central-region/","postDateTime":"2016-12-08T09:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Announcing the AWS Canada (Central) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                    AWS is excited to announce immediate availability of the new Canada (Central) Region. Canada joins Northern Virginia, Ohio, Oregon, Northern California, and AWS GovCloud as the sixth AWS Region in North America and as the fifteenth worldwide, bringing the total number of AWS Availability Zones to 40 globally.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#local#aws-region","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#local","name":"aws-region","description":"local:aws-region","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:11+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#global-infrastructure","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"global-infrastructure","description":"marketing:marchitecture/global-infrastructure","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:51:18+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-redshift","description":"general:products/amazon-redshift","dateCreated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-07T22:36:01+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-09-amazon-kinesis-announces-iam-role-support-in-kinesis-agent","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/09/amazon-kinesis-announces-iam-role-support-in-kinesis-agent/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:30:07+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:11:06+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon Kinesis Agent is a pre-built Java application that offers an easy way to collect and ingest data into \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis services\u003c/a\u003e. The agent monitors log files you specify and continuously sends new data to Amazon Kinesis Streams and Amazon Kinesis Firehose. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon Kinesis Agent now supports using an AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) role for authentication. You can set an IAM role in the agent configuration and the agent will assume the role to get permission to put data into your Kinesis streams and Firehose delivery streams.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/writing-with-agents.html\"\u003eWriting to Amazon Kinesis Firehose with Amazon Kinesis Agent\u003c/a\u003e in the \u003ci\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose Developer Guide\u003c/i\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/writing-with-agents.html\"\u003eWriting to Amazon Kinesis Streams with Amazon Kinesis Agent\u003c/a\u003e in the \u003ci\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams Developer Guide\u003c/i\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:53Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/09/amazon-kinesis-announces-iam-role-support-in-kinesis-agent/","postDateTime":"2016-09-16T11:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis announces IAM role support in Kinesis Agent","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon Kinesis Agent is a pre-built Java application that offers an easy way to collect and ingest data into \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis services\u003c/a\u003e. The agent monitors log files you specify and continuously sends new data to Amazon Kinesis Streams and Amazon Kinesis Firehose. \u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-08-introducing-amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/08/introducing-amazon-kinesis-analytics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:32:38+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce general availability of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/analytics/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Analytics\u003c/a\u003e, a fully managed service for continuously querying streaming data using standard SQL. With Kinesis Analytics, you can write standard SQL queries on streaming data and gain actionable insights in real-time, without having to learn any new programming skills.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can get started with Kinesis Analytics in minutes with three easy steps in the \u003ca target\u003d\"_blank\" href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e. First, you select a Kinesis stream or Kinesis Firehose delivery stream as the input stream. Kinesis Analytics ingests the data, automatically recognizes standard data formats including JSON, CSV, and TSV, and suggests a schema. You can refine this schema, or if your data is unstructured, you can define a new one using our intuitive schema editor. Next, you use the Kinesis Analytics SQL editor and pre-built templates to write your SQL queries. Lastly, you point to where you want Kinesis Analytics to load processed results. Kinesis Analytics takes care of everything required to continuously run your queries, and automatically scales to match the volume and throughput rate of incoming data while delivering sub-second processing latencies.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKinesis Analytics is closely integrated with other AWS services so you can build complete stream processing solutions using services you are already familiar with. It integrates out-of-box with Kinesis Streams and Kinesis Firehose so it’s easy to ingest streaming data and send processed results to Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, Amazon Elasticsearch Service, or your own custom destination.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Kinesis Analytics, you only pay for the resources your queries use. There is no minimum fee or setup cost. For more information on Kinesis Analytics pricing, see the pricing page.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Analytics is currently available in the following AWS Regions: N. Virginia, Oregon, and Ireland. To learn more about Amazon Kinesis Analytics, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/analytics/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e, this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-kinesis-analytics-process-streaming-data-in-real-time-with-sql\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e, and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/documentation/kinesis/\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started with Kinesis Analytics, visit the \u003ca target\u003d\"_blank\" href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/home\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:43Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/08/introducing-amazon-kinesis-analytics/","postDateTime":"2016-08-11T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Amazon Kinesis Analytics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce general availability of \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/analytics.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Analytics\u003c/a\u003e, a fully managed service for continuously querying streaming data using standard SQL. With Kinesis Analytics, you can write standard SQL queries on streaming data and gain actionable insights in real-time, without having to learn any new programming skills.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-firehose","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-firehose","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:54:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-analytics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-analytics","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-analytics","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:14+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis-streams","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis-streams","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis-streams","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:19+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-05-amazon-kinesis-firehose-supports-configurable-retry-window-for-loading-data-into-amazon-redshift","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/05/amazon-kinesis-firehose-supports-configurable-retry-window-for-loading-data-into-amazon-redshift/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:18:31+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:40:00+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose, the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS, now supports configurable retry duration for ingesting data into Amazon Redshift. You can now configure your Firehose delivery streams to retry the Redshift COPY for any time period up to a maximum of 7200 seconds. If the Redshift COPY command fails for any reason, Amazon Kinesis Firehose re-tries the command for the duration of the retry period you specify.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  For more information about ingesting data into Amazon Redshift using Amazon Kinesis Firehose, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/firehose-to-redshift/\"\u003eweb page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html#console-to-redshift\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:29Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/05/amazon-kinesis-firehose-supports-configurable-retry-window-for-loading-data-into-amazon-redshift/","postDateTime":"2016-05-18T09:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Firehose Supports Configurable Retry Window for Loading Data into Amazon Redshift","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose, the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS, now supports configurable retry duration for ingesting data into Amazon Redshift. You can now configure your Firehose delivery streams to retry the Redshift COPY for any time period up to a maximum of 7200 seconds. If the Redshift COPY command fails for any reason, Amazon Kinesis Firehose re-tries the command for the duration of the retry period you specify.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-04-amazon-kinesis-firehose-adds-amazon-elasticsearch-data-ingestion-and-enhanced-monitoring-features","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/04/amazon-kinesis-firehose-adds-amazon-elasticsearch-data-ingestion-and-enhanced-monitoring-features/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:29:55+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T14:09:53+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose, the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS, now supports Amazon Elasticsearch Service as a data delivery destination. You can now use Amazon Kinesis Firehose to stream data to your Amazon Elasticsearch domains continuously and in near real time. Amazon Kinesis Firehose automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and handles all the underlying stream management. For more information, see the Amazon Kinesis Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html#console-to-es\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose can now log data delivery errors to your Amazon CloudWatch Log group, enabling you to get more information for monitoring and troubleshooting data delivery failures. In addition, Kinesis Firehose console now displays the Amazon Redshift COPY command that Amazon Kinesis Firehose generates for loading data into Amazon Redshift. You can use the COPY command for test and data backfill purposes. For more information, see \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/monitoring-with-cloudwatch-logs.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eMonitoring with Amazon CloudWatch Logs\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Firehose developer guide. \u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:24Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/04/amazon-kinesis-firehose-adds-amazon-elasticsearch-data-ingestion-and-enhanced-monitoring-features/","postDateTime":"2016-04-19T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Firehose adds Amazon Elasticsearch Data Ingestion and Enhanced Monitoring Features","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose, the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS, now supports Amazon Elasticsearch Service as a data delivery destination. You can now use Amazon Kinesis Firehose to stream data to your Amazon Elasticsearch domains continuously and in near real time. Amazon Kinesis Firehose automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and handles all the underlying stream management. For more information, see the Amazon Kinesis Firehose \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose.html\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/basic-create.html#console-to-es\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-04-amazon-kinesis-streams-introduces-time-based-shard-iterators-and-shard-level-metrics","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/04/amazon-kinesis-streams-introduces-time-based-shard-iterators-and-shard-level-metrics/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:18:28+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:50:40+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams enables you to build custom applications that process or analyze streaming data for specialized needs. Today we are adding two new features, time-based shard iterators and shard-level metrics, to make it easy to replay and manage your Amazon Kinesis streams.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTime-based iterators make your streams easily replay-able by your processing applications. Using time-based iterators, you can read records from a position in the stream corresponding to a timestamp. This gives you the ability to go back in time and replay the stream for any time window within the default 24-hour or the extended 7-day data retention period. For more information, see \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/APIReference/API_GetShardIterator.html\"\u003eGetShardIterator\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Streams API Reference.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou now get ten new Amazon CloudWatch metrics for monitoring your Amazon Kinesis streams, including seven shard-level metrics. Shard-level metrics make stream management easier when using open-source processing frameworks like Apache Spark Streaming. With shard-level metrics, you can get better visibility into the performance and utilization of shards, which are units of streaming capacity. This allows you to monitor, scale, and troubleshoot your streams more easily. For more information, see \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/monitoring-with-cloudwatch.html#kinesis-metrics-shard\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Shard-level Metrics\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Streams developer guide.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis and get started with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/streaming-data/\"\u003estreaming data\u003c/a\u003e, see the Amazon Kinesis Streams \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/streams/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/introduction.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\nThe Amazon Kinesis Team\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:23Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/04/amazon-kinesis-streams-introduces-time-based-shard-iterators-and-shard-level-metrics/","postDateTime":"2016-04-19T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Streams Introduces Time-based Shard Iterators and Shard-level Metrics","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams enables you to build custom applications that process or analyze streaming data for specialized needs. Today we are adding two new features, time-based shard iterators and shard-level metrics, to make it easy to replay and manage your Amazon Kinesis streams.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-04-amazon-kinesis-agent-now-supports-data-preprocessing-features","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/04/amazon-kinesis-agent-now-supports-data-preprocessing-features/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:21:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:47:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Agent is a pre-built Java application that offers an easy way to collect and send data to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/streams/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e. The agent monitors a set of files for new data and continuously sends it to Amazon Kinesis Streams or Amazon Kinesis Firehose.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe agent now supports preprocessing data before sending it to Amazon Kinesis Streams or Amazon Kinesis Firehose. It can convert a multi-line JSON object to a single line JSON object, convert CSV data to JSON objects, and parse and convert common log entries to JSON objects.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/writing-with-agents.html\"\u003eWriting to Amazon Kinesis Firehose with Amazon Kinesis Agent\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Firehose Developer Guide and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/writing-with-agents.html\"\u003eWriting to Amazon Kinesis Streams with Amazon Kinesis Agent\u003c/a\u003e in the Amazon Kinesis Streams Developer Guide.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Kinesis team\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:22Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/04/amazon-kinesis-agent-now-supports-data-preprocessing-features/","postDateTime":"2016-04-11T11:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Agent Now Supports Data Preprocessing Features","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Agent is a pre-built Java application that offers an easy way to collect and send data to \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/streams.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose\u003c/a\u003e. The agent monitors a set of files for new data and continuously sends it to Amazon Kinesis Streams or Amazon Kinesis Firehose.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-03-amazon-kinesis-firehose-announces-aws-cloudtrail-support","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/03/amazon-kinesis-firehose-announces-aws-cloudtrail-support/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:21:25+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:33:35+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose, the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS, now supports auditing your API calls using \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cloudtrail/\"\u003eAWS CloudTrail\u003c/a\u003e. AWS CloudTrail records AWS API calls for your account and delivers the log files to you. For more details, see \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/monitoring-with-cloudtrail.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eLogging Amazon Kinesis Firehose API calls Using AWS CloudTrail\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started with Amazon Kinesis Firehose, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:15Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/03/amazon-kinesis-firehose-announces-aws-cloudtrail-support/","postDateTime":"2016-03-17T09:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Firehose announces AWS CloudTrail Support","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose, the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS, now supports auditing your API calls using \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cloudtrail.html\"\u003eAWS CloudTrail\u003c/a\u003e. AWS CloudTrail records AWS API calls for your account and delivers the log files to you. For more details, see \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/monitoring-with-cloudtrail.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eLogging Amazon Kinesis Firehose API calls Using AWS CloudTrail\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo get started with Amazon Kinesis Firehose, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose.html\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/what-is-this-service.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#aws-cloudtrail","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"aws-cloudtrail","description":"general:products/aws-cloudtrail","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:56:12+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:56:12+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2016-02-amazon-kinesis-streams-now-available-in-south-america-sao-paulo-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/02/amazon-kinesis-streams-now-available-in-south-america-sao-paulo-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:17+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:37:56+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams enables you to build custom applications that process or analyze streaming data for specialized needs. You can now use Amazon Kinesis Streams from the South America (Sao Paulo) Region, in addition to US East (Northern Virginia), US West (Oregon), US West (Northern California), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Sydney), and Asia Pacific (Seoul) Regions. You can get pricing information for all the regions from our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/streams/pricing/\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo learn more about Amazon Kinesis, visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/streams/\"\u003eweb page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca target\u003d\"_blank\" href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/introduction.html\"\u003edeveloper guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:50:09Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2016/02/amazon-kinesis-streams-now-available-in-south-america-sao-paulo-region/","postDateTime":"2016-02-24T09:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Streams now available in South America (Sao Paulo) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams enables you to build custom applications that process or analyze streaming data for specialized needs. You can now use Amazon Kinesis Streams from the South America (Sao Paulo) Region, in addition to US East (Northern Virginia), US West (Oregon), US West (Northern California), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), Asia Pacific (Sydney), and Asia Pacific (Seoul) Regions. You can get pricing information for all the regions from our \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/streams/pricing/\"\u003epricing page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2016","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2016","description":"year#2016","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-10-amazon-kinesis-extended-data-retention","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/10/amazon-kinesis-extended-data-retention/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:27:04+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:39:45+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis, which we are now calling Amazon Kinesis Streams, stores incoming data for a period of 24 hours by default. Amazon Kinesis Streams can now retain your streaming data for up to 7 days. You can dynamically configure the data retention period through an API call. For more information about extended data retention, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/kinesis-extended-retention.html\"\u003eChanging Data Retention Period\u003c/a\u003e. For extended data retention pricing, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/pricing/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Pricing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams is a managed service that enables you to build custom applications that process or analyze streaming data for specialized needs. Amazon Kinesis Streams can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources, and make it available for your stream processing applications.\u0026nbsp;To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams\u003c/a\u003e website.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:41Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/10/amazon-kinesis-extended-data-retention/","postDateTime":"2015-10-07T10:54:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Streams Extended Data Retention","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis, which we are now calling Amazon Kinesis Streams, stores incoming data for a period of 24 hours by default. Amazon Kinesis Streams can now retain your streaming data for up to 7 days. You can dynamically configure the data retention period through an API call. For more information about extended data retention, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/kinesis-extended-retention.html\"\u003eChanging Data Retention Period\u003c/a\u003e. For extended data retention pricing, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/pricing.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Pricing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams is a managed service that enables you to build custom applications that process or analyze streaming data for specialized needs. Amazon Kinesis Streams can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources, and make it available for your stream processing applications.\u0026nbsp;To learn more, see the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Streams\u003c/a\u003e website.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-10-introducing-amazon-kinesis-firehose","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/10/introducing-amazon-kinesis-firehose/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:24:29+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:44:24+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eTwo years ago we introduced Amazon Kinesis, which we now call Amazon Kinesis Streams, to allow customers to build applications that collect, process, and analyze streaming data with very high throughput. Many customers use Amazon Kinesis Streams to capture streaming data and load it into Amazon S3 or Amazon Redshift. Until now, this required customers to manage the Amazon Kinesis data streams and write custom code to load the data. We are now introducing Amazon Kinesis Firehose, a fully managed service that makes this as easy as an API call.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS. It can capture and automatically load streaming data into Amazon S3 and Amazon Redshift, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools and dashboards you’re already using today. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. It can also batch, compress, and encrypt the data before loading it, minimizing the amount of storage used at the destination and increasing security. You can easily create a Firehose delivery stream from the AWS Management Console, configure it with a few clicks, and start sending data to the stream from hundreds of thousands of data sources to be loaded continuously to AWS – all in just a few minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Firehose, you only pay for the amount of data you transmit through the service. There is no minimum fee or setup cost.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose is currently available in the following AWS Regions: N. Virginia, Oregon, and Ireland. To learn more about Amazon Kinesis Firehose, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/firehose/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e, this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-kinesis-firehose-simple-highly-scalable-data-ingestion/\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e, and the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/documentation/firehose/\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started with Amazon Kinesis Firehose, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/home\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:40Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/10/introducing-amazon-kinesis-firehose/","postDateTime":"2015-10-07T09:26:47Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Amazon Kinesis Firehose","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eTwo years ago we introduced Amazon Kinesis, which we now call Amazon Kinesis Streams, to allow customers to build applications that collect, process, and analyze streaming data with very high throughput. Many customers use Amazon Kinesis Streams to capture streaming data and load it into Amazon S3 or Amazon Redshift. Until now, this required customers to manage the Amazon Kinesis data streams and write custom code to load the data. We are now introducing Amazon Kinesis Firehose, a fully managed service that makes this as easy as an API call.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose is the easiest way to load streaming data into AWS. It can capture and automatically load streaming data into Amazon S3 and Amazon Redshift, enabling near real-time analytics with existing business intelligence tools and dashboards you’re already using today. It is a fully managed service that automatically scales to match the throughput of your data and requires no ongoing administration. It can also batch, compress, and encrypt the data before loading it, minimizing the amount of storage used at the destination and increasing security. You can easily create a Firehose delivery stream from the AWS Management Console, configure it with a few clicks, and start sending data to the stream from hundreds of thousands of data sources to be loaded continuously to AWS – all in just a few minutes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith Amazon Kinesis Firehose, you only pay for the amount of data you transmit through the service. There is no minimum fee or setup cost.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Firehose is currently available in the following AWS Regions: N. Virginia, Oregon, and Ireland. To learn more about Amazon Kinesis Firehose, see our \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/firehose.html\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e, this \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/aws/amazon-kinesis-firehose-simple-highly-scalable-data-ingestion/\"\u003eblog post\u003c/a\u003e, and the \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/documentation/firehose.html\"\u003edocumentation\u003c/a\u003e. To get started with Amazon Kinesis Firehose, visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/home\"\u003eAWS Management Console\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-09-amazon-kinesis-server-side-timestamp","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/09/amazon-kinesis-server-side-timestamp/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:33:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis team has announced the addition of a server-side record timestamp. Each record now has a new attribute, “ApproximateArrivalTimestamp\u0026quot;, which captures the approximate time of record insertion in an Amazon Kinesis stream. Customers can use this parameter to measure the age of a record read from a Kinesis stream, or to group records over time windows. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  For more information about Amazon Kinesis, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eweb page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/introduction.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:36Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/09/amazon-kinesis-server-side-timestamp/","postDateTime":"2015-09-23T09:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Server-side Timestamp","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-06-amazon-kinesis-announces-put-pricing-change-1mb-record-support-and-the-kinesis-producer-library","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/06/amazon-kinesis-announces-put-pricing-change-1mb-record-support-and-the-kinesis-producer-library/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:42:10+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at a massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Kinesis team has announced PUT pricing change and two new capabilities.   \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEffective June 1, 2015, Amazon Kinesis replaces the “PUT Record” pricing dimension with “PUT Payload Unit”. After the change, records smaller than 25KB receive a 50% reduction on the PUT price. For more information, please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/pricing/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Pricing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis raises the record size limit from 50KB to 1MB. For more information, please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/service-sizes-and-limits.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Limits\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis also releases the Kinesis Producer Library (KPL), an easy-to-use and highly configurable library that helps send data to Amazon Kinesis streams. For more information, please visit please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/developing-producers-with-kpl.html\"\u003eKinesis Producer Library\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Amazon Kinesis, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eWeb Page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/monitoring.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:20Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/06/amazon-kinesis-announces-put-pricing-change-1mb-record-support-and-the-kinesis-producer-library/","postDateTime":"2015-06-02T16:30:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis announces PUT pricing change, 1MB record support, and the Kinesis Producer Library","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at a massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Kinesis team has announced PUT pricing change and two new capabilities.   \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEffective June 1, 2015, Amazon Kinesis replaces the “PUT Record” pricing dimension with “PUT Payload Unit”. After the change, records smaller than 25KB receive a 50% reduction on the PUT price. For more information, please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis/pricing.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Pricing\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis raises the record size limit from 50KB to 1MB. For more information, please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/service-sizes-and-limits.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis Limits\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis also releases the Kinesis Producer Library (KPL), an easy-to-use and highly configurable library that helps send data to Amazon Kinesis streams. For more information, please visit please visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/developing-producers-with-kpl.html\"\u003eKinesis Producer Library\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Amazon Kinesis, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis.html\"\u003eWeb Page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/monitoring.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-05-amazon-kinesis-consumer-position-metric","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/05/amazon-kinesis-consumer-position-metric/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:17:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:34:49+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style\u003d\"font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style\u003d\"font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis team has announced the ability for customers to track how close to real time the data their consumer applications are processing. Consumer applications now receive a new attribute called “MillisBehindLatest” with every GetRecords response that indicates how far they are from real time. Customers leveraging the Kinesis Client Library (KCL) can track the progress of their applications by monitoring this new metric at Amazon CloudWatch.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Amazon Kinesis, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eWeb Page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/monitoring.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:18Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/05/amazon-kinesis-consumer-position-metric/","postDateTime":"2015-05-19T09:08:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Consumer Position Metric","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style\u003d\"font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp style\u003d\"font-family: tahoma, arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12px;\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-03-amazon-kinesis-client-library-for-nodejs-developers","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/03/amazon-kinesis-client-library-for-nodejs-developers/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:14:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:42:33+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis team has released Kinesis Client Library (KCL) for Node.js developers. KCL enables developers to build Amazon Kinesis Applications for reading and processing data from an Amazon Kinesis stream. KCL handles complex issues such as adapting to changes in stream volume, load-balancing streaming data, coordinating distributed services, and processing data with fault-tolerance. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis Client Library (KCL) makes it easier for developers to build applications that take action on real-time data, power dashboards, generate alerts, implement dynamic pricing strategies, or emit data to other big data services such as Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), Amazon Elastic Map Reduce (Amazon EMR), and Amazon Redshift.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Amazon Kinesis and KCL, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eweb page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca target\u003d\"_blank\" href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/kinesis-record-processor-app.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e. You can download Amazon Kinesis Client Library for Node.js from \u003ca target\u003d\"_blank\" href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-client-nodejs\"\u003eGithub\u003c/a\u003e or \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/aws-kcl\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003enpm\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Kinesis Team\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:06Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/03/amazon-kinesis-client-library-for-nodejs-developers/","postDateTime":"2015-03-26T10:00:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Client Library for Node.js Developers","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-03-introducing-amazon-cognito-streams-automatically-stream-user-id-data-to-amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/03/introducing-amazon-cognito-streams-automatically-stream-user-id-data-to-amazon-kinesis/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:36:32+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Cognito Streams feature allows you to automatically stream user identity data from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/cognito/\"\u003eAmazon Cognito\u003c/a\u003e to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis\u003c/a\u003e. By streaming user identity data to Amazon Kinesis, you can do real-time processing, create powerful dashboards and gain insights about your user data stored in Amazon Cognito. You can also move this data from Amazon Kinesis to other services such as Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, and Amazon DynamoDB for storage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can enable this feature from your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/cognito\"\u003eAmazon Cognito console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"http://mobile.awsblog.com/post/Tx35782XTJZROY4\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:03Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/03/introducing-amazon-cognito-streams-automatically-stream-user-id-data-to-amazon-kinesis/","postDateTime":"2015-03-04T10:16:31Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Introducing Amazon Cognito Streams: Automatically stream user identity data to Amazon Kinesis","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Cognito Streams feature allows you to automatically stream user identity data from \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/cognito.html\"\u003eAmazon Cognito\u003c/a\u003e to \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis.html\"\u003eAmazon Kinesis\u003c/a\u003e. By streaming user identity data to Amazon Kinesis, you can do real-time processing, create powerful dashboards and gain insights about your user data stored in Amazon Cognito. You can also move this data from Amazon Kinesis to other services such as Amazon S3, Amazon Redshift, and Amazon DynamoDB for storage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can enable this feature from your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://console.aws.amazon.com/cognito\"\u003eAmazon Cognito console\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"http://mobile.awsblog.com/post/Tx35782XTJZROY4\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eblog\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-cognito","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-cognito","description":"general:products/amazon-cognito","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:55:30+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:55:30+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-03-amazon-kinesis-propagation-delay-reduction","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/03/amazon-kinesis-propagation-delay-reduction/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:16:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:35:25+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis team has announced sub-second record propagation delay for all customers at no additional cost. All new and existing Kinesis streams will observe significantly reduced end-to-end record propagation delay without requiring any additional configuration.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  For more information about Amazon Kinesis, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eWeb Page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/kinesis-record-processor-app.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  The Amazon Kinesis Team\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:49:03Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/03/amazon-kinesis-propagation-delay-reduction/","postDateTime":"2015-03-03T10:24:14Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Propagation Delay Reduction","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis team has announced sub-second record propagation delay for all customers at no additional cost. All new and existing Kinesis streams will observe significantly reduced end-to-end record propagation delay without requiring any additional configuration.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  For more information about Amazon Kinesis, please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"/content/aws.amazon.com/live/en_US/kinesis.html\"\u003eWeb Page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/kinesis-record-processor-app.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  The Amazon Kinesis Team\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-01-26-amazon-kinesis-now-available-in-us-west-northern-california-region","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/01/26/amazon-kinesis-now-available-in-us-west-northern-california-region/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:25:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:37:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources. Developers can write stream processing applications with the Kinesis Client Library that take action on real-time data such as web site click-streams, financial transaction data, social media feeds, IT logs, location-tracking events, and more. Amazon Kinesis-enabled applications can power real-time dashboards, generate alerts, drive real-time business decisions such as changing pricing and advertising strategies, or emit data to other big data services such as Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), Amazon Elastic Map Reduce (Amazon EMR), and Amazon Redshift.\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is now available to all customers in US West (Northern California) Region. All customers can now use Amazon Kinesis from US West (Northern California) in addition to US East (Northern Virginia), US West (Oregon), EU (Ireland), EU (Frankfurt), Asia Pacific (Singapore), Asia Pacific (Tokyo), and Asia Pacific (Sydney) Regions, further reducing the latencies associated with high throughput streaming data ingestion and processing. The pricing for US West (Northern California) Region can be found on the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/pricing/\" adhocenable\u003d\"false\"\u003ePricing Page\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Amazon Kinesis, please visit please visit our \u003ca href\u003d\"http://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/pricing/\" adhocenable\u003d\"false\"\u003eWeb Page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/introduction.html\" adhocenable\u003d\"false\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:48:58Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/01/26/amazon-kinesis-now-available-in-us-west-northern-california-region/","postDateTime":"2015-01-26T08:28:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis now available in US West (Northern California) Region","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003eAmazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources. Developers can write stream processing applications with the Kinesis Client Library that take action on real-time data such as web site click-streams, financial transaction data, social media feeds, IT logs, location-tracking events, and more. Amazon Kinesis-enabled applications can power real-time dashboards, generate alerts, drive real-time business decisions such as changing pricing and advertising strategies, or emit data to other big data services such as Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), Amazon Elastic Map Reduce (Amazon EMR), and Amazon Redshift.\n\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2015-01-12-amazon-kinesis-client-library-for-ruby-developers","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/01/12/amazon-kinesis-client-library-for-ruby-developers/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:19:21+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:30:07+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon Kinesis team has released Kinesis Client Library (KCL) for Ruby developers. KCL enables developers to build Amazon Kinesis Applications for reading and processing data from an Amazon Kinesis stream. KCL handles complex issues such as adapting to changes in stream volume, load-balancing streaming data, coordinating distributed services, and processing data with fault-tolerance. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  Amazon Kinesis Client Library (KCL) makes it easier for developers to build applications that take action on real-time data, power dashboards, generate alerts, implement dynamic pricing strategies, or emit data to other big data services such as Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3), Amazon Elastic Map Reduce (Amazon EMR), and Amazon Redshift. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e  For more information about Amazon Kinesis and KCL, please visit our \u003ca adhocenable\u003d\"false\" href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\"\u003eWeb Page\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca adhocenable\u003d\"false\" href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/kinesis-record-processor-app.html\"\u003eDeveloper Guide\u003c/a\u003e. You can download Amazon Kinesis Client Library for Ruby from \u003ca adhocenable\u003d\"false\" href\u003d\"https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-kinesis-client-ruby\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eGithub\u003c/a\u003e, or \u003ca adhocenable\u003d\"false\" href\u003d\"https://rubygems.org/gems/aws-kclrb/versions/1.0.0\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eRuby Gem\u003c/a\u003e (\u003ca adhocenable\u003d\"false\" href\u003d\"http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/aws-kclrb/1.0.0\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eRuby Gem Documentation\u003c/a\u003e) \u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:48:56Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2015/01/12/amazon-kinesis-client-library-for-ruby-developers/","postDateTime":"2015-01-12T09:18:27Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"Amazon Kinesis Client Library for Ruby Developers ","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2015","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2015","description":"year#2015","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:13:24+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#developers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"developers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/developers","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:34+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"whats-new-v2#about-aws-whats-new-2014-12-04-new-putrecords-api-in-amazon-kinesis-to-enable-batch-data-records-input","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"whats-new-v2","name":"/about-aws/whats-new/2014/12/04/new-putrecords-api-in-amazon-kinesis-to-enable-batch-data-records-input/","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:13:18+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-07-25T13:41:12+0000","additionalFields":{"postBody":"\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Amazon Kinesis team has released a new API operation, PutRecords. You can use the new PutRecords operation to send up to 500 records to your Kinesis stream in a single HTTP call. This new feature allows you to put data into your Kinesis stream with greater efficiency and reduced complexity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor more information about Amazon Kinesis, please visit the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://aws.amazon.com/kinesis/\" adhocenable\u003d\"false\"\u003eproduct page\u003c/a\u003e. You can learn more about the new PutRecords operation by visiting the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/dev/kinesis-using-api-java.html#kinesis-using-api-java-add-data-to-stream\" adhocenable\u003d\"false\"\u003eKinesis Developer Guide\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"http://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesis/latest/APIReference/API_PutRecords.html\" adhocenable\u003d\"false\"\u003eAPI Reference\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n","modifiedDate":"2019-10-06T04:48:46Z","headlineUrl":"/about-aws/whats-new/2014/12/04/new-putrecords-api-in-amazon-kinesis-to-enable-batch-data-records-input/","postDateTime":"2014-12-04T15:15:00Z","contentType":"Launch Announcement","headline":"New PutRecords API in Amazon Kinesis to Enable Batch Data Records Input","postSummary":"\u003cp\u003e                    Amazon Kinesis is a fully managed service for real-time processing of streaming data at massive scale. Amazon Kinesis can continuously capture and store terabytes of data per hour from hundreds of thousands of sources.\u003c/p\u003e\n"}},"tags":[{"id":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture#developers","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#marketing-marchitecture","name":"developers","description":"marketing:marchitecture/developers","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T13:59:34+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T13:59:34+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#general-products#amazon-kinesis","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#general-products","name":"amazon-kinesis","description":"general:products/amazon-kinesis","dateCreated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-08T19:07:35+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#launch-announcement","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Launch Announcement","description":"Launch Announcement","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:27+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:08+0000"},{"id":"whats-new-v2#year#2014","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"whats-new-v2#year","name":"2014","description":"year#2014","dateCreated":"2023-11-09T14:11:54+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-11-09T14:11:54+0000"}]}],"metadata":{"count":143,"totalHits":143},"fieldTypes":{"regionalAvailability":"LongText","nofollow":"Boolean","date":"Date","language":"Text","title":"Text","postDateTime":"DateTime","body":"Text","postSummary":"LongText","ctaLabel":"Text","mediaThumbnail":"Text","nosnippet":"Boolean","price":"Text","ctaLink":"URL","headline":"Text","contentType":"Text","bodyBack":"LongText","secondaryCTALabel":"Text","primaryCTALink":"URL","noindex":"Boolean","level":"Text","heading":"Text","mediaType":"Text","mediaAlt":"Text","headlineUrl":"Text","mediaSrc":"URL","durationMinutes":"Number","badge":"JSON","videoImageUrl":"URL","postBody":"LongText","secondaryCTALink":"URL","Video":"URL","modifiedDate":"DateTime","namePerson":"Text","location":"Text","time":"Text","publishedDate":"DateTime","durationReadtime":"Number","primaryCTALabel":"Text"}}